4:moves57:change of WHERE the item is: a place, or a holder's handss4:rules54:information that is a requirement: should / should-nots4:sames37:two items identical in one comparisons4:times7:passings5:actors27:item that is change drivings5:drafts73:information an actor created that awaits a decision; status derived laters5:events20:activity of happeneds6:changes33:different of one item across times8:activitys65:information about change: actor, action, object, target (the row)s8:decisions67:activity that permanentises an information: changeable -> unchangeds9:differents41:two items not identical in one comparisons9:non-actors52:item that drives no change; can still undergo changes9:unchangeds28:same of one item across times12:relationships438:A RELATIONSHIP is about two things: nothing in the universe is identical, any two things hold same parts and different parts, and a relationship reads those differences AT THE EXISTENCE LEVEL — where the two sit: apart, touching, overlapping, one containing the other (parent–child at the core) — which IS the Venn2 reading. Attribute-level differences (colour, weight) are NOT relationships; they are content comparisons of fields.s4:kinds13:category_packs4:names14:ontology-termss6:levelsl23:s4:items4:times10:comparisons4:sames9:differents6:changes9:unchangeds14:transformations4:moves5:actors9:non-actors12:physicalnesss13:consumabilitys11:informations13:structuralitys8:activitys11:observations4:rules5:events5:drafts8:decisions10:governances10:compliances6:sources37:design/59 Part 1; design/56 v0.56 B11s9:record_ids5:rec_4d16:s10:provenanced3:s10:could_readl0:s11:asserted_bys10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:sources6:systems10:rule_citeds8:BOOT-INTs11:record_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:04.948007+00:00s12:content_forms6:inlines15:occurrence_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:04.948022+00:00s15:submission_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:04.948019+00:00s16:evidence_summaryns3:seqi5;s4:refsl0:s5:actors10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:actions11:CREATE-RULEs6:objects16:REL-LAW-TWO-ENDSs6:origind2:s12:subsystem_ids6:kernels8:built_idi0;s6:targetns7:payloadd4:s11:enforced_bys28:the gate's relation-row steps11:enforcements4:lives4:texts531:a relationship cannot hold two identical ends — its two ends must be DIFFERENT THINGS in normal terms, or THE SAME THING AT DIFFERENT TIMES; nothing else exists, and that is exhaustive BY THE BASE ITSELF: the base holds exactly two axes of distinguishability — identity (same-or-different) and time (two places in the record) — so a relationship's ends must be separated on at least one of them; a row relating a thing to itself at one time has nothing distinguishable to read and is refused by name at the relationship door.s7:rule_ids16:REL-LAW-TWO-ENDSs9:record_ids5:rec_5d16:s10:provenanced3:s10:could_readl0:s11:asserted_bys10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:sources6:systems10:rule_citeds8:BOOT-INTs11:record_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:04.953629+00:00s12:content_forms6:inlines15:occurrence_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:04.953654+00:00s15:submission_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:04.953649+00:00s16:evidence_summaryns3:seqi7;s4:refsl0:s5:actors10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:actions11:CREATE-INFOs6:objects10:space:roots6:origind2:s12:subsystem_ids6:kernels8:built_idi0;s6:targetns7:payloadd3:s11:space_classs9:permanents4:kinds10:info_spaces4:names4:roots9:record_ids5:rec_7d16:s10:provenanced3:s10:could_readl0:s11:asserted_bys10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:sources6:systems10:rule_citeds8:BOOT-INTs11:record_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:04.955869+00:00s12:content_forms6:inlines15:occurrence_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:04.955887+00:00s15:submission_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:04.955884+00:00s16:evidence_summaryns3:seqi8;s4:refsl0:s5:actors10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:actions11:CREATE-RULEs6:objects10:ROOT-NEG-1s6:origind2:s12:subsystem_ids6:kernels8:built_idi0;s6:targetns7:payloadd9:s11:enforced_bys141:require_prior + ceiling checks (per-op) AND the gate authority step (no authorising chain -> ROOT-NEG-1; EP-17 W1); reach grows with accountss11:enforcements4:lives4:rootb1s4:texts61:no valid authorising rule chain -> 