variant counts live openings at a moment, never openings across a lifetime (design/39 §3)s6:paramsd3:s4:roles8:requireds6:entitys8:requireds7:channels8:requireds9:law_citeds17:COMM-LAW-CONTRACTs4:kinds13:op_definitions4:names10:COMMS-OPENs4:texts111:operation COMMS-OPEN: when invoked and its checks pass -> append a COMMS-OPEN decision citing COMM-LAW-CONTRACTs4:tiers5:owners7:rule_ids13:op:COMMS-OPENs8:polaritys1:+s9:record_ids6:rec_96d16:s10:provenanced3:s10:could_readl0:s11:asserted_bys10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:sources6:systems10:rule_citeds10:CAP-IS-LAWs11:record_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.283910+00:00s12:content_forms6:inlines15:occurrence_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.283937+00:00s15:submission_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.283930+00:00s16:evidence_summaryns3:seqi97;s4:refsl0:s5:actors10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:actions9:CREATE-OPs6:objects13:op:COMMS-SENDs6:origind2:s12:subsystem_ids6:kernels8:built_idi0;s6:targetns7:payloadd7:s10:definitiond10:s11:descriptions45:enqueue a message (payload content-addressed)s12:object_params7:channels12:payload_froml2:s7:channels2:tos12:target_params2:tos14:content_paramsd1:s7:messages12:message_hashs17:structural_paramsl1:s7:channels4:cells1:Ss6:checksl2:d8:s10:key_paramsl2:s6:entitys7:channels11:open_actions10:COMMS-OPENs12:close_actions11:COMMS-CLOSEs15:close_actor_keys6:entitys4:cites14:COMM-LAW-QUEUEs5:checks12:live_presents7:messages204:COMMS-SEND: no live channel by this name — a message crosses a channel that is OPEN, and a send on a closed or never-opened channel is refused, not recorded (COMM-LAW-QUEUE's scheduled liveness, EP-49C)s7:presentd1:s7:channels7:channeld8:s10:key_paramsl2:s6:entitys7:channels11:open_actions10:COMMS-OPENs12:close_actions11:COMMS-CLOSEs15:close_actor_keys6:entitys4:cites17:COMM-LAW-CONTRACTs5:checks12:live_presents7:messages194:COMMS-SEND: the sender holds no live opening of this channel — a channel is an opening of somebody's and only its holder may send on it (COMM-LAW-CONTRACT's scheduled sender authority, EP-49C)s7:presentd2:s6:entitys6:$actors7:channels7:channels6:paramsd2:s7:channels8:requireds7:messages8:requireds9:law_citeds14:COMM-LAW-QUEUEs4:kinds13:op_definitions4:names10:COMMS-SENDs4:texts108:operation COMMS-SEND: when invoked and its checks pass -> append a COMMS-SEND decision citing COMM-LAW-QUEUEs4:tiers5:owners7:rule_ids13:op:COMMS-SENDs8:polaritys1:+s9:record_ids6:rec_97d16:s10:provenanced3:s10:could_readl0:s11:asserted_bys10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:sources6:systems10:rule_citeds10:CAP-IS-LAWs11:record_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.290108+00:00s12:content_forms6:inlines15:occurrence_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.290176+00:00s15:submission_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.290169+00:00s16:evidence_summaryns3:seqi98;s4:refsl0:s5:actors10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:actions9:CREATE-OPs6:objects13:op:COMMS-RECVs6:origind2:s12:subsystem_ids6:kernels8:built_idi0;s6:targetns7:payloadd7:s10:definitiond8:s11:descriptions17:dequeue a messages12:object_params7:channels12:payload_froml2:s7:channels12:message_hashs17:structural_paramsl1:s7:channels4:cells1:Ss6:checksl2:d8:s10:key_paramsl2:s6:entitys7:channels11:open_actions10:COMMS-OPENs12:close_actions11:COMMS-CLOSEs15:close_actor_keys6:entitys4:cites14:COMM-LAW-QUEUEs5:checks12:live_presents7:messages161:COMMS-RECV: no live channel by this name — a receive on a closed or never-opened channel is refused, not recorded (COMM-LAW-QUEUE's scheduled liveness, EP-49C)s7:presentd1:s7:channels7:channeld10:s10:add_actions10:COMMS-SENDs10:sub_actions10:COMMS-RECVs4:cites14:COMM-LAW-QUEUEs5:checks14:fold_thresholds7:messages206:COMMS-RECV: the queue is empty — a receive takes a pending message, and a receive where sends minus receives is not above zero is refused, not recorded (COMM-LAW-QUEUE's scheduled non-empty guard, EP-49C)s8:operators1:>s9:fold_names11:queue_depths9:key_fields7:channels9:key_params7:channels9:thresholdi0;s6:paramsd1:s7:channels8:requireds9:law_citeds14:COMM-LAW-QUEUEs4:kinds13:op_definitions4:names10:COMMS-RECVs4:texts108:operation COMMS-RECV: when invoked and its checks pass -> append a COMMS-RECV decision citing COMM-LAW-QUEUEs4:tiers5:owners7:rule_ids13:op:COMMS-RECVs8:polaritys1:+s9:record_ids6:rec_98d16:s10:provenanced3:s10:could_readl0:s11:asserted_bys10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:sources6:systems10:rule_citeds10:CAP-IS-LAWs11:record_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.294431+00:00s12:content_forms6:inlines15:occurrence_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.294449+00:00s15:submission_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.294446+00:00s16:evidence_summaryns3:seqi99;s4:refsl0:s5:actors10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:actions9:CREATE-OPs6:objects14:op:COMMS-CLOSEs6:origind2:s12:subsystem_ids6:kernels8:built_idi0;s6:targetns7:payloadd7:s10:definitiond8:s11:descriptions19:tear down a channels12:object_params7:channels12:payload_froml1:s7:channels17:structural_paramsl1:s7:channels4:cells1:Ss6:checksl1:d8:s10:key_paramsl2:s6:entitys7:channels11:open_actions10:COMMS-OPENs12:close_actions11:COMMS-CLOSEs15:close_actor_keys6:entitys4:cites17:COMM-LAW-CONTRACTs5:checks12:live_presents7:messages310:COMMS-CLOSE: the closer holds no live opening of this channel — a close tears down the closer's own opening; a close of a channel this entity does not hold is refused, not recorded, and under two entities holding one name a close drops exactly the closer's (COMM-LAW-CONTRACT's scheduled whose-close, EP-49C)s7:presentd2:s6:entitys6:$actors7:channels7:channels6:paramsd1:s7:channels8:requireds9:law_citeds17:COMM-LAW-CONTRACTs4:kinds13:op_definitions4:names11:COMMS-CLOSEs4:texts113:operation COMMS-CLOSE: when invoked and its checks pass -> append a COMMS-CLOSE decision citing COMM-LAW-CONTRACTs4:tiers5:owners7:rule_ids14:op:COMMS-CLOSEs8:polaritys1:+s9:record_ids6:rec_99d16:s10:provenanced3:s10:could_readl0:s11:asserted_bys10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:sources6:systems10:rule_citeds10:CAP-IS-LAWs11:record_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.297744+00:00s12:content_forms6:inlines15:occurrence_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.297830+00:00s15:submission_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.297824+00:00s16:evidence_summaryns3:seqi100;s4:refsl0:s5:actors10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:actions9:CREATE-OPs6:objects12:op:SHM-GRANTs6:origind2:s12:subsystem_ids6:kernels8:built_idi0;s6:targetns7:payloadd7:s10:definitiond11:s11:descriptions61:grant shared access to a region (interior writes NOT audited)s11:stamp_actorl1:s7:granters12:object_params6:regions12:payload_froml3:s6:regions8:granteess4:modes12:target_params8:granteess14:param_defaultsd2:s4:modes2:rws8:granteesl0:s17:structural_paramsl1:s6:regions4:cells1:Ss6:checksl2:d6:s4:cites20:COMM-LAW-SHARE-GRANTs5:checks13:require_priors5:fields6:regions5:params6:regions6:actions9:MEM-GRANTs7:messages365:SHM-GRANT: no MEM-GRANT founds this region — a share is granted OVER something a prior record established, and a region that is merely a string the caller supplied names nothing to share. The grant inherits the region's establishment and never mints it, so a share over an unfounded region would append an act nobody could have performed, and this rule refuses itd7:s10:key_paramsl1:s6:regions11:open_actions9:MEM-GRANTs12:close_actions9:MEM-EVICTs4:cites20:COMM-LAW-SHARE-GRANTs5:checks12:live_presents7:messages493:SHM-GRANT: no LIVE MEM-GRANT holds this region — a share is granted over a region that is CURRENTLY mapped, not merely one a prior MEM-GRANT once founded; a region granted and then evicted (MEM-EVICT) is no longer live, and a share over it would append an act over a region nobody holds. The historical prerequisite the require_prior row checks is not the live one (COMM-LAW-SHARE-GRANT's scheduled liveness — the EP-49C live_present kind reused, no new check kind; EP-MAINT-OUTSIDE-4 R10)s7:presentd1:s6:regions6:regions6:paramsd1:s6:regions8:requireds9:law_citeds20:COMM-LAW-SHARE-GRANTs4:kinds13:op_definitions4:names9:SHM-GRANTs4:texts112:operation SHM-GRANT: when invoked and its checks pass -> append a SHM-GRANT decision citing COMM-LAW-SHARE-GRANTs4:tiers5:owners7:rule_ids12:op:SHM-GRANTs8:polaritys1:+s9:record_ids7:rec_100d16:s10:provenanced3:s10:cou