6:s10:provenanced3:s10:could_readl0:s11:asserted_bys10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:sources6:systems10:rule_citeds10:CAP-IS-LAWs11:record_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.387379+00:00s12:content_forms6:inlines15:occurrence_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.387395+00:00s15:submission_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.387391+00:00s16:evidence_summaryns3:seqi121;s4:refsl0:s5:actors10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:actions9:CREATE-OPs6:objects17:op:CREATE-ACCOUNTs6:origind2:s12:subsystem_ids6:kernels8:built_idi0;s6:targetns7:payloadd7:s10:definitiond11:s11:descriptions104:found an identity: an account (identity founding; verified is DERIVED per check, never a stored boolean)s11:stamp_actorl1:s10:founded_bys12:object_params10:account_ids12:payload_froml2:s10:account_ids11:actor_classs14:payload_derived1:s4:kindd1:s3:tpls7:accounts17:structural_paramsl2:s10:account_ids11:actor_classs4:cells1:Ss5:mintsl1:s10:account_ids6:checksl0:s6:paramsd2:s10:account_ids8:requireds11:actor_classs8:requireds9:law_citeds10:CAP-IS-LAWs4:kinds13:op_definitions4:names14:CREATE-ACCOUNTs4:texts106:operation CREATE-ACCOUNT: when invoked and its checks pass -> append an account founding citing CAP-IS-LAWs4:tiers5:owners7:rule_ids17:op:CREATE-ACCOUNTs8:polaritys1:+s9:record_ids7:rec_121d16:s10:provenanced3:s10:could_readl0:s11:asserted_bys10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:sources6:systems10:rule_citeds10:CAP-IS-LAWs11:record_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.390396+00:00s12:content_forms6:inlines15:occurrence_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.390413+00:00s15:submission_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.390409+00:00s16:evidence_summaryns3:seqi122;s4:refsl0:s5:actors10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:actions9:CREATE-OPs6:objects17:op:VERIFY-ACCOUNTs6:origind2:s12:subsystem_ids6:kernels8:built_idi0;s6:targetns7:payloadd7:s10:definitiond11:s11:descriptions737:record that an account passed an identity check — evidence stored AS A HASH (verify-never-reveal; no plaintext secret ever enters the record, CONST-SECRETS), the verifier named (itself verified or a founding anchor; recursion grounds at the founding). C6 P8 (B17): CLASSIFY IS ATTEST GENERALISED — this attest-shaped op gains a TARGET (what it classifies: an actor, an object, or the band being assigned) and an EVIDENCE KIND, both OPTIONAL and declared STRUCTURAL in the META, so a classify act names what it classifies and the kind of evidence. A class is the LATEST LIVE such act on an entity, computed AT READ (never a stored band). A bare identity-verify act omits both and is byte-unchanged from before P8; no new op is minted.s11:param_kindsd2:s13:evidence_kinds4:texts6:targets4:texts11:stamp_actorl1:s8:verifiers12:object_params7:accounts12:payload_froml4:s7:accounts13:evidence_hashs6:targets13:evidence_kinds14:payload_derived1:s4:kindd1:s3:tpls12:verifications17:structural_paramsl4:s7:accounts13:evidence_hashs6:targets13:evidence_kinds4:cells1:Ss6:checksl1:d6:s4:cites10:CAP-IS-LAWs5:checks13:require_priors5:fields10:account_ids5:params7:accounts6:actions14:CREATE-ACCOUNTs7:messages69:cannot verify an account that was never founded — capability is laws6:paramsd4:s13:evidence_hashs8:requireds13:evidence_kinds8:optionals6:targets8:optionals7:accounts8:requireds9:law_citeds10:CAP-IS-LAWs4:kinds13:op_definitions4:names14:VERIFY-ACCOUNTs4:texts101:operation VERIFY-ACCOUNT: when invoked and its checks pass -> append a verification citing CAP-IS-LAWs4:tiers5:owners7:rule_ids17:op:VERIFY-ACCOUNTs8:polaritys1:+s9:record_ids7:rec_122d16:s10:provenanced3:s10:could_readl0:s11:asserted_bys10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:sources6:systems10:rule_citeds10:CAP-IS-LAWs11:record_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.393753+00:00s12:content_forms6:inlines15:occurrence_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.393767+00:00s15:submission_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.393764+00:00s16:evidence_summaryns3:seqi123;s4:refsl0:s5:actors10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:actions9:CREATE-OPs6:objects15:op:CREATE-SPACEs6:origind2:s12:subsystem_ids6:kernels8:built_idi0;s6:targetns7:payloadd7:s10:definitiond11:s11:descriptions71:found a space — a node in the containment tree, nested under a parents12:payload_froml2:s4:names6:parents13:object_derived1:s3:tpls12:space:{name}s14:payload_derived2:s4:kindd1:s3:tpls5:spaces5:spaced1:s4:copys6:parents16:authority_regimes18:attenuation-familys17:structural_paramsl2:s4:names6:parents4:cells1:Ss5:mintsl1:s4:names6:checksl1:d4:s10:cite_cycles8:BOOT-INTs12:cite_missings10:CAP-IS-LAWs12:parent_params6:parents5:checks10:space_trees6:paramsd2:s4:names8:requireds6:parents8:requireds9:law_citeds10:CAP-IS-LAWs4:kinds13:op_definitions4:names12:CREATE-SPACEs4:texts101:operation CREATE-SPACE: when invoked and its checks pass -> append a space founding citing CAP-IS-LAWs4:tiers5:owners7:rule_ids15:op:CREATE-SPACEs8:polaritys1:+s9:record_ids7:rec_123d16:s10:provenanced3:s10:could_readl0:s11:asserted_bys10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:sources6:systems10:rule_citeds10:CAP-IS-LAWs11:record_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.396319+00:00s12:content_forms6:inlines15:occurrence_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.396332+00:00s15:submission_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.396328+00:00s16:evidence_summaryns3:seqi124;s4:refsl0:s5:actors10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:actions9:CREATE-OPs6:objects22:op:CREATE-RELATIONSHIPs6:origind2:s12:subsystem_ids6:kernels8:built_idi0;s6:targetns7:payloadd7:s10:definitiond8:s11:descriptions240:record a relation row — one venn2 fact (subject, object, geometry, zone); the frame derives from the cited rule, the reading from that rule's text, the roles from actor/object/target (design/25 v2.1 rulings 6/7); unrelated is never storeds12:payload_froml4:s7:subjects6:objects8:geometrys4:zones13:object_derived1:s3:tpls22:rel:{subject}:{object}s17:structural_paramsl4:s7:subjects6:objects8:geometrys4:zones4:cells1:Ss6:checksl1:d5:s4:cites10:CAP-IS-LAWs5:checks12:value_domains5:params8:geometrys6:domainl4:s2:ADs2:INs2:NSs2:EMs7:messages190:CREATE-RELATIONSHIP: geometry is one of the four closed venn2 values AD, IN, NS, EM (design/25 v2.1 B5) — unrelated is never stored, so an absent or unknown geometry is refused at the doors6:paramsd3:s6:objects8:requireds7:subjects8:requireds8:geometrys8:requireds9:law_citeds10:CAP-IS-LAWs4:kinds13:op_definitions4:names19:CREATE-RELATIONSHIPs4:texts106:operation CREATE-RELATIONSHIP: when invoked and its checks pass -> append a relation row citing CAP-IS-LAWs4:tiers5:owners7:rule_ids22:op:CREATE-RELATIONSHIPs8:polaritys1:+s9:record_ids7:rec_124d16:s10:provenanced3:s10:could_readl0:s11:asserted_bys10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:sources6:systems10:rule_citeds10:CAP-IS-LAWs11:record_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.399724+00:00s12:content_forms6:inlines15:occurrence_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.399787+00:00s15:submission_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.399759+00:00s16:evidence_summaryns3:seqi125;s4:refsl0:s5:actors10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:actions9:CREATE-OPs6:objects14:op:CREATE-ROLEs6:origind2:s12:subsystem_ids6:kernels8:built_idi0;s6:targetns7:payloadd7:s10:definitiond12:s11:descriptions60:found a role — a name grants may cite (it stores no power)s12:payload_froml2:s4:names5:spaces13:object_derived1:s3:tpls11:role:{name}s14:param_defaultsd1:s5:spaces10:space:roots14:payload_derived1:s4:kindd1:s3:tpls4:roles16:authority_regimes18:attenuation-familys17:structural_paramsl1:s4:names4:cells1:Ss5:mintsl1:s4:names6:checksl0:s6:paramsd1:s4:names8:requireds9:law_citeds10:CAP-IS-LAWs4:kinds13:op_definitions4:names11:CREATE-ROLEs4:texts99:operation CREATE-ROLE: when invoked and its checks pass -> append a role founding citing CAP-IS-LAWs4:tiers5:owners7:rule_ids14:op:CREATE-ROLEs8:polaritys1:+s9:record_ids7:rec_125d16:s10:provenanced3:s10:could_readl0:s11:asserted_bys10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:sources6:systems10:rule_citeds10:CAP-IS-LAWs11:record_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.403047+00:00s12:content_forms6:inlines15:occurrence_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.403068+00:00s15:submission_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.403064+00:00s16:evidence_summaryns3:seqi126;s4:refsl0:s5:actors10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:actions9:CREATE-OPs6:objects8:op:GRANTs6:origind2:s12:subsystem_ids6:kernels8:built_idi0;s6:targetns7:payloadd7:s10:definitiond12:s11:descriptions78:record a positive grant: grantee x actions x info x space (power is the grant)s12:payload_froml6:s7:grantees7:actionss4:infos5:spaces8:grant_ids4:roles13:object_derived1:s3:tpls16:grant:{grant_id}s14:param_defaultsd1:s4:rolens14:payload_derived2:s4:kindd1:s3:tpls5:grants8:polarityd1:s3:tpls1:+s16:authority_regimes18:attenuation-familys17:structural_paramsl5:s8:grant_ids7:grantees7:actionss4:infos5:spaces4:cells1:Ss5:mintsl1:s8:grant_ids6:checksl0:s6:paramsd5:s4:infos8:requireds5:spaces8:requireds7:actionss8:requireds7:grantees8:requireds8:grant_ids8:requireds9:law_citeds10:CAP-IS-LAWs4:kinds13:op_definitions4:names5:GRANTs4:texts151:operation GRANT: when invoked and its checks pass -> append a grant citing CAP-IS-LAW (attenuation containment moved to the gate chokepoint, EP-18 R-A)s4:tiers5:owners7:rule_ids8:op:GRANTs8:polaritys1:+s9:record_ids7:rec_126d16:s10:provenanced3:s10:could_readl0:s11:asserted_bys10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:sources6:systems10:rule_citeds10:CAP-IS-LAWs11:record_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.408934+00:00s12:content_forms6:inlines15:occurrence_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.408955+00:00s15:submission_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.408950+00:00s16:evidence_summaryns3:seqi127;s4:refsl0:s5:actors10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:actions9:CREATE-OPs6:objects9:op:REVOKEs6:origind2:s12:subsystem_ids6:kernels8:built_idi0;s6:targetns7:payloadd7:s10:definitiond10:s11:descriptions63:revoke a grant — supersedes it latest-wins (nothing cascades)s12:payload_froml1:s8:grant_ids13:object_derived1:s3:tpls16:grant:{grant_id}s14:payload_derived1:s4:kindd1:s3:tpls6:revokes16:authority_regimes18:attenuation-familys17:structural_paramsl1:s8:grant_ids4:cells1:Ss6:checksl0:s6:paramsd1:s8:grant_ids8:requireds9:law_citeds10:CAP-IS-LAWs4:kinds13:op_definitions4:names6:REVOKEs4:texts87:operation REVOKE: when invoked and its checks pass -> append a revoke citing CAP-IS-LAWs4:tiers5:owners7:rule_ids9:op:REVOKEs8:polaritys1:+s9:record_ids7:rec_127d16:s10:provenanced3:s10:could_readl0:s11:asserted_bys10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:sources6:systems10:rule_citeds10:CAP-IS-LAWs11:record_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.412985+00:00s12:content_forms6:inlines15:occurrence_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.413005+00:00s15:submission_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.413001+00:00s16:evidence_summaryns3:seqi128;s4:refsl0:s5:actors10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:actions9:CREATE-OPs6:objects22:op:DESIGNATE-SUCCESSORs6:origind2:s12:subsystem_ids6:kernels8:built_idi0;s6:targetns7:payloadd7:s10:definitiond9:s11:descriptions231:the root designates a verified human successor (a recorded ceremony, never a stored owner field). The gate anchor guard refuses a non-root designator, an unverified successor, or a pure-agentic successor (CONST-AUTHORITY-ANCHORED).s12:object_params9:successors12:payload_froml1:s9:successors14:payload_derived1:s4:kindd1:s3:tpls10:successions17:structural_paramsl1:s9:successors4:cells1:Ss6:checksl0:s6:paramsd1:s9:successors8:requireds9:law_citeds10:CAP-IS-LAWs4:kinds13:op_definitions4:names19:DESIGNATE-SUCCESSORs4:texts124:operation DESIGNATE-SUCCESSOR: when invoked and the anchor guard passes -> append a succession designation citing CAP-IS-LAWs4:tiers5:owners7:rule_ids22:op:DESIGNATE-SUCCESSORs8:polaritys1:+s9:record_ids7:rec_128d16:s10:provenanced3:s10:could_readl0:s11:asserted_bys10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:sources6:systems10:rule_citeds10:CAP-IS-LAWs11:record_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.416966+00:00s12:content_forms6:inlines15:occurrence_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.416994+00:00s15:submission_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.416989+00:00s16:evidence_summaryns3:seqi129;s4:refsl0:s5:actors10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:actions9:CREATE-OPs6:objects20:op:ACCEPT-SUCCESSIONs6:origind2:s12:subsystem_ids6:kernels8:built_idi0;s6:targetns7:payloadd7:s10:definitiond8:s11:descriptions161:the designated successor accepts — the acceptance half of the designation-acceptance pair the current-successor fold reads (the accepter is the record's actor)s12:payload_froml0:s13:object_derived1:s3:tpls17:system:successions14:payload_derived1:s4:kindd1:s3:tpls10:successions4:cells1:Ss6:checksl0:s6:paramsd0:s9:law_citeds10:CAP-IS-LAWs4:kinds13:op_definitions4:names17:ACCEPT-SUCCESSIONs4:texts93:operation ACCEPT-SUCCESSION: when invoked -> append a succession acceptance citing CAP-IS-LAWs4:tiers5:owners7:rule_ids20:op:ACCEPT-SUCCESSIONs8:polaritys1:+s9:record_ids7:rec_129d16:s10:provenanced3:s10:could_readl0:s11:asserted_bys10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:sources6:systems10:rule_citeds10:CAP-IS-LAWs11:record_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.434262+00:00s12:content_forms6:inlines15:occurrence_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.434362+00:00s15:submission_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.434354+00:00s16:evidence_summaryns3:seqi130;s4:refsl0:s5:actors10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:actions9:CREATE-OPs6:objects20:op:REVOKE-SUCCESSIONs6:origind2:s12:subsystem_ids6:kernels8:built_idi0;s6:targetns7:payloadd7:s10:definitiond8:s11:descriptions124:the root revokes the current succession designation (supersedes the pair). The gate anchor guard refuses a non-root revoker.s12:payload_froml0:s13:object_derived1:s3:tpls17:system:successions14:payload_derived1:s4:kindd1:s3:tpls10:successions4:cells1:Ss6:checksl0:s6:paramsd0:s9:law_citeds10:CAP-IS-LAWs4:kinds13:op_definitions4:names17:REVOKE-SUCCESSIONs4:texts121:operation REVOKE-SUCCESSION: when invoked and the anchor guard passes -> append a succession revocation citing CAP-IS-LAWs4:tiers5:owners7:rule_ids20:op:REVOKE-SUCCESSIONs8:polaritys1:+s9:record_ids7:rec_130d16:s10:provenanced3:s10:could_readl0:s11:asserted_bys10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:sources6:systems10:rule_citeds10:CAP-IS-LAWs11:record_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.439027+00:00s12:content_forms6:inlines15:occurrence_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.439054+00:00s15:submission_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.439048+00:00s16:evidence_summaryns3:seqi131;s4:refsl0:s5:actors10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:actions9:CREATE-OPs6:objects11:op:HANDOVERs6:origind2:s12:subsystem_ids6:kernels8:built_idi0;s6:targetns7:payloadd7:s10:definitiond8:s11:descriptions386:the root hands over root authority to the accepted successor (owner account retirement / self-removal): the old chain-end's authority ends by supersession, the successor becomes the new chain-end BY DERIVATION (no owner field is written). The gate anchor guard refuses it unless a valid, accepted, verified human successor exists — root authority never orphans (exit-with-continuity).s12:payload_froml0:s13:object_derived1:s3:tpls21:system:root-authoritys14:payload_derived1:s4:kindd1:s3:tpls8:handovers4:cells1:Ss6:checksl0:s6:paramsd0:s9:law_citeds10:CAP-IS-LAWs4:kinds13:op_definitions4:names8:HANDOVERs4:texts126:operation HANDOVER: when invoked and the anchor guard passes (a valid successor exists) -> append a handover citing CAP-IS-LAWs4:tiers5:owners7:rule_ids11:op:HANDOVERs8:polaritys1:+s9:record_ids7:rec_131d16:s10:provenanced3:s10:could_readl0:s11:asserted_bys10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:sources6:systems10:rule_citeds10:CAP-IS-LAWs11:record_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.450040+00:00s12:content_forms6:inlines15:occurrence_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.450067+00:00s15:submission_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.450062+00:00s16:evidence_summaryns3:seqi135;s4:refsl0:s5:actors10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:actions9:CREATE-OPs6:objects14:op:SEAL-SECRETs6:origind2:s12:subsystem_ids6:kernels8:built_idi0;s6:targetns7:payloadd7:s10:definitiond10:s11:descriptions280:seal a secret under a name — the value crosses ONCE, is sealed into the vault (write-once, keyed by hash, NO read path), and the record holds the HASH only, never the value (verify-never-reveal, CONST-SECRETS). Re-sealing a name ROTATES it: supersession by hash, latest-per-names12:payload_froml1:s4:names13:object_derived1:s3:tpls13:secret:{name}s13:secret_paramsd1:s5:values11:secret_hashs17:structural_paramsl1:s4:names4:cells1:Ss5:mintsl1:s4:names6:checksl0:s6:paramsd2:s4:names8:requireds5:values8:requireds9:law_citeds10:CAP-IS-LAWs4:kinds13:op_definitions4:names11:SEAL-SECRETs4:texts167:operation SEAL-SECRET: when invoked -> seal the value in the vault and append a seal record carrying the HASH only (the value never enters a payload) citing CAP-IS-LAWs4:tiers5:owners7:rule_ids14:op:SEAL-SECRETs8:polaritys1:+s9:record_ids7:rec_135d16:s10:provenanced3:s10:could_readl0:s11:asserted_bys10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:sources6:systems10:rule_citeds10:CAP-IS-LAWs11:record_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.452634+00:00s12:content_forms6:inlines15:occurrence_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.452657+00:00s15:submission_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.452651+00:00s16:evidence_summaryns3:seqi136;s4:refsl0:s5:actors10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:actions9:CREATE-OPs6:objects16:op:VERIFY-SECRETs6:origind2:s12:subsystem_ids6:kernels8:built_idi0;s6:targetns7:payloadd7:s10:definitiond9:s11:descriptions318:verify a candidate against the secret sealed under a name — the vault compares BY HASH inside the S-plane; the decision records MATCH / NO-MATCH + the sealed hash, NEVER the candidate (verify-never-reveal, CONST-SECRETS). Account verification is a consumer of this family (the vault seed re-homes here, design/31 J8)s12:payload_froml1:s4:names13:object_derived1:s3:tpls13:secret:{name}s13:secret_verifyd4:s10:hash_fields11:secret_hashs10:name_params4:names12:result_fields6:results15:candidate_params9:candidates17:structural_paramsl1:s4:names4:cells1:Ss6:checksl0:s6:paramsd2:s4:names8:requireds9:candidates8:requireds9:law_citeds10:CAP-IS-LAWs4:kinds13:op_definitions4:names13:VERIFY-SECRETs4:texts190:operation VERIFY-SECRET: when invoked -> compare the candidate against the sealed secret and append a MATCH/NO-MATCH decision carrying the sealed hash, never the candidate, citing CAP-IS-LAWs4:tiers5:owners7:rule_ids16:op:VERIFY-SECRETs8:polaritys1:+s9:record_ids7:rec_136d16:s10:provenanced3:s10:could_readl0:s11:asserted_bys10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:sources6:systems10:rule_citeds10:CAP-IS-LAWs11:record_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.455555+00:00s12:content_forms6:inlines15:occurrence_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.455577+00:00s15:submission_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.455572+00:00s16:evidence_summaryns3:seqi137;s4:refsl0:s5:actors10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:actions9:CREATE-OPs6:objects11:op:key-binds6:origind2:s12:subsystem_ids6:kernels8:built_idi0;s6:targetns7:payloadd7:s10:definitiond10:s11:descriptions492:bind a public key to an account — the LAW-class member of the key family (design/37 §4). A recorded ceremony act citing KEY-LAW-BIND; validity is a live supersession fold (kernel.keys), never a stored value. Adds NO check kind: the account/public_key are recorded, not namespace keys. The root key's leash and the succession key half live at the gate anchor guard, engaging only when the key-bind law is live and, for the succession half, only per-account (a keyless account is untouched).s12:object_params7:accounts12:payload_froml2:s7:accounts10:public_keys14:payload_derived2:s4:kindd1:s3:tpls8:key-binds5:classd1:s3:tpls3:LAWs17:structural_paramsl3:s7:accounts10:public_keys2:ats21:occurrence_time_paramd2:s11:when_absents7:defaults5:params2:ats4:cells1:Ss6:checksl0:s6:paramsd3:s10:public_keys8:requireds2:ats8:optionals7:accounts8:requireds9:law_citeds12:KEY-LAW-BINDs4:kinds13:op_definitions4:names8:key-binds4:texts131:operation key-bind: when invoked -> append a key-bind record (class LAW) binding the account to the public key, citing KEY-LAW-BINDs4:tiers5:owners7:rule_ids11:op:key-binds8:polaritys1:+s9:record_ids7:rec_137d16:s10:provenanced3:s10:could_readl0:s11:asserted_bys10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:sources6:systems10:rule_citeds10:CAP-IS-LAWs11:record_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.459943+00:00s12:content_forms6:inlines15:occurrence_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.459980+00:00s15:submission_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.459974+00:00s16:evidence_summaryns3:seqi138;s4:refsl0:s5:actors10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:actions9:CREATE-OPs6:objects13:op:key-rotates6:origind2:s12:subsystem_ids6:kernels8:built_idi0;s6:targetns7:payloadd7:s10:definitiond10:s11:descriptions443:rotate an account's bound key — the DECISION-class supersession that replaces the binding with a new public key (latest-supersession-wins; the prior bind stays on the record as DATA, an old signature over it remains verifiable as evidence of who decided then). A rotate of the ROOT key refuses without a successor key bound through the human-only succession ceremony (the gate anchor guard, is_root_key_op); a non-root key rotates unleashed.s12:object_params7:accounts12:payload_froml2:s7:accounts10:public_keys14:payload_derived2:s4:kindd1:s3:tpls10:key-rotates5:classd1:s3:tpls8:DECISIONs17:structural_paramsl3:s7:accounts10:public_keys2:ats21:occurrence_time_paramd2:s11:when_absents7:defaults5:params2:ats4:cells1:Ss6:checksl0:s6:paramsd3:s10:public_keys8:requireds2:ats8:optionals7:accounts8:requireds9:law_citeds12:KEY-LAW-BINDs4:kinds13:op_definitions4:names10:key-rotates4:texts193:operation key-rotate: when invoked and the gate anchor guard passes -> append a key-rotate record (class DECISION) superseding the account's binding with the new public key, citing KEY-LAW-BINDs4:tiers5:owners7:rule_ids13:op:key-rotates8:polaritys1:+s9:record_ids7:rec_138d16:s10:provenanced3:s10:could_readl0:s11:asserted_bys10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:sources6:systems10:rule_citeds10:CAP-IS-LAWs11:record_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.464399+00:00s12:content_forms6:inlines15:occurrence_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.464422+00:00s15:submission_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.464417+00:00s16:evidence_summaryns3:seqi139;s4:refsl0:s5:actors10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:actions9:CREATE-OPs6:objects13:op:key-revokes6:origind2:s12:subsystem_ids6:kernels8:built_idi0;s6:targetns7:payloadd7:s10:definitiond10:s11:descriptions405:revoke an account's bound key — the DECISION-class supersession to none (the fold reads the account as no longer holding a valid key). Nothing cascades: validity is re-derived live from the record, never read from a cache. A revoke of the ROOT key refuses without a successor key bound through the human-only succession ceremony (the gate anchor guard, is_root_key_op); a non-root key revokes unleashed.s12:object_params7:accounts12:payload_froml1:s7:accounts14:payload_derived2:s4:kindd1:s3:tpls10:key-revokes5:classd1:s3:tpls8:DECISIONs17:structural_paramsl2:s7:accounts2:ats21:occurrence_time_paramd2:s11:when_absents7:defaults5:params2:ats4:cells1:Ss6:checksl0:s6:paramsd2:s2:ats8:optionals7:accounts8:requireds9:law_citeds12:KEY-LAW-BINDs4:kinds13:op_definitions4:names10:key-revokes4:texts177:operation key-revoke: when invoked and the gate anchor guard passes -> append a key-revoke record (class DECISION) superseding the account's binding to none, citing KEY-LAW-BINDs4:tiers5:owners7:rule_ids13:op:key-revokes8:polaritys1:+s9:record_ids7:rec_139d16:s10:provenanced3:s10:could_readl0:s11:asserted_bys10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:sources6:systems10:rule_citeds10:CAP-IS-LAWs11:record_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.470468+00:00s12:content_forms6:inlines15:occurrence_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.470556+00:00s15:submission_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.470549+00:00s16:evidence_summaryns3:seqi140;s4:refsl0:s5:actors10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:actions9:CREATE-OPs6:objects18:op:ANSWER-RETURNEDs6:origind2:s12:subsystem_ids6:kernels8:built_idi0;s6:targetns7:payloadd7:s10:definitiond10:s11:descriptions321:record the answer of an executor outside the S-plane — an INPUT-class arrival that binds to its hand-out by the store's own citation and is accepted only against the world it was judged in. The content is FROZEN: replay consumes it and never re-invokes the answerer (the clock-as-sensor law generalized to every oracle)s12:payload_froml3:s11:handout_seqs6:answers16:claimed_crossings13:object_derived1:s3:tpls22:crossing:{handout_seq}s14:param_defaultsd1:s16:claimed_crossingns14:payload_derived2:s12:record_classd1:s3:tpls5:INPUTs4:kindd1:s3:tpls15:crossing-answers17:structural_paramsl2:s11:handout_seqs6:answers4:cells1:Ss6:checksl1:d4:s14:crossing_params11:handout_seqs16:cite_correlations20:CROSSING-CORRELATIONs4:cites14:CROSSING-STALEs5:checks11:fingerprints6:paramsd2:s11:handout_seqs8:requireds6:answers8:requireds9:law_citeds20:CROSSING-CORRELATIONs4:kinds13:op_definitions4:names15:ANSWER-RETURNEDs4:texts176:operation ANSWER-RETURNED: when invoked and the cited hand-out is open and its seal still holds -> append the frozen answer as an INPUT-class record citing CROSSING-CORRELATIONs4:tiers5:owners7:rule_ids18:op:ANSWER-RETURNEDs8:polaritys1:+s9:record_ids7:rec_140d16:s10:provenanced3:s10:could_readl0:s11:asserted_bys10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:sources6:systems10:rule_citeds10:CAP-IS-LAWs11:record_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.475520+00:00s12:content_forms6:inlines15:occurrence_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.475542+00:00s15:submission_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.475537+00:00s16:evidence_summaryns3:seqi141;s4:refsl0:s5:actors10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:actions9:CREATE-OPs6:objects21:op:PRESENT-CREDENTIALs6:origind2:s12:subsystem_ids6:kernels8:built_idi0;s6:targetns7:payloadd7:s10:definitiond10:s11:descriptions422:record that a channel presented, on an open crossing, the vault-held credential that crossing was handed out under. The vault COMPARES by hash inside the S-plane; the record carries MATCH/NO-MATCH and the sealed hash, never the candidate and never the value. No read path is used and none exists — the vault's whole surface is seal and compare, so the record can prove a secret was used without any actor ever reading its12:payload_froml2:s11:handout_seqs4:names13:object_derived1:s3:tpls22:crossing:{handout_seq}s13:secret_verifyd4:s10:hash_fields11:secret_hashs10:name_params4:names12:result_fields6:results15:candidate_params9:candidates14:payload_derived2:s12:record_classd1:s3:tpls8:DECISIONs4:kindd1:s3:tpls19:crossing-credentials17:structural_paramsl2:s11:handout_seqs4:names4:cells1:Ss6:checksl0:s6:paramsd3:s11:handout_seqs8:requireds4:names8:requireds9:candidates8:requireds9:law_citeds13:CONST-SECRETSs4:kinds13:op_definitions4:names18:PRESENT-CREDENTIALs4:texts229:operation PRESENT-CREDENTIAL: when invoked on an open crossing -> compare the presented credential against the sealed secret and append a MATCH/NO-MATCH decision carrying the sealed hash, never the candidate, citing CONST-SECRETSs4:tiers5:owners7:rule_ids21:op:PRESENT-CREDENTIALs8:polaritys1:+s9:record_ids7:rec_141d16:s10:provenanced3:s10:could_readl0:s11:asserted_bys10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:sources6:systems10:rule_citeds10:CAP-IS-LAWs11:record_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.478419+00:00s12:content_forms6:inlines15:occurrence_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.478440+00:00s15:submission_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.478434+00:00s16:evidence_summaryns3:seqi142;s4:refsl0:s5:actors10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:actions9:CREATE-OPs6:objects12:op:FILE-OPENs6:origind2:s12:subsystem_ids6:kernels8:built_idi0;s6:targetns7:payloadd7:s10:definitiond9:s11:descriptions65:open a file: the explicit custody grant (design/10 §6, open row)s12:object_params4:paths12:payload_froml3:s4:paths5:inodes5:flagss16:provenance_params10:provenances17:structural_paramsl4:s4:paths5:inodes5:flagss10:provenances4:cells1:Ss6:checksl0:s6:paramsd4:s10:provenances8:optionals4:paths8:requireds5:flagss8:optionals5:inodes8:optionals9:law_citeds11:FS-LAW-PERMs4:kinds13:op_definitions4:names9:FILE-OPENs4:texts103:operation FILE-OPEN: when invoked and its checks pass -> append a FILE-OPEN decision citing FS-LAW-PERMs4:tiers5:owners7:rule_ids12:op:FILE-OPENs8:polaritys1:+s9:record_ids7:rec_142d16:s10:provenanced3:s10:could_readl0:s11:asserted_bys10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:sources6:systems10:rule_citeds10:CAP-IS-LAWs11:record_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.482324+00:00s12:content_forms6:inlines15:occurrence_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.482347+00:00s15:submission_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.482342+00:00s16:evidence_summaryns3:seqi143;s4:refsl0:s5:actors10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:actions9:CREATE-OPs6:objects13:op:FILE-CLOSEs6:origind2:s12:subsystem_ids6:kernels8:built_idi0;s6:targetns7:payloadd7:s10:definitiond10:s11:descriptions76:release an open custody (design/10 §6, close row — the symmetric release)s12:object_params4:paths12:payload_froml2:s4:paths5:inodes16:provenance_params10:provenances17:structural_paramsl3:s4:paths5:inodes10:provenances4:cells1:Ss6:checksl0:s6:paramsd3:s10:provenances8:optionals4:paths8:requireds5:inodes8:optionals8:act_kinds7:releases9:law_citeds11:FS-LAW-PERMs4:kinds13:op_definitions4:names10:FILE-CLOSEs4:texts105:operation FILE-CLOSE: when invoked and its checks pass -> append a FILE-CLOSE decision citing FS-LAW-PERMs4:tiers5:owners7:rule_ids13:op:FILE-CLOSEs8:polaritys1:+s9:record_ids7:rec_143d16:s10:provenanced3:s10:could_readl0:s11:asserted_bys10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:sources6:systems10:rule_citeds10:CAP-IS-LAWs11:record_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.487329+00:00s12:content_forms6:inlines15:occurrence_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.487354+00:00s15:submission_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.487349+00:00s16:evidence_summaryns3:seqi144;s4:refsl0:s5:actors10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:actions9:CREATE-OPs6:objects16:op:FILE-TRUNCATEs6:origind2:s12:subsystem_ids6:kernels8:built_idi0;s6:targetns7:payloadd7:s10:definitiond12:s11:descriptions63:set a file's length; the resulting content is content-addresseds11:param_kindsd1:s6:lengths8:quantitys12:content_forms4:blobs12:object_params4:paths12:payload_froml2:s4:paths5:inodes14:content_paramsd1:s7:contentd2:s4:hashs12:content_hashs6:lengths6:lengths16:provenance_params10:provenances17:structural_paramsl4:s4:paths5:inodes6:lengths10:provenances4:cells1:Ss6:checksl0:s6:paramsd5:s10:provenances8:optionals4:paths8:requireds5:inodes8:optionals6:lengths8:optionals7:contents8:requireds9:law_citeds11:FS-LAW-PERMs4:kinds13:op_definitions4:names13:FILE-TRUNCATEs4:texts111:operation FILE-TRUNCATE: when invoked and its checks pass -> append a FILE-TRUNCATE decision citing FS-LAW-PERMs4:tiers5:owners7:rule_ids16:op:FILE-TRUNCATEs8:polaritys1:+s9:record_ids7:rec_144d16:s10:provenanced3:s10:could_readl0:s11:asserted_bys10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:sources6:systems10:rule_citeds10:CAP-IS-LAWs11:record_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.491910+00:00s12:content_forms6:inlines15:occurrence_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.491945+00:00s15:submission_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.491926+00:00s16:evidence_summaryns3:seqi145;s4:refsl0:s5:actors10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:actions9:CREATE-OPs6:objects13:op:FILE-MKDIRs6:origind2:s12:subsystem_ids6:kernels8:built_idi0;s6:targetns7:payloadd7:s10:definitiond11:s10:mints_froms17:record_coordinates11:descriptions68:create a directory (design/10 §6, mkdir row — a namespace create)s12:object_params4:paths12:payload_froml2:s4:paths4:perms14:param_defaultsd1:s4:perms3:755s16:provenance_params10:provenances17:structural_paramsl3:s4:paths4:perms10:provenances4:cells1:Ss6:checksl3:d7:s10:binds_kindd1:s7:literals3:dirs4:cites16:FS-LAW-NAMESPACEs5:checks7:bindings6:effects4:binds7:messages212:the name is already held in the living namespace, and a create that recorded an act over it would be a second act on one name — the state would still be right and the record would hold a create nobody performeds7:requires7:unbounds9:key_params4:pathd6:s4:cites16:FS-LAW-NAMESPACEs5:checks7:bindings6:key_ofs9:containers7:messages219:the name this act would take sits inside a container the living namespace does not hold — a name is only takeable inside something that is there, and a create recorded here would put a name in a place no record foundss7:requires5:bounds9:key_params4:pathd6:s4:cites16:FS-LAW-NAMESPACEs5:checks4:kinds6:key_ofs9:containers7:messages159:the container this act would take a name inside is held, and the record does not describe it as a directory — a thing that holds no names cannot be given ones7:requires3:dirs9:key_params4:paths6:paramsd3:s10:provenances8:optionals4:paths8:requireds4:perms8:optionals9:law_citeds16:FS-LAW-NAMESPACEs4:kinds13:op_definitions4:names10:FILE-MKDIRs4:texts110:operation FILE-MKDIR: when invoked and its checks pass -> append a FILE-MKDIR decision citing FS-LAW-NAMESPACEs4:tiers5:owners7:rule_ids13:op:FILE-MKDIRs8:polaritys1:+s9:record_ids7:rec_145d16:s10:provenanced3:s10:could_readl0:s11:asserted_bys10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:sources6:systems10:rule_citeds10:CAP-IS-LAWs11:record_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.496921+00:00s12:content_forms6:inlines15:occurrence_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.496937+00:00s15:submission_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.496934+00:00s16:evidence_summaryns3:seqi146;s4:refsl0:s5:actors10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:actions9:CREATE-OPs6:objects13:op:FILE-RMDIRs6:origind2:s12:subsystem_ids6:kernels8:built_idi0;s6:targetns7:payloadd7:s10:definitiond9:s11:descriptions52:remove an empty directory (design/10 §6, rmdir row)s12:object_params4:paths12:payload_froml1:s4:paths16:provenance_params10:provenances17:structural_paramsl2:s4:paths10:provenances4:cells1:Ss6:checksl3:d6:s4:cites16:FS-LAW-NAMESPACEs5:checks7:bindings6:effects6:unbinds7:messages95:the name is not held in the living namespace, so there is nothing here for this act to be abouts7:requires5:bounds9:key_params4:pathd5:s4:cites16:FS-LAW-NAMESPACEs5:checks4:kinds7:messages183:the name is held but the record does not describe it as a directory, and this operation removes directories — an act recorded here would claim a directory was removed where none wass7:requires3:dirs9:key_params4:pathd5:s4:cites16:FS-LAW-NAMESPACEs5:checks8:containss7:messages270:the name is held, it names a directory, and the living namespace still holds names inside it — removing it would leave every one of those names inside something that is no longer there, and the record would say the directory was removed while its contents went nowheres7:requires5:emptys9:key_params4:paths6:paramsd2:s10:provenances8:optionals4:paths8:requireds9:law_citeds16:FS-LAW-NAMESPACEs4:kinds13:op_definitions4:names10:FILE-RMDIRs4:texts110:operation FILE-RMDIR: when invoked and its checks pass -> append a FILE-RMDIR decision citing FS-LAW-NAMESPACEs4:tiers5:owners7:rule_ids13:op:FILE-RMDIRs8:polaritys1:+s9:record_ids7:rec_146d16:s10:provenanced3:s10:could_readl0:s11:asserted_bys10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:sources6:systems10:rule_citeds10:CAP-IS-LAWs11:record_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.500578+00:00s12:content_forms6:inlines15:occurrence_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.500600+00:00s15:submission_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.500596+00:00s16:evidence_summaryns3:seqi147;s4:refsl0:s5:actors10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:actions9:CREATE-OPs6:objects15:op:FILE-SYMLINKs6:origind2:s12:subsystem_ids6:kernels8:built_idi0;s6:targetns7:payloadd7:s10:definitiond11:s10:mints_froms17:record_coordinates11:descriptions71:create a symbolic link — the link's target is the new inode's contents12:object_params4:paths12:payload_froml2:s4:paths6:targets12:target_params6:targets16:provenance_params10:provenances17:structural_paramsl3:s4:paths6:targets10:provenances4:cells1:Ss6:checksl3:d7:s10:binds_kindd1:s7:literals4:links4:cites16:FS-LAW-NAMESPACEs5:checks7:bindings6:effects4:binds7:messages212:the name is already held in the living namespace, and a create that recorded an act over it would be a second act on one name — the state would still be right and the record would hold a create nobody performeds7:requires7:unbounds9:key_params4:pathd6:s4:cites16:FS-LAW-NAMESPACEs5:checks7:bindings6:key_ofs9:containers7:messages219:the name this act would take sits inside a container the living namespace does not hold — a name is only takeable inside something that is there, and a create recorded here would put a name in a place no record foundss7:requires5:bounds9:key_params4:pathd6:s4:cites16:FS-LAW-NAMESPACEs5:checks4:kinds6:key_ofs9:containers7:messages159:the container this act would take a name inside is held, and the record does not describe it as a directory — a thing that holds no names cannot be given ones7:requires3:dirs9:key_params4:paths6:paramsd3:s10:provenances8:optionals4:paths8:requireds6:targets8:requireds9:law_citeds16:FS-LAW-NAMESPACEs4:kinds13:op_definitions4:names12:FILE-SYMLINKs4:texts114:operation FILE-SYMLINK: when invoked and its checks pass -> append a FILE-SYMLINK decision citing FS-LAW-NAMESPACEs4:tiers5:owners7:rule_ids15:op:FILE-SYMLINKs8:polaritys1:+s9:record_ids7:rec_147d16:s10:provenanced3:s10:could_readl0:s11:asserted_bys10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:sources6:systems10:rule_citeds10:CAP-IS-LAWs11:record_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.503918+00:00s12:content_forms6:inlines15:occurrence_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.503933+00:00s15:submission_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.503930+00:00s16:evidence_summaryns3:seqi148;s4:refsl0:s5:actors10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:actions9:CREATE-OPs6:objects14:op:FILE-RENAMEs6:origind2:s12:subsystem_ids6:kernels8:built_idi0;s6:targetns7:payloadd7:s10:definitiond10:s11:descriptions59:atomically rename / move a name (design/10 §6, rename row)s12:object_params4:paths12:payload_froml2:s4:paths8:new_paths12:target_params8:new_paths16:provenance_params10:provenances17:structural_paramsl3:s4:paths8:new_paths10:provenances4:cells1:Ss6:checksl3:d6:s4:cites16:FS-LAW-NAMESPACEs5:checks7:bindings6:effects6:unbinds7:messages58:the name being renamed is not held in the living namespaces7:requires5:bounds9:key_params4:pathd5:s4:cites16:FS-LAW-NAMESPACEs5:checks8:containss7:messages203:the destination name is held and the living namespace still holds names inside it — a rename onto it would replace a container while its contents stayed recorded inside a name that no longer holds thems7:requires5:emptys9:key_params8:new_pathd5:s10:binds_kindd1:s8:from_keys4:paths4:cites16:FS-LAW-NAMESPACEs5:checks7:bindings6:effects4:binds9:key_params8:new_paths6:paramsd3:s10:provenances8:optionals4:paths8:requireds8:new_paths8:requireds9:law_citeds16:FS-LAW-NAMESPACEs4:kinds13:op_definitions4:names11:FILE-RENAMEs4:texts112:operation FILE-RENAME: when invoked and its checks pass -> append a FILE-RENAME decision citing FS-LAW-NAMESPACEs4:tiers5:owners7:rule_ids14:op:FILE-RENAMEs8:polaritys1:+s9:record_ids7:rec_148d16:s10:provenanced3:s10:could_readl0:s11:asserted_bys10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:sources6:systems10:rule_citeds10:CAP-IS-LAWs11:record_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.507556+00:00s12:content_forms6:inlines15:occurrence_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.507573+00:00s15:submission_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.507570+00:00s16:evidence_summaryns3:seqi149;s4:refsl0:s5:actors10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:actions9:CREATE-OPs6:objects13:op:FILE-CHOWNs6:origind2:s12:subsystem_ids6:kernels8:built_idi0;s6:targetns7:payloadd7:s10:definitiond9:s11:descriptions63:change file ownership — an amendment of the file's permissions12:object_params4:paths12:payload_froml4:s4:paths5:inodes3:uids3:gids16:provenance_params10:provenances17:structural_paramsl5:s4:paths5:inodes3:uids3:gids10:provenances4:cells1:Ss6:checksl0:s6:paramsd5:s10:provenances8:optionals3:gids8:optionals3:uids8:optionals4:paths8:requireds5:inodes8:optionals9:law_citeds11:FS-LAW-PERMs4:kinds13:op_definitions4:names10:FILE-CHOWNs4:texts105:operation FILE-CHOWN: when invoked and its checks pass -> append a FILE-CHOWN decision citing FS-LAW-PERMs4:tiers5:owners7:rule_ids13:op:FILE-CHOWNs8:polaritys1:+s9:record_ids7:rec_149d16:s10:provenanced3:s10:could_readl0:s11:asserted_bys10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:sources6:systems10:rule_citeds10:CAP-IS-LAWs11:record_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.510114+00:00s12:content_forms6:inlines15:occurrence_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.510137+00:00s15:submission_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.510134+00:00s16:evidence_summaryns3:seqi150;s4:refsl0:s5:actors10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:actions9:CREATE-OPs6:objects13:op:FILE-TIMESs6:origind2:s12:subsystem_ids6:kernels8:built_idi0;s6:targetns7:payloadd7:s10:definitiond9:s11:descriptions54:set a file's timestamps (design/10 §6, utimensat row)s12:object_params4:paths12:payload_froml4:s4:paths5:inodes5:atimes5:mtimes16:provenance_params10:provenances17:structural_paramsl5:s4:paths5:inodes5:atimes5:mtimes10:provenances4:cells1:Ss6:checksl0:s6:paramsd5:s10:provenances8:optionals4:paths8:requireds5:atimes8:optionals5:inodes8:optionals5:mtimes8:optionals9:law_citeds11:FS-LAW-PERMs4:kinds13:op_definitions4:names10:FILE-TIMESs4:texts105:operation FILE-TIMES: when invoked and its checks pass -> append a FILE-TIMES decision citing FS-LAW-PERMs4:tiers5:owners7:rule_ids13:op:FILE-TIMESs8:polaritys1:+s9:record_ids7:rec_150d16:s10:provenanced3:s10:could_readl0:s11:asserted_bys10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:sources6:systems10:rule_citeds10:CAP-IS-LAWs11:record_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.512808+00:00s12:content_forms6:inlines15:occurrence_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.512822+00:00s15:submission_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.512818+00:00s16:evidence_summaryns3:seqi151;s4:refsl0:s5:actors10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:actions9:CREATE-OPs6:objects17:op:FILE-XATTR-SETs6:origind2:s12:subsystem_ids6:kernels8:built_idi0;s6:targetns7:payloadd7:s10:definitiond10:s11:descriptions67:set an ordinary extended attribute — a recorded metadata DECISIONs11:param_kindsd1:s5:values5:bytess12:object_params4:paths12:payload_froml4:s4:paths5:inodes4:names5:values16:provenance_params10:provenances17:structural_paramsl5:s4:paths5:inodes4:names5:values10:provenances4:cells1:Ss6:checksl0:s6:paramsd5:s10:provenances8:optionals4:names8:requireds4:paths8:requireds5:inodes8:optionals5:values8:optionals9:law_citeds11:FS-LAW-PERMs4:kinds13:op_definitions4:names14:FILE-XATTR-SETs4:texts113:operation FILE-XATTR-SET: when invoked and its checks pass -> append a FILE-XATTR-SET decision citing FS-LAW-PERMs4:tiers5:owners7:rule_ids17:op:FILE-XATTR-SETs8:polaritys1:+s9:record_ids7:rec_151d16:s10:provenanced3:s10:could_readl0:s11:asserted_bys10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:sources6:systems10:rule_citeds10:CAP-IS-LAWs11:record_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.515822+00:00s12:content_forms6:inlines15:occurrence_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.515838+00:00s15:submission_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.515836+00:00s16:evidence_summaryns3:seqi152;s4:refsl0:s5:actors10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:actions9:CREATE-OPs6:objects20:op:FILE-XATTR-REMOVEs6:origind2:s12:subsystem_ids6:kernels8:built_idi0;s6:targetns7:payloadd7:s10:definitiond9:s11:descriptions37:remove an ordinary extended attributes12:object_params4:paths12:payload_froml3:s4:paths5:inodes4:names16:provenance_params10:provenances17:structural_paramsl4:s4:paths5:inodes4:names10:provenances4:cells1:Ss6:checksl0:s6:paramsd4:s10:provenances8:optionals4:names8:requireds4:paths8:requireds5:inodes8:optionals9:law_citeds11:FS-LAW-PERMs4:kinds13:op_definitions4:names17:FILE-XATTR-REMOVEs4:texts119:operation FILE-XATTR-REMOVE: when invoked and its checks pass -> append a FILE-XATTR-REMOVE decision citing FS-LAW-PERMs4:tiers5:owners7:rule_ids20:op:FILE-XATTR-REMOVEs8:polaritys1:+s9:record_ids7:rec_152d16:s10:provenanced3:s10:could_readl0:s11:asserted_bys10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:sources6:systems10:rule_citeds10:CAP-IS-LAWs11:record_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.519252+00:00s12:content_forms6:inlines15:occurrence_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.519268+00:00s15:submission_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.519266+00:00s16:evidence_summaryns3:seqi153;s4:refsl0:s5:actors10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:actions9:CREATE-OPs6:objects17:op:FILE-XATTR-LAWs6:origind2:s12:subsystem_ids6:kernels8:built_idi0;s6:targetns7:payloadd7:s10:definitiond12:s11:descriptions163:set a PERMISSION-BEARING extended attribute (security.* / system.posix_acl_*) — a rule with a one-file scope, recorded as LAW because its content is prescriptives11:param_kindsd1:s5:values4:texts12:object_params4:paths12:payload_froml4:s4:paths5:inodes4:names5:values14:param_defaultsd1:s5:spaces10:space:roots14:payload_derived1:s7:rule_idd1:s3:tpls17:acl:{path}#{name}s16:provenance_params10:provenances17:structural_paramsl6:s4:paths5:inodes4:names5:values5:spaces10:provenances4:cells1:Ss6:checksl0:s6:paramsd6:s10:provenances8:optionals4:names8:requireds4:paths8:requireds5:inodes8:optionals5:spaces8:optionals5:values8:optionals9:law_citeds11:FS-LAW-PERMs4:kinds13:op_definitions4:names14:FILE-XATTR-LAWs4:texts113:operation FILE-XATTR-LAW: when invoked and its checks pass -> append a FILE-XATTR-LAW decision citing FS-LAW-PERMs4:tiers5:owners7:rule_ids17:op:FILE-XATTR-LAWs8:polaritys1:+s9:record_ids7:rec_153d16:s10:provenanced3:s10:could_readl0:s11:asserted_bys10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:sources6:systems10:rule_citeds10:CAP-IS-LAWs11:record_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.523900+00:00s12:content_forms6:inlines15:occurrence_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.523917+00:00s15:submission_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.523913+00:00s16:evidence_summaryns3:seqi154;s4:refsl0:s5:actors10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:actions9:CREATE-OPs6:objects12:op:FILE-LOCKs6:origind2:s12:subsystem_ids6:kernels8:built_idi0;s6:targetns7:payloadd7:s10:definitiond10:s11:descriptions271:grant exclusivity over a byte range of a file (design/10 §6, the fcntl F_SETLK and flock rows — a lock grant, recorded, citing its rule). `length` 0 carries the POSIX meaning: to the end of the file, however far that moves. `owner` is the holder the port could assert.s11:param_kindsd1:s6:lengths8:quantitys12:object_params4:paths12:payload_froml6:s4:paths5:inodes5:ltypes5:starts6:lengths5:owners16:provenance_params10:provenances17:structural_paramsl7:s4:paths5:inodes5:ltypes5:starts6:lengths5:owners10:provenances4:cells1:Ss6:checksl0:s6:paramsd7:s10:provenances8:optionals4:paths8:requireds5:inodes8:optionals5:ltypes8:requireds5:owners8:optionals5:starts8:optionals6:lengths8:optionals9:law_citeds11:FS-LAW-LOCKs4:kinds13:op_definitions4:names9:FILE-LOCKs4:texts103:operation FILE-LOCK: when invoked and its checks pass -> append a FILE-LOCK decision citing FS-LAW-LOCKs4:tiers5:owners7:rule_ids12:op:FILE-LOCKs8:polaritys1:+s9:record_ids7:rec_154d16:s10:provenanced3:s10:could_readl0:s11:asserted_bys10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:sources6:systems10:rule_citeds10:CAP-IS-LAWs11:record_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.526874+00:00s12:content_forms6:inlines15:occurrence_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.526888+00:00s15:submission_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.526885+00:00s16:evidence_summaryns3:seqi155;s4:refsl0:s5:actors10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:actions9:CREATE-OPs6:objects14:op:FILE-UNLOCKs6:origind2:s12:subsystem_ids6:kernels8:built_idi0;s6:targetns7:payloadd7:s10:definitiond11:s11:descriptions280:release exclusivity a caller held (design/10 §6). `mechanism` says which caller act released it: an explicit unlock, or the POSIX rule that closing a descriptor for the file releases that process's locks on it — the mechanism belongs beneath the decision, never in place of it.s11:param_kindsd1:s6:lengths8:quantitys12:object_params4:paths12:payload_froml6:s4:paths5:inodes5:starts6:lengths5:owners9:mechanisms16:provenance_params10:provenances17:structural_paramsl7:s4:paths5:inodes5:starts6:lengths5:owners9:mechanisms10:provenances4:cells1:Ss6:checksl0:s6:paramsd7:s10:provenances8:optionals4:paths8:requireds5:inodes8:optionals5:owners8:optionals5:starts8:optionals6:lengths8:optionals9:mechanisms8:optionals8:act_kinds7:releases9:law_citeds11:FS-LAW-LOCKs4:kinds13:op_definitions4:names11:FILE-UNLOCKs4:texts107:operation FILE-UNLOCK: when invoked and its checks pass -> append a FILE-UNLOCK decision citing FS-LAW-LOCKs4:tiers5:owners7:rule_ids14:op:FILE-UNLOCKs8:polaritys1:+s9:record_ids7:rec_155d16:s10:provenanced3:s10:could_readl0:s11:asserted_bys10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:sources6:systems10:rule_citeds10:CAP-IS-LAWs11:record_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.529997+00:00s12:content_forms6:inlines15:occurrence_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.530010+00:00s15:submission_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.530007+00:00s16:evidence_summaryns3:seqi156;s4:refsl0:s5:actors10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:actions9:CREATE-OPs6:objects22:op:FILE-READ-AGGREGATEs6:origind2:s12:subsystem_ids6:kernels8:built_idi0;s6:targetns7:payloadd7:s10:definitiond10:s11:descriptions151:the read-traffic audit aggregate for one inode over one window (STREAM); the caller's bytes were delivered exactly and are not what this record carriess11:param_kindsd1:s5:bytess8:quantitys12:object_params4:paths12:payload_froml4:s4:paths5:inodes5:readss5:bytess16:provenance_params10:provenances17:structural_paramsl5:s4:paths5:inodes5:readss5:bytess10:provenances4:cells1:Ss6:checksl0:s6:paramsd5:s10:provenances8:optionals4:paths8:requireds5:bytess8:optionals5:inodes8:optionals5:readss8:optionals9:law_citeds19:FS-READ-AGGREGATIONs4:kinds13:op_definitions4:names19:FILE-READ-AGGREGATEs4:texts131:operation FILE-READ-AGGREGATE: when invoked and its checks pass -> append a FILE-READ-AGGREGATE decision citing FS-READ-AGGREGATIONs4:tiers5:owners7:rule_ids22:op:FILE-READ-AGGREGATEs8:polaritys1:+s9:record_ids7:rec_156d16:s10:provenanced3:s10:could_readl0:s11:asserted_bys10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:sources6:systems10:rule_citeds10:CAP-IS-LAWs11:record_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.533236+00:00s12:content_forms6:inlines15:occurrence_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.533259+00:00s15:submission_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.533253+00:00s16:evidence_summaryns3:seqi157;s4:refsl0:s5:actors10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:actions9:CREATE-OPs6:objects10:op:MAP-UIDs6:origind2:s12:subsystem_ids6:kernels8:built_idi0;s6:targetns7:payloadd7:s10:definitiond10:s11:descriptions161:record that a kernel-asserted uid at the port acts as a named account — a recorded act, from which actor resolution is DERIVED; never a synchronized user tables12:payload_froml2:s3:uids7:accounts13:object_derived1:s3:tpls9:uid:{uid}s16:provenance_params10:provenances17:structural_paramsl3:s3:uids7:accounts10:provenances4:cells1:Ss5:mintsl1:s3:uids6:checksl0:s6:paramsd3:s10:provenances8:optionals3:uids8:requireds7:accounts8:requireds9:law_citeds10:CAP-IS-LAWs4:kinds13:op_definitions4:names7:MAP-UIDs4:texts98:operation MAP-UID: when invoked and its checks pass -> append a MAP-UID decision citing CAP-IS-LAWs4:tiers5:owners7:rule_ids10:op:MAP-UIDs8:polaritys1:+s9:record_ids7:rec_157d16:s10:provenanced3:s10:could_readl0:s11:asserted_bys10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:sources6:systems10:rule_citeds10:CAP-IS-LAWs11:record_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.542066+00:00s12:content_forms6:inlines15:occurrence_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.542094+00:00s15:submission_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.542087+00:00s16:evidence_summaryns3:seqi158;s4:refsl0:s5:actors10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:actions9:CREATE-OPs6:objects15:op:CUSTODY-HALTs6:origind2:s12:subsystem_ids6:kernels8:built_idi0;s6:targetns7:payloadd7:s10:definitiond9:s11:descriptions153:halt the assume: the state replayed from the record alone differs from the state being served, so the mount goes read-only and the divergence is recordeds12:object_params6:reasons12:payload_froml2:s6:reasons6:details16:provenance_params10:provenances17:structural_paramsl3:s6:reasons6:details10:provenances4:cells1:Ss6:checksl0:s6:paramsd3:s10:provenances8:optionals6:details8:optionals6:reasons8:requireds9:law_citeds22:FS-LAW-DIVERGENCE-HALTs4:kinds13:op_definitions4:names12:CUSTODY-HALTs4:texts120:operation CUSTODY-HALT: when invoked and its checks pass -> append a CUSTODY-HALT decision citing FS-LAW-DIVERGENCE-HALTs4:tiers5:owners7:rule_ids15:op:CUSTODY-HALTs8:polaritys1:+s9:record_ids7:rec_158d16:s10:provenanced3:s10:could_readl0:s11:asserted_bys10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:sources6:systems10:rule_citeds10:CAP-IS-LAWs11:record_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.547026+00:00s12:content_forms6:inlines15:occurrence_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.547050+00:00s15:submission_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.547045+00:00s16:evidence_summaryns3:seqi159;s4:refsl0:s5:actors10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:actions9:CREATE-OPs6:objects24:op:FILE-CUSTODY-TRANSFERs6:origind2:s12:subsystem_ids6:kernels8:built_idi0;s6:targetns7:payloadd7:s10:definitiond8:s11:descriptions800:hand an OPEN HANDLE from one entity to another: the custody plane's verb for a handover, and the one act in it whose subject is a RELATION BETWEEN TWO PARTIES rather than a fact about a file. Every other FILE-* action answers what a file IS or who holds exclusivity over part of one; this one answers WHO HOLDS IT NOW, and the answer is a fold of these records rather than a field on anything. THE RECORD SHAPE IS THE POINT, not the check vocabulary: EP-30-E1 established that a current holding is expressible when the state is written as an amending declaration of the SAME action under latest-seq-wins, and blind when it is written as a separate act — so a handover amends this action and never mints a second one. `device` is INHERITED from the binding that founded it and is never derived here.s12:object_params6:handles12:payload_froml4:s6:handles11:from_entitys9:to_entitys6:devices17:structural_paramsl4:s6:handles11:from_entitys9:to_entitys6:devices4:cells1:Ss6:checksl5:d6:s4:cites23:FS-LAW-CUSTODY-TRANSFERs5:checks13:require_priors5:fields10:account_ids5:params11:from_entitys6:actions14:CREATE-ACCOUNTs7:messages302:the party this act would hand the handle FROM is not an established entity — a handover names two parties, and a party is a recorded establishment rather than a string the caller supplies. A transfer whose giver is a bare value is a property change wearing a transfer's name, and this rule refuses itd6:s4:cites23:FS-LAW-CUSTODY-TRANSFERs5:checks13:require_priors5:fields10:account_ids5:params9:to_entitys6:actions14:CREATE-ACCOUNTs7:messages283:the party this act would hand the handle TO is not an established entity — a handover names two parties, and a party is a recorded establishment rather than a string the caller supplies. A transfer whose receiver is a bare value hands the handle to nobody, and this rule refuses itd6:s4:cites23:FS-LAW-CUSTODY-TRANSFERs5:checks13:require_priors5:fields4:paths5:params6:handles6:actions9:FILE-OPENs7:messages178:no FILE-OPEN founds this handle — custody cannot be handed over before it is granted, and a transfer of a handle no record opens would append an act nobody could have performedd6:s4:cites23:FS-LAW-CUSTODY-TRANSFERs5:checks13:require_priors5:fields6:devices5:params6:devices6:actions11:BIND-DEVICEs7:messages242:the device this handle stands on is not one a prior BIND-DEVICE founded — the transfer INHERITS the device identity from the binding and never re-derives it, so a device no binding founds is a channel-side invention and this rule refuses itd9:s11:value_fields9:to_entitys12:when_unbounds6:permits4:cites23:FS-LAW-CUSTODY-TRANSFERs5:checks11:bound_fields5:fields6:handles5:params11:from_entitys6:actions21:FILE-CUSTODY-TRANSFERs7:messages342:the party this act would hand the handle FROM is not the party that holds it — this handle's latest transfer named a different entity as its recipient, and a handover by someone other than the holder is not a transfer of custody but an assertion about one. THE GIVER MUST HOLD WHAT IT GIVES AWAY, and this rule refuses an act that does not.s9:key_params6:handles6:paramsd4:s11:from_entitys8:requireds6:devices8:requireds6:handles8:requireds9:to_entitys8:requireds9:law_citeds23:FS-LAW-CUSTODY-TRANSFERs4:kinds13:op_definitions4:names21:FILE-CUSTODY-TRANSFERs4:texts139:operation FILE-CUSTODY-TRANSFER: when invoked and its checks pass -> append a FILE-CUSTODY-TRANSFER decision citing FS-LAW-CUSTODY-TRANSFERs4:tiers5:owners7:rule_ids24:op:FILE-CUSTODY-TRANSFERs8:polaritys1:+s9:record_ids7:rec_159d16:s10:provenanced3:s10:could_readl0:s11:asserted_bys10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:sources6:systems10:rule_citeds10:CAP-IS-LAWs11:record_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.551729+00:00s12:content_forms6:inlines15:occurrence_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.551746+00:00s15:submission_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.551744+00:00s16:evidence_summaryns3:seqi160;s4:refsl0:s5:actors10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:actions9:CREATE-OPs6:objects15:op:SESSION-OPENs6:origind2:s12:subsystem_ids6:kernels8:built_idi0;s6:targetns7:payloadd7:s10:definitiond11:s11:descriptions420:record that a decider has opened a live working context, declaring the read-set that binds what it is doing. A known contact point, so a law change whose reach meets this session's declared view can be delivered to it rather than overtaking it in flight. This is the decider session of the two-times law, unrelated to the POSIX setsid session — the /proc and scheduling surfaces keep the POSIX word for the POSIX things12:payload_froml3:s10:session_ids8:read_sets7:accounts13:object_derived1:s3:tpls20:session:{session_id}s14:param_defaultsd1:s7:accounts6:$actors14:payload_derived3:s12:record_classd1:s3:tpls8:DECISIONs4:kindd1:s3:tpls7:sessions5:eventd1:s3:tpls4:opens17:structural_paramsl3:s10:session_ids8:read_sets7:accounts4:cells1:Ss5:mintsl1:s10:session_ids6:checksl0:s6:paramsd3:s10:session_ids8:requireds7:accounts8:optionals8:read_sets8:requireds9:law_citeds16:SESSION-DECLAREDs4:kinds13:op_definitions4:names12:SESSION-OPENs4:texts120:operation SESSION-OPEN: when invoked -> append the decider's session with its declared read-set, citing SESSION-DECLAREDs4:tiers5:owners7:rule_ids15:op:SESSION-OPENs8:polaritys1:+s9:record_ids7:rec_160d16:s10:provenanced3:s10:could_readl0:s11:asserted_bys10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:sources6:systems10:rule_citeds10:CAP-IS-LAWs11:record_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.556905+00:00s12:content_forms6:inlines15:occurrence_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.556930+00:00s15:submission_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.556924+00:00s16:evidence_summaryns3:seqi161;s4:refsl0:s5:actors10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:actions9:CREATE-OPs6:objects16:op:SESSION-CLOSEs6:origind2:s12:subsystem_ids6:kernels8:built_idi0;s6:targetns7:payloadd7:s10:definitiond9:s11:descriptions127:record that a decider's working context has ended. Live-or-closed is the difference between the two records and is held nowheres12:payload_froml1:s10:session_ids13:object_derived1:s3:tpls20:session:{session_id}s14:payload_derived3:s12:record_classd1:s3:tpls8:DECISIONs4:kindd1:s3:tpls7:sessions5:eventd1:s3:tpls5:closes17:structural_paramsl1:s10:session_ids4:cells1:Ss6:checksl0:s6:paramsd1:s10:session_ids8:requireds9:law_citeds16:SESSION-DECLAREDs4:kinds13:op_definitions4:names13:SESSION-CLOSEs4:texts98:operation SESSION-CLOSE: when invoked -> append the close of that session, citing SESSION-DECLAREDs4:tiers5:owners7:rule_ids16:op:SESSION-CLOSEs8:polaritys1:+s9:record_ids7:rec_161d16:s10:provenanced3:s10:could_readl0:s11:asserted_bys10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:sources6:systems10:rule_citeds10:CAP-IS-LAWs11:record_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.563206+00:00s12:content_forms6:inlines15:occurrence_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.563234+00:00s15:submission_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.563228+00:00s16:evidence_summaryns3:seqi162;s4:refsl0:s5:actors10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:actions9:CREATE-OPs6:objects11:op:OVERTURNs6:origind2:s12:subsystem_ids6:kernels8:built_idi0;s6:targetns7:payloadd7:s10:definitiond10:s11:descriptions424:record the reconciliation verdict on one act a late-arriving law reached: an appended decision acting FORWARD, citing the reaching law (or the overturned ancestor whose exclusion reached it), the overturned act, and both deciding times. Nothing recorded is edited and nothing disappears — the act and its overturn are both permanently on the record, and an asOf answer from before the overturn still shows the act's effects12:anchor_guards10:post-states12:payload_froml9:s10:target_seqs12:reaching_seqs20:target_deciding_times22:reaching_deciding_times5:sweeps7:law_seqs5:rounds5:basiss6:reasons13:object_derived1:s3:tpls19:record:{target_seq}s14:payload_derived2:s12:record_classd1:s3:tpls8:DECISIONs4:kindd1:s3:tpls8:overturns17:structural_paramsl9:s10:target_seqs12:reaching_seqs20:target_deciding_times22:reaching_deciding_times5:sweeps7:law_seqs5:rounds5:basiss6:reasons4:cells1:Ss6:checksl0:s6:paramsd9:s10:target_seqs8:requireds12:reaching_seqs8:requireds20:target_deciding_times8:requireds22:reaching_deciding_times8:requireds5:basiss8:optionals5:rounds8:optionals5:sweeps8:requireds6:reasons8:optionals7:law_seqs8:optionals9:law_citeds18:TWO-TIMES-OVERTURNs4:kinds13:op_definitions4:names8:OVERTURNs4:texts457:operation OVERTURN: when invoked and the sweep's computed post-state leaves no chain without a root and does not move root -> append the reconciliation verdict citing TWO-TIMES-OVERTURN; otherwise refuse citing CONST-AUTHORITY-ANCHORED and route to the owner. The anchor leash is part of this definition at birth, never a later patch, and its trigger reads no act kind: it asks the anchor law's own effect-level question of the post-state the sweep computeds4:tiers5:owners7:rule_ids11:op:OVERTURNs8:polaritys1:+s9:record_ids7:rec_162d16:s10:provenanced3:s10:could_readl0:s11:asserted_bys10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:sources6:systems10:rule_citeds10:CAP-IS-LAWs11:record_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.567461+00:00s12:content_forms6:inlines15:occurrence_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.567478+00:00s15:submission_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.567475+00:00s16:evidence_summaryns3:seqi163;s4:refsl0:s5:actors10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:actions9:CREATE-OPs6:objects20:op:DECLARE-IO-WINDOWs6:origind2:s12:subsystem_ids6:kernels8:built_idi0;s6:targetns7:payloadd7:s10:definitiond8:s11:descriptions1543:declare an I/O WINDOW under DEV-LAW-BIND: the named surface through which a class of device I/O may be admitted, WITH THE ACCESS THAT SURFACE COSTS. DEV-LAW-BIND says a bind grants custody and not I/O and that I/O admission CITES A WINDOW DECLARATION BY NAME; this op is how such a declaration comes into existence. THE ACCESS COST IS A REQUIRED PARAMETER AND NOT AN ANNOTATION (K12 — every view costs its own dependencies, priced at authoring): a window whose surface can only be read by a privileged observer is a window that has bought a privilege, and a declaration that hid that would price the view at zero. `sees` AND `does_not_see` ARE BOTH REQUIRED: the no-bare-form instruction extended from parameter forms to parameter ABSENCES — a window declaring nothing it sees would still admit its act class while claiming no observability, which is the comforting-fallback shape wearing a declaration. A window declares ADMISSION and never GRANULARITY: at what granularity an admitted act is RECORDED is the INTAKE declaration, which is EP-29 W2's first product and is deliberately absent from this vocabulary so nothing lands by drift. `families`, `events_available` and `established` ARE PARAMETERS AND NOT DECORATION: a window may not be declared without saying how its surface was ESTABLISHED, which is the whole lesson of the pass that authored it — a window declared against a surface nobody drove is the wrong-reference class authored into law. NOT declared `act_kind: release` — this op founds a declaration, it ends nothing.s12:payload_froml12:s6:windows12:device_classs7:surfaces15:surface_versions6:accesss16:access_mechanisms12:access_scopes4:seess12:does_not_sees8:familiess16:events_availables11:establisheds13:object_derived1:s3:tpls15:window:{window}s17:structural_paramsl12:s6:windows12:device_classs7:surfaces15:surface_versions6:accesss16:access_mechanisms12:access_scopes4:seess12:does_not_sees8:familiess16:events_availables11:establisheds4:cells1:Ss6:checksl0:s6:paramsd12:s11:establisheds8:requireds12:access_scopes8:requireds12:device_classs8:requireds12:does_not_sees8:requireds15:surface_versions8:requireds16:access_mechanisms8:requireds16:events_availables8:requireds4:seess8:requireds6:accesss8:requireds6:windows8:requireds7:surfaces8:requireds8:familiess8:requireds9:law_citeds12:DEV-LAW-BINDs4:kinds13:op_definitions4:names17:DECLARE-IO-WINDOWs4:texts120:operation DECLARE-IO-WINDOW: when invoked and its checks pass -> append a DECLARE-IO-WINDOW decision citing DEV-LAW-BINDs4:tiers5:owners7:rule_ids20:op:DECLARE-IO-WINDOWs8:polaritys1:+s9:record_ids7:rec_163d16:s10:provenanced3:s10:could_readl0:s11:asserted_bys10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:sources6:systems10:rule_citeds10:CAP-IS-LAWs11:record_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.571017+00:00s12:content_forms6:inlines15:occurrence_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.571030+00:00s15:submission_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.571027+00:00s16:evidence_summaryns3:seqi164;s4:refsl0:s5:actors10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:actions9:CREATE-OPs6:objects25:op:DEVICE-IO-WINDOW-WRITEs6:origind2:s12:subsystem_ids6:kernels8:built_idi0;s6:targetns7:payloadd7:s10:definitiond8:s11:descriptions2003:admit a device I/O write across a DECLARED window. This is the act class DEV-LAW-BIND named and, until this pass, founded no declaration for — so it refused citing the terminal rule that an act class no declaration founds does not exist. THE REFUSAL IS NARROWED HERE AND NOT REMOVED: the act is now declared, and it refuses on THREE stated grounds instead of on absence. FIRST, a bind: a bind grants custody and I/O still needs the custody to exist, so an I/O act naming a device no record ever bound refuses. SECOND, AND IT IS WHAT MAKES CUSTODY REVOCABLE RATHER THAN ONLY GRANTABLE (EP-30-W2): the bind must still BE IN FORCE. The first ground asks whether a bind EVER happened, and history never unhappens, so it went on admitting bytes for a device whose custody had ended — the gap EP-30-P1 pinned as a measured verdict rather than as a paragraph. This row reads the LATEST record in this device's binding stream and requires it to still declare a driver. Because op:UNBIND writes its record into BIND-DEVICE's own stream (EP-30-W1b) while still recording that UNBIND wrote it, the latest record after a revocation is the unbind, an unbind declares no driver, and the licence stops computing. A FRESH BIND RESTORES IT: latest-seq-wins means a re-bind is the newest declaration and admits again, so a revocation is not a one-way door. THIRD, and this is the sentence DEV-LAW-BIND wrote, I/O ADMISSION CITES A WINDOW DECLARATION BY NAME: the cited window must be a DECLARED one, and a name that no DECLARE-IO-WINDOW record founds is refused — which is why the citation is checked against that action and not against the law records generally, since keying it on rule ids would let any law id in the founding pass as a window. EVERY OTHER DEVICE ACT CLASS STILL HOLDS NO DECLARATION and still refuses citing the terminal rule; this op widens the permitted set by exactly the windows the founding declares and by nothing else. NOT declared `act_kind: release` — it moves bytes, it ends nothing.s12:object_params6:devices12:payload_froml3:s6:devices6:windows5:bytess17:structural_paramsl3:s6:devices6:windows5:bytess4:cells1:Ss6:checksl3:d6:s4:cites12:DEV-LAW-BINDs5:checks13:require_priors5:fields6:devices5:params6:devices6:actions11:BIND-DEVICEs7:messages91:cannot move bytes for a device no record ever bound — a bind grants the custody I/O needsd8:s11:value_fields6:drivers4:cites12:DEV-LAW-BINDs5:checks11:prior_values5:fields6:devices5:params6:devices6:actions11:BIND-DEVICEs7:messages214:the binding declaration this act's licence computes from declares its driver explicitly UNESTABLISHED, so custody is declared absent and no licence computes — refused, recorded, citing the law that grants custodys7:requires11:establishedd6:s4:cites12:DEV-LAW-BINDs5:checks13:require_priors5:fields6:windows5:params6:windows6:actions17:DECLARE-IO-WINDOWs7:messages128:I/O admission cites a window declaration BY NAME and this name is declared by no record — an undeclared window permits nothings6:paramsd3:s5:bytess8:requireds6:devices8:requireds6:windows8:requireds9:law_citeds12:DEV-LAW-BINDs4:kinds13:op_definitions4:names22:DEVICE-IO-WINDOW-WRITEs4:texts130:operation DEVICE-IO-WINDOW-WRITE: when invoked and its checks pass -> append a DEVICE-IO-WINDOW-WRITE decision citing DEV-LAW-BINDs4:tiers5:owners7:rule_ids25:op:DEVICE-IO-WINDOW-WRITEs8:polaritys1:+s9:record_ids7:rec_164d16:s10:provenanced3:s10:could_readl0:s11:asserted_bys10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:sources6:systems10:rule_citeds10:CAP-IS-LAWs11:record_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.580285+00:00s12:content_forms6:inlines15:occurrence_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.580300+00:00s15:submission_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.580296+00:00s16:evidence_summaryns3:seqi167;s4:refsl0:s5:actors10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:actions9:CREATE-OPs6:objects17:op:DECLARE-INTAKEs6:origind2:s12:subsystem_ids6:kernels8:built_idi0;s6:targetns7:payloadd7:s10:definitiond9:s11:descriptions2494:declare an INTAKE under DEV-LAW-INTAKE: the grade at which device INPUT arrivals admitted through a named window are RECORDED. DEV-LAW-INTAKE says an arrival is never recorded at per-interrupt grade and that a covering record spans a bounded WINDOW of arrivals; this op is how such a bound comes into existence. IT DECLARES THE GRADE AND NEVER THE ADMISSION — admission is DECLARE-IO-WINDOW's, under DEV-LAW-BIND, and the two are kept apart because a declaration that did both could widen what is admitted while appearing to change only how much is written down. 

EVERY MEASUREMENT-DERIVED VALUE IS A STRUCTURED FIELD AND NOT A BARE NUMBER, and `derived_values` NAMES WHICH PARAMETERS THOSE ARE. A bare number in law is a value whose population and basis are unfalsifiable (charter §A51): each derived value carries `value`, `cell`, `population`, `basis` and `why_this_value` — the last named that way because `derivation` is a RESERVED KEY estate-wide (T-CHAIN-COMPUTED: no record anywhere carries a stored reasoning chain, because a stored chain is a stored derivative) — so a value with no calibration cell behind it is visible as a MISSING KEY rather than as a missing sentence. `derived_values` is a required parameter rather than a convention so that the set being checked is declared by the record itself; a declaration cannot shrink its own audited population by leaving a derived value off the list, because a derived value not on the list is a defect the rows read structurally. 

AN UNESTABLISHED VALUE IS DECLARED UNESTABLISHED, NEVER OMITTED — the no-bare-form instruction extended from parameter forms to parameter ABSENCES, which is the shape DECLARE-IO-WINDOW's required `does_not_see` already took. A class whose per-act unit the calibration could not establish carries `value: null` with the basis stating WHY, rather than a plausible number divided out of a requested load. 

`closers` ARE EVENT-BASED BY LAW, and `limits` and `does_not_declare` ARE REQUIRED: a declaration that named no limit would generalise silently from one guest and one boot, and a declaration that named no absence would read as covering everything it did not mention. `established` states how the table this declaration derives from was TAKEN — an intake declared against a calibration nobody drove is the wrong-reference class authored into law, one layer in from where the window declarations met it. 

NOT declared `act_kind: release` — this op founds a declaration, it ends nothing.s11:param_kindsd2:s12:max_arrivalss11:measurements25:arrivals_per_admitted_acts11:measurements12:payload_froml12:s6:intakes12:device_classs6:windows5:grades12:max_arrivalss25:arrivals_per_admitted_acts14:derived_valuess7:closerss7:recordss16:does_not_declares6:limitss11:establisheds13:object_derived1:s3:tpls15:intake:{intake}s17:structural_paramsl12:s6:intakes12:device_classs6:windows5:grades12:max_arrivalss25:arrivals_per_admitted_acts14:derived_valuess7:closerss7:recordss16:does_not_declares6:limitss11:establisheds4:cells1:Ss6:checksl1:d6:s4:cites14:DEV-LAW-INTAKEs5:checks13:require_priors5:fields6:windows5:params6:windows6:actions17:DECLARE-IO-WINDOWs7:messages185:an intake declares the grade at which arrivals ADMITTED THROUGH A WINDOW are recorded, and this window name is founded by no declaration — a grade for an admission that does not exists6:paramsd12:s11:establisheds8:requireds12:device_classs8:requireds12:max_arrivalss8:requireds14:derived_valuess8:requireds16:does_not_declares8:requireds25:arrivals_per_admitted_acts8:requireds5:grades8:requireds6:intakes8:requireds6:limitss8:requireds6:windows8:requireds7:closerss8:requireds7:recordss8:requireds9:law_citeds14:DEV-LAW-INTAKEs4:kinds13:op_definitions4:names14:DECLARE-INTAKEs4:texts116:operation DECLARE-INTAKE: when invoked and its checks pass -> append a DECLARE-INTAKE decision citing DEV-LAW-INTAKEs4:tiers5:owners7:rule_ids17:op:DECLARE-INTAKEs8:polaritys1:+s9:record_ids7:rec_167d16:s10:provenanced3:s10:could_readl0:s11:asserted_bys10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:sources6:systems10:rule_citeds10:CAP-IS-LAWs11:record_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.584374+00:00s12:content_forms6:inlines15:occurrence_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.584392+00:00s15:submission_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.584389+00:00s16:evidence_summaryns3:seqi168;s4:refsl0:s5:actors10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:actions9:CREATE-OPs6:objects22:op:DEVICE-INTAKE-COVERs6:origind2:s12:subsystem_ids6:kernels8:built_idi0;s6:targetns7:payloadd7:s10:definitiond9:s11:descriptions5011:write the COVERING RECORD DEV-LAW-INTAKE governs: one recorded INPUT standing for a WINDOW of admitted device arrivals. THIS LAW HAS DESCRIBED THIS RECORD SINCE v1.22.0 AND SUPPLIED NO OPERATION THAT WRITES ONE — EP-29 W3b's walk found that exactly one operation cited this law and it was DECLARE-INTAKE, the DECLARING operation, so C3's intake crossing and C7's fail-closed refusal both required a record no operation could produce. This is that operation, and the division from DECLARE-INTAKE is the point: DECLARE-INTAKE declares THE GRADE at which arrivals are recorded and writes no arrival; this writes ONE RECORD AT THAT DECLARED GRADE and declares nothing. Recording through DECLARE-INTAKE is barred by this law's own words, and filing this record under DEV-LAW-BIND would file the RECORD's question under the ADMISSION law — a second source of truth about what this world's law declares.

WHAT IT CARRIES IS THE LAW'S OWN LIST AND NOTHING BESIDE IT: the COUNT of arrivals covered, the BYTE TOTAL over them, the DEVICE the arrivals were attributed to, the WINDOW they were admitted under BY NAME, and this law's citation together with the intake declaration's name. NEVER THE CONTENT — device I/O content is STREAM and is classified out, which the window declarations already state in their own `does_not_see`. A covering record makes no governed act invisible: it names how many there were and how many bytes they moved.

FAIL-CLOSED AT THE DEVICE LAYER, AND THE GATE COMPUTES THE LICENCE RATHER THAN A CALLER ASSERTING IT. The `prior_value` check reads THE CITED DECLARATION'S OWN `max_arrivals.value` and requires it ESTABLISHED. Where this law declares a class's threshold UNESTABLISHED — an explicit no-value, not an unwritten gap — no licence computes, the act is permitted by nothing, and the gate refuses it citing the TIP-LEVEL TERMINAL RULE that what no declaration permits does not exist. That is the same citation an act class no declaration founds already gets, so this operation introduces no second citation object and no law gains a sentence. THE VALUE COMES FROM THE LAW-DATA AND NEVER FROM A PARAMETER: nothing a caller passes can move the answer, which is what separates a licence test from a check the caller satisfies by construction.

THE CUSTODY ROW IS DERIVED FROM THE DECLARATION'S OWN CLOSER, NOT ADDED FOR SAFETY. Every intake declaration under this law names `unbind` as a closer — the covering record closes when the custody that admitted the I/O ends — so a covering record written for a device no record binds would contradict the declaration it cites. Its refusal cites DEV-LAW-BIND because custody is that law's object; the RECORD is filed under DEV-LAW-INTAKE, which is this operation's `law_cited` and the whole of what the wrong-law bar is about.

AND THE CLOSER IS NOW ENFORCED AND NOT ONLY DECLARED (EP-30-W2). The custody row above asks whether a bind EVER happened, which history answers YES forever, so an unbind closed nothing and this operation went on writing covering records after the custody that admitted the arrivals had ended — a declaration naming `unbind` as its closer, with nothing closing. The second custody row reads the LATEST record in this device's binding stream and requires it to still declare a driver: op:UNBIND writes into BIND-DEVICE's own stream (EP-30-W1b), an unbind declares no driver, and the licence stops computing at exactly the act the declaration named. It cites DEV-LAW-BIND on the same ground as the row above — custody is that law's object — and a fresh bind restores admission, because latest-seq-wins makes the newest declaration the one in force.

EVERY PARAMETER FORM IS EXPLICIT (charter C7's rule, and the no-bare-form instruction this law's declaring operation already carries): a form taken by silence is not declining the choice, it is taking it undecided.

TWO THINGS THIS OPERATION DOES NOT ENFORCE, WRITTEN HERE RATHER THAN LEFT TO BE DISCOVERED, because each is a gap the licensed vocabulary cannot close and both are RAISED by the pass that landed this. (1) THE WINDOW ROW AND THE INTAKE ROW MAY MEET TWO DIFFERENT RECORDS: each `require_prior` is an independent existence scan, so a caller naming a declared window and a declared intake that do not belong together satisfies both — the same limitation that made the threshold read unsayable, and closing it needs a same-record read across two fields, which the licence for one kind does not cover. (2) NO ROW REFUSES `arrival_count` OF ONE. This law's never-clause binds DECLARATIONS — no declaration may set a bound of one — and a covering record standing for exactly one arrival is the per-interrupt grade wearing a window's name in the law's own words; expressing it needs a numeric comparison against a parameter that no live check kind performs. Both are named for the operation's first consumer rather than fixed by a kind nobody licensed.

NOT declared `act_kind: release` — this operation writes a record, it ends nothing.s11:param_kindsd2:s10:byte_totals11:measurements13:arrival_counts11:measurements12:object_params6:devices12:payload_froml5:s6:intakes6:devices6:windows13:arrival_counts10:byte_totals17:structural_paramsl5:s6:intakes6:devices6:windows13:arrival_counts10:byte_totals4:cells1:Ss6:checksl4:d6:s4:cites12:DEV-LAW-BINDs5:checks13:require_priors5:fields6:devices5:params6:devices6:actions11:BIND-DEVICEs7:messages199:cannot cover arrivals for a device no record ever bound — every intake declaration under this law names unbind as a closer, so a covering record without custody contradicts the declaration it citesd8:s11:value_fields6:drivers4:cites12:DEV-LAW-BINDs5:checks11:prior_values5:fields6:devices5:params6:devices6:actions11:BIND-DEVICEs7:messages277:the binding declaration this covering record's licence computes from declares its driver explicitly UNESTABLISHED, so the custody its own intake declaration names as the closer is declared absent and no licence computes — refused, recorded, citing the law that grants custodys7:requires11:establishedd6:s4:cites14:DEV-LAW-INTAKEs5:checks13:require_priors5:fields6:windows5:params6:windows6:actions14:DECLARE-INTAKEs7:messages177:no intake declaration covers this window, so there is no declared GRADE at which arrivals admitted through it are recorded — a covering record at a grade no declaration foundsd8:s11:value_fields18:max_arrivals.values4:cites10:P3-CLOSUREs5:checks11:prior_values5:fields6:intakes5:params6:intakes6:actions14:DECLARE-INTAKEs7:messages204:this intake declaration leaves its threshold UNESTABLISHED, so no licence computes for an arrival of its class and the act is permitted by nothing — refused, recorded, citing the tip-level terminal rules7:requires11:establisheds6:paramsd5:s10:byte_totals8:requireds13:arrival_counts8:requireds6:devices8:requireds6:intakes8:requireds6:windows8:requireds9:law_citeds14:DEV-LAW-INTAKEs4:kinds13:op_definitions4:names19:DEVICE-INTAKE-COVERs4:texts126:operation DEVICE-INTAKE-COVER: when invoked and its checks pass -> append a DEVICE-INTAKE-COVER decision citing DEV-LAW-INTAKEs4:tiers5:owners7:rule_ids22:op:DEVICE-INTAKE-COVERs8:polaritys1:+s9:record_ids7:rec_168d16:s10:provenanced3:s10:could_readl0:s11:asserted_bys10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:sources6:systems10:rule_citeds10:CAP-IS-LAWs11:record_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.595713+00:00s12:content_forms6:inlines15:occurrence_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.595730+00:00s15:submission_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.595725+00:00s16:evidence_summaryns3:seqi171;s4:refsl0:s5:actors10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:actions9:CREATE-OPs6:objects15:op:OPEN-CONTENTs6:origind2:s12:subsystem_ids6:kernels8:built_idi0;s6:targetns7:payloadd7:s10:definitiond7:s11:descriptions66:an allowed reader opens a sealed content piece — a recorded reads12:object_params5:pieces17:structural_paramsl1:s5:pieces4:cells1:Ss6:checksl0:s6:paramsd1:s5:pieces8:requireds9:law_citeds10:CAP-IS-LAWs4:kinds13:op_definitions4:names12:OPEN-CONTENTs4:texts108:operation OPEN-CONTENT: when invoked and its checks pass -> append a OPEN-CONTENT decision citing CAP-IS-LAWs4:tiers5:owners7:rule_ids15:op:OPEN-CONTENTs8:polaritys1:+s9:record_ids7:rec_171d16:s10:provenanced3:s10:could_readl0:s11:asserted_bys10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:sources6:systems10:rule_citeds10:CAP-IS-LAWs11:record_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.599019+00:00s12:content_forms6:inlines15:occurrence_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.599033+00:00s15:submission_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.599030+00:00s16:evidence_summaryns3:seqi172;s4:refsl0:s5:actors10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:actions9:CREATE-OPs6:objects14:op:SOCKET-OPENs6:origind2:s12:subsystem_ids6:kernels8:built_idi0;s6:targetns7:payloadd7:s10:definitiond9:s11:descriptions201:open a socket of a declared family, by an established entity, under the socket grant law (who may open what, to where); the wire act, HOST-MODELLED — no real socket on the host (design/51 §5, N1/N2)s12:object_params6:sockets12:payload_froml3:s6:entitys6:sockets6:familys17:structural_paramsl3:s6:entitys6:sockets6:familys4:cells1:Ss5:mintsl1:s6:sockets6:checksl2:d6:s4:cites13:NET-LAW-GRANTs5:checks13:require_priors5:fields10:account_ids5:params6:entitys6:actions14:CREATE-ACCOUNTs7:messages138:SOCKET-OPEN: the opener was never established — a socket is opened BY somebody, and the somebody must exist on the record (who may open)d5:s4:cites13:NET-LAW-GRANTs5:checks12:value_domains5:params6:familys6:domainl3:s4:inets5:inet6s4:unixs7:messages201:SOCKET-OPEN: this family is not one the socket grant law declares — the declared set is inet, inet6, unix (what may be opened); a family the law does not name is refused, recorded, never a type errors6:paramsd3:s6:entitys8:requireds6:familys8:requireds6:sockets8:requireds9:law_citeds13:NET-LAW-GRANTs4:kinds13:op_definitions4:names11:SOCKET-OPENs4:texts109:operation SOCKET-OPEN: when invoked and its checks pass -> append a SOCKET-OPEN decision citing NET-LAW-GRANTs4:tiers5:owners7:rule_ids14:op:SOCKET-OPENs8:polaritys1:+s9:record_ids7:rec_172d16:s10:provenanced3:s10:could_readl0:s11:asserted_bys10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:sources6:systems10:rule_citeds10:CAP-IS-LAWs11:record_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.603584+00:00s12:content_forms6:inlines15:occurrence_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.603656+00:00s15:submission_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.603652+00:00s16:evidence_summaryns3:seqi173;s4:refsl0:s5:actors10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:actions9:CREATE-OPs6:objects14:op:SOCKET-BINDs6:origind2:s12:subsystem_ids6:kernels8:built_idi0;s6:targetns7:payloadd7:s10:definitiond8:s11:descriptions95:bind a socket the record opened to a local address; the wire act, host-modelled (design/51 §5)s12:object_params6:sockets12:payload_froml2:s6:sockets7:addresss17:structural_paramsl2:s6:sockets7:addresss4:cells1:Ss6:checksl1:d6:s4:cites13:NET-LAW-GRANTs5:checks13:require_priors5:fields6:sockets5:params6:sockets6:actions11:SOCKET-OPENs7:messages121:SOCKET-BIND: no SOCKET-OPEN established this socket — a wire act names a socket the record opened (who may act on what)s6:paramsd2:s6:sockets8:requireds7:addresss8:requireds9:law_citeds13:NET-LAW-GRANTs4:kinds13:op_definitions4:names11:SOCKET-BINDs4:texts109:operation SOCKET-BIND: when invoked and its checks pass -> append a SOCKET-BIND decision citing NET-LAW-GRANTs4:tiers5:owners7:rule_ids14:op:SOCKET-BINDs8:polaritys1:+s9:record_ids7:rec_173d16:s10:provenanced3:s10:could_readl0:s11:asserted_bys10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:sources6:systems10:rule_citeds10:CAP-IS-LAWs11:record_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.606556+00:00s12:content_forms6:inlines15:occurrence_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.606574+00:00s15:submission_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.606571+00:00s16:evidence_summaryns3:seqi174;s4:refsl0:s5:actors10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:actions9:CREATE-OPs6:objects16:op:SOCKET-LISTENs6:origind2:s12:subsystem_ids6:kernels8:built_idi0;s6:targetns7:payloadd7:s10:definitiond8:s11:descriptions89:mark a socket the record opened as listening; the wire act, host-modelled (design/51 §5)s12:object_params6:sockets12:payload_froml1:s6:sockets17:structural_paramsl1:s6:sockets4:cells1:Ss6:checksl1:d6:s4:cites13:NET-LAW-GRANTs5:checks13:require_priors5:fields6:sockets5:params6:sockets6:actions11:SOCKET-OPENs7:messages123:SOCKET-LISTEN: no SOCKET-OPEN established this socket — a wire act names a socket the record opened (who may act on what)s6:paramsd1:s6:sockets8:requireds9:law_citeds13:NET-LAW-GRANTs4:kinds13:op_definitions4:names13:SOCKET-LISTENs4:texts113:operation SOCKET-LISTEN: when invoked and its checks pass -> append a SOCKET-LISTEN decision citing NET-LAW-GRANTs4:tiers5:owners7:rule_ids16:op:SOCKET-LISTENs8:polaritys1:+s9:record_ids7:rec_174d16:s10:provenanced3:s10:could_readl0:s11:asserted_bys10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:sources6:systems10:rule_citeds10:CAP-IS-LAWs11:record_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.609835+00:00s12:content_forms6:inlines15:occurrence_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.610173+00:00s15:submission_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.610165+00:00s16:evidence_summaryns3:seqi175;s4:refsl0:s5:actors10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:actions9:CREATE-OPs6:objects17:op:SOCKET-CONNECTs6:origind2:s12:subsystem_ids6:kernels8:built_idi0;s6:targetns7:payloadd7:s10:definitiond8:s11:descriptions143:connect a socket the record opened to a target; the wire act — the target is recorded, the reach ungated today (host-modelled, design/51 §5)s12:object_params6:sockets12:payload_froml2:s6:sockets6:targets17:structural_paramsl2:s6:sockets6:targets4:cells1:Ss6:checksl1:d6:s4:cites13:NET-LAW-GRANTs5:checks13:require_priors5:fields6:sockets5:params6:sockets6:actions11:SOCKET-OPENs7:messages124:SOCKET-CONNECT: no SOCKET-OPEN established this socket — a wire act names a socket the record opened (who may act on what)s6:paramsd2:s6:sockets8:requireds6:targets8:requireds9:law_citeds13:NET-LAW-GRANTs4:kinds13:op_definitions4:names14:SOCKET-CONNECTs4:texts115:operation SOCKET-CONNECT: when invoked and its checks pass -> append a SOCKET-CONNECT decision citing NET-LAW-GRANTs4:tiers5:owners7:rule_ids17:op:SOCKET-CONNECTs8:polaritys1:+s9:record_ids7:rec_175d16:s10:provenanced3:s10:could_readl0:s11:asserted_bys10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:sources6:systems10:rule_citeds10:CAP-IS-LAWs11:record_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.624457+00:00s12:content_forms6:inlines15:occurrence_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.624506+00:00s15:submission_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.624481+00:00s16:evidence_summaryns3:seqi176;s4:refsl0:s5:actors10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:actions9:CREATE-OPs6:objects16:op:SOCKET-ACCEPTs6:origind2:s12:subsystem_ids6:kernels8:built_idi0;s6:targetns7:payloadd7:s10:definitiond8:s11:descriptions113:accept a peer on a socket the record opened; the wire act — the peer is recorded (host-modelled, design/51 §5)s12:object_params6:sockets12:payload_froml2:s6:sockets4:peers17:structural_paramsl2:s6:sockets4:peers4:cells1:Ss6:checksl1:d6:s4:cites13:NET-LAW-GRANTs5:checks13:require_priors5:fields6:sockets5:params6:sockets6:actions11:SOCKET-OPENs7:messages123:SOCKET-ACCEPT: no SOCKET-OPEN established this socket — a wire act names a socket the record opened (who may act on what)s6:paramsd2:s4:peers8:requireds6:sockets8:requireds9:law_citeds13:NET-LAW-GRANTs4:kinds13:op_definitions4:names13:SOCKET-ACCEPTs4:texts113:operation SOCKET-ACCEPT: when invoked and its checks pass -> append a SOCKET-ACCEPT decision citing NET-LAW-GRANTs4:tiers5:owners7:rule_ids16:op:SOCKET-ACCEPTs8:polaritys1:+s9:record_ids7:rec_176d16:s10:provenanced3:s10:could_readl0:s11:asserted_bys10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:sources6:systems10:rule_citeds10:CAP-IS-LAWs11:record_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.629718+00:00s12:content_forms6:inlines15:occurrence_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.629740+00:00s15:submission_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.629734+00:00s16:evidence_summaryns3:seqi177;s4:refsl0:s5:actors10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:actions9:CREATE-OPs6:objects15:op:SOCKET-CLOSEs6:origind2:s12:subsystem_ids6:kernels8:built_idi0;s6:targetns7:payloadd7:s10:definitiond8:s11:descriptions320:tear down a socket the record opened; the wire act, host-modelled (design/51 §5). Reached by the op directly on the host — the flat syscall-ops map cannot discriminate a socket fd's close from a file fd's, so `close` stays unmapped on the host (:3266 precision 3); EP-48G maps it in-guest where the fd's kind is knowns12:object_params6:sockets12:payload_froml1:s6:sockets17:structural_paramsl1:s6:sockets4:cells1:Ss6:checksl1:d6:s4:cites13:NET-LAW-GRANTs5:checks13:require_priors5:fields6:sockets5:params6:sockets6:actions11:SOCKET-OPENs7:messages122:SOCKET-CLOSE: no SOCKET-OPEN established this socket — a wire act names a socket the record opened (who may act on what)s6:paramsd1:s6:sockets8:requireds9:law_citeds13:NET-LAW-GRANTs4:kinds13:op_definitions4:names12:SOCKET-CLOSEs4:texts111:operation SOCKET-CLOSE: when invoked and its checks pass -> append a SOCKET-CLOSE decision citing NET-LAW-GRANTs4:tiers5:owners7:rule_ids15:op:SOCKET-CLOSEs8:polaritys1:+s9:record_ids7:rec_177d16:s10:provenanced3:s10:could_readl0:s11:asserted_bys10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:sources6:systems10:rule_citeds10:CAP-IS-LAWs11:record_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.634013+00:00s12:content_forms6:inlines15:occurrence_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.634038+00:00s15:submission_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.634032+00:00s16:evidence_summaryns3:seqi178;s4:refsl0:s5:actors10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:actions9:CREATE-OPs6:objects16:op:BORDER-SUBMITs6:origind2:s12:subsystem_ids6:kernels8:built_idi0;s6:targetns7:payloadd7:s10:definitiond9:s11:descriptions462:an outside entity submits a DRAFT through its system-facing channel -- a request the gate decides against the record BEFORE any effect, never executed as the act itself (design/51 N3, the door). A crossing is an opening of the entity's system-facing channel (design/39); the entity is prior-established under CAP-IS-LAW, never a peer-minted token (the API-gateway trap refused, design/51 section 9). The submit row's content hash IS the crossing id (archi :3266)s12:object_params6:entitys12:payload_froml2:s6:entitys5:drafts14:payload_derived2:s12:record_classd1:s3:tpls8:DECISIONs4:kindd1:s3:tpls13:border-submits17:structural_paramsl2:s6:entitys5:drafts4:cells1:Ss6:checksl1:d6:s4:cites10:CAP-IS-LAWs5:checks13:require_priors5:fields10:account_ids5:params6:entitys6:actions14:CREATE-ACCOUNTs7:messages267:BORDER-SUBMIT: the submitter was never established -- a crossing is an opening of somebody's system-facing channel, and the somebody must exist on the record (an entity is its recorded establishment, design/39; never a peer-minted token, the API-gateway trap refused)s6:paramsd2:s5:drafts8:requireds6:entitys8:requireds9:law_citeds17:COMM-LAW-CONTRACTs4:kinds13:op_definitions4:names13:BORDER-SUBMITs4:texts144:operation BORDER-SUBMIT: when invoked and its checks pass -> append a border-submit DECISION (a draft the gate decides) citing COMM-LAW-CONTRACTs4:tiers5:owners7:rule_ids16:op:BORDER-SUBMITs8:polaritys1:+s9:record_ids7:rec_178d16:s10:provenanced3:s10:could_readl0:s11:asserted_bys10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:sources6:systems10:rule_citeds10:CAP-IS-LAWs11:record_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.639906+00:00s12:content_forms6:inlines15:occurrence_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.639924+00:00s15:submission_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.639921+00:00s16:evidence_summaryns3:seqi179;s4:refsl0:s5:actors10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:actions9:CREATE-OPs6:objects15:op:BORDER-REPLYs6:origind2:s12:subsystem_ids6:kernels8:built_idi0;s6:targetns7:payloadd7:s10:definitiond9:s11:descriptions480:the border's REPLY to an allowed crossing -- it carries the crossing id (the submit row's content hash) and a SEAL over exactly what was shown (a REAL Ed25519 signature via the signer where the library is present, REFUSED and never faked when absent -- N10, RW-FAKE-SEAL). The reply binds to its submit by the store's recomputation of the submit's content hash at the gate chokepoint, never by the reply's own claim (the crossing.py correlation discipline, the border's direction)s12:object_params11:crossing_ids12:payload_froml3:s11:crossing_ids5:showns4:seals14:payload_derived2:s12:record_classd1:s3:tpls8:DECISIONs4:kindd1:s3:tpls12:border-replys17:structural_paramsl3:s11:crossing_ids5:showns4:seals4:cells1:Ss6:checksl0:s6:paramsd3:s11:crossing_ids8:requireds4:seals8:requireds5:showns8:requireds9:law_citeds17:COMM-LAW-CONTRACTs4:kinds13:op_definitions4:names12:BORDER-REPLYs4:texts232:operation BORDER-REPLY: when invoked -> append a border-reply DECISION carrying the crossing id and the seal over exactly what was shown, citing COMM-LAW-CONTRACT (the binding to its submit is the gate chokepoint's, not a handler's)s4:tiers5:owners7:rule_ids15:op:BORDER-REPLYs8:polaritys1:+s9:record_ids7:rec_179d16:s10:provenanced3:s10:could_readl0:s11:asserted_bys10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:sources6:systems10:rule_citeds10:CAP-IS-LAWs11:record_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.644813+00:00s12:content_forms6:inlines15:occurrence_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.644832+00:00s15:submission_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.644827+00:00s16:evidence_summaryns3:seqi180;s4:refsl0:s5:actors10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:actions9:CREATE-OPs6:objects17:op:BORDER-REFUSALs6:origind2:s12:subsystem_ids6:kernels8:built_idi0;s6:targetns7:payloadd7:s10:definitiond9:s11:descriptions384:the border's REFUSAL of a crossing, surfaced through the system's own WINDOW: the record carries the reason (readable by the human through the window) and names the refused ENTITY -- whose own system-facing channel this refusal never writes to (design/51 N3: a refusal reaches the human through the window, never through the refused party; the system is not the courier of the reason)s12:object_params11:crossing_ids12:payload_froml3:s6:entitys11:crossing_ids6:reasons14:payload_derived2:s12:record_classd1:s3:tpls8:DECISIONs4:kindd1:s3:tpls14:border-refusals17:structural_paramsl3:s6:entitys11:crossing_ids6:reasons4:cells1:Ss6:checksl0:s6:paramsd3:s11:crossing_ids8:requireds6:entitys8:requireds6:reasons8:requireds9:law_citeds17:COMM-LAW-CONTRACTs4:kinds13:op_definitions4:names14:BORDER-REFUSALs4:texts170:operation BORDER-REFUSAL: when invoked -> append a border-refusal DECISION carrying the reason (shown through the window) and the refused entity, citing COMM-LAW-CONTRACTs4:tiers5:owners7:rule_ids17:op:BORDER-REFUSALs8:polaritys1:+s9:record_ids7:rec_180d16:s10:provenanced3:s10:could_readl0:s11:asserted_bys10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:sources6:systems10:rule_citeds10:CAP-IS-LAWs11:record_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.650442+00:00s12:content_forms6:inlines15:occurrence_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.650467+00:00s15:submission_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.650461+00:00s16:evidence_summaryns3:seqi181;s4:refsl0:s5:actors10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:actions9:CREATE-OPs6:objects10:op:RECEIPTs6:origind2:s12:subsystem_ids6:kernels8:built_idi0;s6:targetns7:payloadd7:s10:definitiond10:s11:descriptions1762:the RECEIVER's own record of a crossing (design/51 N9, EP-49D). A row sent from body A is received at body B as INPUT through B's border; B appends THIS receipt to ITS OWN record -- A never writes B's record and B never A's (one pen per record, D08.30 / the single-writer lock, store.py). The receipt cites the received row's CONTENT HASH (content_hash -- border.content_id, the crossing id that excludes record_time so two bodies recording one crossing at different times derive the SAME hash, D08.40); the FROM-BODY (from_body -- the sender's bound SYSTEM PUBLIC KEY together with its genesis hash, a body's NAME, D08.42 -- a copied seed is a FORK the chain exposes, never a clash); the sender's SIGNATURE (from_sig -- verified under from_body's key, real-or-refused N10); the UNDER-RULE (under_rule); and the REVEALED-SET (revealed_set -- the selective-disclosure leaf set when a tree was presented, D08.48, empty otherwise). Identity is what CROSSED, never trust in the peer's own record (N4's cap; the API-gateway trap refused, design/51 section 9). One row, ONE receipt: a second receipt for the same content_hash is refused at the gate chokepoint (idempotent). C6 P8 (SPIKE-3 N2, SPIKE-5, B15): RECEIPT gains THREE OPTIONAL structural fields — the CHECKS MAP (who / body / memory_sane, each pass|fail), the DISCLOSURE_LEVEL (HASHES-ONLY | SHELLS | FULL), and the ADDRESS_FORM (row | segment: a segment receipt cites the SEGMENT hash in the content_hash slot and is verified by blob-rehash, receipt_binds_segment, not by content_id). admitted_level is DERIVED AT READ from the checks map + disclosure_level, NEVER stored (I10). A bare row receipt omits all three and is byte-unchanged from before P8 apart from three null fields the honest record carriess11:param_kindsd2:s12:address_forms4:texts16:disclosure_levels4:texts12:object_params12:content_hashs12:payload_froml8:s12:content_hashs9:from_bodys8:from_sigs10:under_rules12:revealed_sets6:checkss16:disclosure_levels12:address_forms14:payload_derived2:s12:record_classd1:s3:tpls8:DECISIONs4:kindd1:s3:tpls7:receipts17:structural_paramsl8:s12:content_hashs9:from_bodys8:from_sigs10:under_rules12:revealed_sets6:checkss16:disclosure_levels12:address_forms4:cells1:Ss6:checksl0:s6:paramsd8:s10:under_rules8:requireds12:address_forms8:optionals12:content_hashs8:requireds12:revealed_sets8:requireds16:disclosure_levels8:optionals6:checkss8:optionals8:from_sigs8:requireds9:from_bodys8:requireds9:law_citeds17:COMM-LAW-CONTRACTs4:kinds13:op_definitions4:names7:RECEIPTs4:texts395:operation RECEIPT: when invoked -> append a receipt DECISION (the receiver's own record of a crossing) carrying the received row's content hash, the from-body (the sender's bound system public key + genesis hash), the sender's signature, the under-rule and the revealed-set, citing COMM-LAW-CONTRACT (the binding of exactly one receipt per received row is the gate chokepoint's, not a handler's)s4:tiers5:owners7:rule_ids10:op:RECEIPTs8:polaritys1:+s9:record_ids7:rec_181d16:s10:provenanced3:s10:could_readl0:s11:asserted_bys10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:sources6:systems10:rule_citeds10:CAP-IS-LAWs11:record_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.655958+00:00s12:content_forms6:inlines15:occurrence_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.656003+00:00s15:submission_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.655976+00:00s16:evidence_summaryns3:seqi182;s4:refsl0:s5:actors10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:actions9:CREATE-OPs6:objects15:op:VIEW-SERVICEs6:origind2:s12:subsystem_ids6:kernels8:built_idi0;s6:targetns7:payloadd7:s10:definitiond10:s11:descriptions1322:the SERVICING of a mandated view is a record (design/51 N6, EP-50). A view DEFINITION is already a record (CREATE-VIEW, kind view_definition -- views.py); what was missing is a SERVICING signal for a MASTER/query view (no move_to), which in v1 had NO recorded per-run signal at all (paper_tigers could clear a mandated view only by a non-empty delivery queue -- delivery was the only witness). A VIEW-SERVICE DECISION is appended each time a mandated view is serviced, carrying WHO (servicer -- STAMPED from the acting actor, the engine's fact never the caller's claim, so a servicing cannot be attributed to another), WHEN (the seq of this record) and OVER-WHICH-HEAD (head_seq -- the store head the servicer serviced over). paper_tigers reads VIEW-SERVICE, so a mandated view NEVER serviced is a FOLD and not an inference (N6); DELIVERY is RETAINED as a SECOND WITNESS (design/51 section 6 item 4). Cites ROOT-NEG-6 -- the SAME founded law CREATE-VIEW cites (a view definition is law, contradiction-gated; no new law is minted, EP-50 architect precision board :3377). The fold FUNCTIONS stay CODE (mechanism, S-plane, air rider 1); this op records the servicing DECISION, never a fold's definition. checks: [] -- servicing is a recorded act, gated by no new check kind (OP_CHECKS unchanged; this mints an OP, not a KIND)s11:stamp_actorl1:s8:servicers12:payload_froml2:s9:view_names8:head_seqs13:object_derived1:s3:tpls16:view:{view_name}s14:payload_derived2:s12:record_classd1:s3:tpls8:DECISIONs4:kindd1:s3:tpls12:view_services17:structural_paramsl2:s9:view_names8:head_seqs4:cells1:Ss6:checksl0:s6:paramsd2:s8:head_seqs8:requireds9:view_names8:requireds9:law_citeds10:ROOT-NEG-6s4:kinds13:op_definitions4:names12:VIEW-SERVICEs4:texts364:operation VIEW-SERVICE: when invoked -> append a view_service DECISION recording that a mandated view was serviced, carrying the view name, the head seq serviced over, and the servicer (stamped from the acting actor), citing ROOT-NEG-6 (the same founded law CREATE-VIEW cites; a mandated view never serviced becomes a fold, not an inference -- design/51 N6, EP-50)s4:tiers5:owners7:rule_ids15:op:VIEW-SERVICEs8:polaritys1:+s9:record_ids7:rec_182d16:s10:provenanced3:s10:could_readl0:s11:asserted_bys10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:sources6:systems10:rule_citeds10:CAP-IS-LAWs11:record_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.660898+00:00s12:content_forms6:inlines15:occurrence_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.660921+00:00s15:submission_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.660916+00:00s16:evidence_summaryns3:seqi183;s4:refsl0:s5:actors10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:actions9:CREATE-OPs6:objects18:op:FILTER-DECISIONs6:origind2:s12:subsystem_ids6:kernels8:built_idi0;s6:targetns7:payloadd7:s10:definitiond8:s11:descriptions830:the firewall's filtering decision as a record (design/51 N8, EP-52). A connection is ADMITTED or REFUSED by an established entity, CITING a FILTER-RULE (a CREATE-RULE of law class NET-LAW-FILTER) over a socket the record OPENED (EP-48) — the deciding rule recorded so 'which rule dropped this' is a fold (src/subsystems/filter.py), never an inference. The record DECIDES; the guest kernel's netfilter DROPS — the seam is NAMED (guest-netfilter) and the host record never claims the drop (DIGEST-C4 §6). HOST-MODELLED: no real packet is dropped by the host; the guest-real drop is proven guest-only under the pinned kernel (EP-00 rule 9). A routing/name FACT the world hands us is INPUT (ANSWER-RETURNED), never this decision (design/44 §2). The filter READS and decides OVER the socket table; it never rewrites a socket act.s12:object_params10:connections12:payload_froml5:s6:entitys10:connections4:rules8:decisions4:seams17:structural_paramsl5:s6:entitys10:connections4:rules8:decisions4:seams4:cells1:Ss6:checksl5:d6:s4:cites14:NET-LAW-FILTERs5:checks13:require_priors5:fields10:account_ids5:params6:entitys6:actions14:CREATE-ACCOUNTs7:messages152:FILTER-DECISION: the decider was never established — a filtering decision is made BY somebody, and the somebody must exist on the record (who decides)d6:s4:cites14:NET-LAW-FILTERs5:checks13:require_priors5:fields6:sockets5:params10:connections6:actions11:SOCKET-OPENs7:messages195:FILTER-DECISION: no SOCKET-OPEN established this connection — the filter decides OVER a socket the record opened (EP-48), never a string the caller supplies, and never by rewriting a socket actd6:s4:cites14:NET-LAW-FILTERs5:checks13:require_priors5:fields7:rule_ids5:params4:rules6:actions11:CREATE-RULEs7:messages194:FILTER-DECISION: the cited FILTER-RULE is not in the record — the firewall is rules IN the record, and a decision citing NO law is refused, recorded, never taken from a table beside the recordd5:s4:cites14:NET-LAW-FILTERs5:checks12:value_domains5:params8:decisions6:domainl2:s5:admits6:refuses7:messages139:FILTER-DECISION: a filtering decision is ADMIT or REFUSE — a value this law does not name is refused, recorded, never a free-text verdictd5:s4:cites14:NET-LAW-FILTERs5:checks12:value_domains5:params4:seams6:domainl1:s15:guest-netfilters7:messages209:FILTER-DECISION: the enforcement seam is NAMED and is the GUEST kernel's netfilter — the record decides and names the seam; a seam the law does not name (e.g. the host claiming the drop) is refused, recordeds6:paramsd5:s10:connections8:requireds4:rules8:requireds4:seams8:requireds6:entitys8:requireds8:decisions8:requireds9:law_citeds14:NET-LAW-FILTERs4:kinds13:op_definitions4:names15:FILTER-DECISIONs4:texts259:operation FILTER-DECISION: when invoked and its checks pass -> append a FILTER-DECISION decision citing NET-LAW-FILTER — a connection admitted or refused, the deciding FILTER-RULE recorded, the guest-netfilter seam named; the record decides, netfilter dropss4:tiers5:owners7:rule_ids18:op:FILTER-DECISIONs8:polaritys1:+s9:record_ids7:rec_183d16:s10:provenanced3:s10:could_readl0:s11:asserted_bys10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:sources6:systems10:rule_citeds10:CAP-IS-LAWs11:record_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.666481+00:00s12:content_forms6:inlines15:occurrence_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.666530+00:00s15:submission_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.666525+00:00s16:evidence_summaryns3:seqi184;s4:refsl0:s5:actors10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:actions9:CREATE-OPs6:objects14:op:SUBMIT-VIEWs6:origind2:s12:subsystem_ids6:kernels8:built_idi0;s6:targetns7:payloadd7:s10:definitiond9:s11:descriptions1158:a non-system actor -- a person, the owner, a program -- SUBMITS a view add/change proposal (the proposal-and-ban path, design/56 §10 H cut 2). The gate VERIFIES the submitter's view-tier authority (an established account or the genesis anchor holds standing; a master/owner-tier view requires the root chain-end) and the change's lawfulness (a well-formed view definition), then EXECUTES it as the SYSTEM (a CREATE-VIEW by the literal SYSTEM recorder whose payload cites this submit row by reference -- the border :1488 recomputation shape) or BANS it (a refusal recorded, the reason named). Its admission is VIEW-TIER AUTHORITY, not account establishment: it carries NO CREATE-ACCOUNT require_prior, so the owner (a genesis boot anchor) submits and is not refused 'never established' -- and BORDER-SUBMIT's establishment law is untouched (a distinct op, never a weakening of the border; not a second crossing -- a foreign body still travels BORDER-SUBMIT, and an unestablished non-anchor submitter is refused by name). Records a structured proposal and interprets no content -> cell S (B4). The submit row's content hash IS the id the executed write cites.s12:payload_froml6:s4:names4:whens4:thens4:binds6:derives7:refreshs13:object_derived1:s3:tpls11:view:{name}s14:payload_derived2:s12:record_classd1:s3:tpls8:DECISIONs4:kindd1:s3:tpls11:view_submits17:structural_paramsl6:s4:names4:whens4:thens4:binds6:derives7:refreshs4:cells1:Ss6:checksl0:s6:paramsd6:s4:binds8:optionals4:names8:requireds4:thens8:optionals4:whens8:optionals6:derives8:optionals7:refreshs8:optionals9:law_citeds17:VIEW-SUBMIT-ROUTEs4:kinds13:op_definitions4:names11:SUBMIT-VIEWs4:texts243:operation SUBMIT-VIEW: when invoked and the gate's submit-verify-execute decision passes -> append a view_submit DECISION (a proposal the SYSTEM then executes as a CREATE-VIEW citing this submit by reference, or bans), citing VIEW-SUBMIT-ROUTEs4:tiers5:owners7:rule_ids14:op:SUBMIT-VIEWs8:polaritys1:+s9:record_ids7:rec_184d16:s10:provenanced3:s10:could_readl0:s11:asserted_bys10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:sources6:systems10:rule_citeds10:CAP-IS-LAWs11:record_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.671525+00:00s12:content_forms6:inlines15:occurrence_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.671548+00:00s15:submission_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.671543+00:00s16:evidence_summaryns3:seqi185;s4:refsl0:s5:actors10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:actions9:CREATE-OPs6:objects14:op:RETIRE-RULEs6:origind2:s12:subsystem_ids6:kernels8:built_idi0;s6:targetns7:payloadd7:s10:definitiond8:s11:descriptions1593:END A RULE as its own recorded act (design/56 §3 B8; C8 P7). Before this operation gov-os had no act that ends a rule: operations retire by RETIRE-OP, while a rule was only ever overwritten by a later row of the same id. RETIRE-RULE appends a retirement row carrying the rule's id and the scope it cites; the rule fold (views.active_rules) honours it as the rule's end-marker, so a retired rule binds nothing after its retirement row (an act it refused before the row is still refused as of that time; the same act after the row proceeds), while its rows stay on the record in the OLD band (append-only: nothing rewritten, nothing deleted). WHO: SYSTEM, the root chain-end, or a holder of the amendment authority the rule names -- the gate asks its own authority question of the counterfactual amendment, a CREATE-RULE on this rule id in the rule's own scope (a law carries its binding scope, J5; a rule is info of kind law, design/31 J3), and the retire must cite exactly that scope. WHAT: a live rule whose only fold is the rule view -- a record with a lifecycle fold of its own (an operation's definition, a view, an obligation, a seam act-kind row) is refused, so the record never carries a retirement its own fold would not honour. The constitutional tier refuses retirement through the system for every actor, the root and SYSTEM included (CONST-SELF-PROTECT, riding the constitution guard's rule branch); only the founding's own actor ends one, at genesis above the gate. Recognised by its act, as RETIRE-OP is. Records a structured retirement and interprets no content -> cell S (B4).s12:object_params7:rule_ids12:payload_froml2:s7:rule_ids5:scopes17:structural_paramsl2:s7:rule_ids5:scopes4:cells1:Ss6:checksl0:s6:paramsd2:s5:scopes8:requireds7:rule_ids8:requireds9:law_citeds10:CAP-IS-LAWs4:kinds13:op_definitions4:names11:RETIRE-RULEs4:texts187:operation RETIRE-RULE: when invoked and the gate's retirement decision passes -> append a retirement row the rule fold honours (the retired rule binds nothing after it), citing CAP-IS-LAWs4:tiers5:owners7:rule_ids14:op:RETIRE-RULEs8:polaritys1:+s9:record_ids7:rec_185d16:s10:provenanced3:s10:could_readl0:s11:asserted_bys10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:sources6:systems10:rule_citeds10:CAP-IS-LAWs11:record_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.676828+00:00s12:content_forms6:inlines15:occurrence_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.676872+00:00s15:submission_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.676864+00:00s16:evidence_summaryns3:seqi186;s4:refsl0:s5:actors10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:actions9:CREATE-OPs6:objects15:op:DECIDE-DRAFTs6:origind2:s12:subsystem_ids6:kernels8:built_idi0;s6:targetns7:payloadd7:s10:definitiond8:s11:descriptions1416:DECIDE A DRAFT as its own recorded act (design/56 §3 B9; design/59 Part 1; C8 P8). A draft is information an actor created that awaits a decision; before this operation its decision was not its own act (the ontology census's second gap, design/59). DECIDE-DRAFT appends ONE decision row: actor the deciding actor, object the draft (record:{draft_seq}, the record-coordinate form OVERTURN uses for an act about a prior record), result accepted or refused. The draft's STATUS is DERIVED from the decision rows on read (views.draft_status: awaiting with none, decided with one) and never stored on the draft; the draft's own row is untouched. ONE DECISION PER DRAFT, and a decided draft STAYS decided: a second DECIDE-DRAFT on the same draft is refused by name (fold_threshold, decisions_on_draft < 1, keyed by draft_seq); there is no amend arm -- after a refusal the lawful path is a NEW draft, and a wrong decision is reached by the standing overturn machinery, never by deciding the same draft again. THE DECISION NAMES A REAL DRAFT: the gate refuses a draft_seq that names no record (never written, or not yet written), a border crossing (decided by the border's own sealed path, BORDER-REPLY / BORDER-REFUSAL -- the two decide different draft classes, COEXIST), or a record that is not an information item (kernel.gate._draft_decision_step). Records a structured decision and interprets no content -> cell S (B4).s12:payload_froml2:s9:draft_seqs6:results13:object_derived1:s3:tpls18:record:{draft_seq}s17:structural_paramsl2:s9:draft_seqs6:results4:cells1:Ss6:checksl2:d5:s4:cites10:CAP-IS-LAWs5:checks12:value_domains5:params6:results6:domainl2:s8:accepteds7:refuseds7:messages152:DECIDE-DRAFT: a draft's decision is accepted or refused (design/56 B9) -- a value this law does not name is refused, recorded, never a free-text verdictd8:s10:add_actions12:DECIDE-DRAFTs4:cites10:CAP-IS-LAWs5:checks14:fold_thresholds8:operators1:<s9:fold_names18:decisions_on_drafts9:key_fields9:draft_seqs9:key_params9:draft_seqs9:thresholdi1;s6:paramsd2:s6:results8:requireds9:draft_seqs8:requireds9:law_citeds10:CAP-IS-LAWs4:kinds13:op_definitions4:names12:DECIDE-DRAFTs4:texts322:operation DECIDE-DRAFT: when invoked, the result is accepted or refused, the draft carries no decision yet, and the gate finds the draft_seq names a real information item (never a border crossing) -> append the decision row (the draft's status is derived from it, never stored), citing CAP-IS-LAW; otherwise refuse by names4:tiers5:owners7:rule_ids15:op:DECIDE-DRAFTs8:polaritys1:+s9:record_ids7:rec_186d16:s10:provenanced3:s10:could_readl0:s11:asserted_bys10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:sources6:systems10:rule_citeds10:ROOT-NEG-6s11:record_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.681801+00:00s12:content_forms6:inlines15:occurrence_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.681817+00:00s15:submission_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.681814+00:00s16:evidence_summaryns3:seqi187;s4:refsl0:s5:actors10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:actions11:CREATE-VIEWs6:objects16:view:rule-masters6:origind2:s12:subsystem_ids6:kernels8:built_idi0;s6:targetns7:payloadd7:s4:binds12:active_ruless4:kinds15:view_definitions4:names11:rule-masters4:texts57:master view rule-master: derived by the active_rules folds4:tiers5:owners7:rule_ids16:view:rule-masters8:polaritys1:+s9:record_ids7:rec_187d16:s10:provenanced3:s10:could_readl0:s11:asserted_bys10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:sources6:systems10:rule_citeds10:ROOT-NEG-6s11:record_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.683952+00:00s12:content_forms6:inlines15:occurrence_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.683978+00:00s15:submission_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.683972+00:00s16:evidence_summaryns3:seqi188;s4:refsl0:s5:actors10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:actions11:CREATE-VIEWs6:objects17:view:actor-masters6:origind2:s12:subsystem_ids6:kernels8:built_idi0;s6:targetns7:payloadd7:s4:binds6:actorss4:kinds15:view_definitions4:names12:actor-masters4:texts52:master view actor-master: derived by the actors folds4:tiers5:owners7:rule_ids17:view:actor-masters8:polaritys1:+s9:record_ids7:rec_188d16:s10:provenanced3:s10:could_readl0:s11:asserted_bys10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:sources6:systems10:rule_citeds10:ROOT-NEG-6s11:record_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.686396+00:00s12:content_forms6:inlines15:occurrence_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.686418+00:00s15:submission_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.686412+00:00s16:evidence_summaryns3:seqi189;s4:refsl0:s5:actors10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:actions11:CREATE-VIEWs6:objects20:view:resource-masters6:origind2:s12:subsystem_ids6:kernels8:built_idi0;s6:targetns7:payloadd7:s4:binds9:resourcess4:kinds15:view_definitions4:names15:resource-masters4:texts58:master view resource-master: derived by the resources folds4:tiers5:owners7:rule_ids20:view:resource-masters8:polaritys1:+s9:record_ids7:rec_189d16:s10:provenanced3:s10:could_readl0:s11:asserted_bys10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:sources6:systems10:rule_citeds10:ROOT-NEG-6s11:record_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.688760+00:00s12:content_forms6:inlines15:occurrence_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.688788+00:00s15:submission_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.688773+00:00s16:evidence_summaryns3:seqi190;s4:refsl0:s5:actors10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:actions11:CREATE-VIEWs6:objects22:view:permission-masters6:origind2:s12:subsystem_ids6:kernels8:built_idi0;s6:targetns7:payloadd7:s4:binds11:permissionss4:kinds15:view_definitions4:names17:permission-masters4:texts62:master view permission-master: derived by the permissions folds4:tiers5:owners7:rule_ids22:view:permission-masters8:polaritys1:+s9:record_ids7:rec_190d16:s10:provenanced3:s10:could_readl0:s11:asserted_bys10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:sources6:systems10:rule_citeds10:ROOT-NEG-6s11:record_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.690806+00:00s12:content_forms6:inlines15:occurrence_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.690828+00:00s15:submission_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.690822+00:00s16:evidence_summaryns3:seqi191;s4:refsl0:s5:actors10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:actions11:CREATE-VIEWs6:objects24:view:relationship-masters6:origind2:s12:subsystem_ids6:kernels8:built_idi0;s6:targetns7:payloadd7:s4:binds13:relationshipss4:kinds15:view_definitions4:names19:relationship-masters4:texts66:master view relationship-master: derived by the relationships folds4:tiers5:owners7:rule_ids24:view:relationship-masters8:polaritys1:+s9:record_ids7:rec_191d16:s10:provenanced3:s10:could_readl0:s11:asserted_bys10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:sources6:systems10:rule_citeds10:ROOT-NEG-6s11:record_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.692731+00:00s12:content_forms6:inlines15:occurrence_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.692748+00:00s15:submission_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.692742+00:00s16:evidence_summaryns3:seqi192;s4:refsl0:s5:actors10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:actions11:CREATE-VIEWs6:objects16:view:op-registrys6:origind2:s12:subsystem_ids6:kernels8:built_idi0;s6:targetns7:payloadd7:s4:binds14:op_definitionss4:kinds15:view_definitions4:names11:op-registrys4:texts59:master view op-registry: derived by the op_definitions folds4:tiers5:owners7:rule_ids16:view:op-registrys8:polaritys1:+s9:record_ids7:rec_192d16:s10:provenanced3:s10:could_readl0:s11:asserted_bys10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:sources6:systems10:rule_citeds10:ROOT-NEG-6s11:record_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.694418+00:00s12:content_forms6:inlines15:occurrence_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.694441+00:00s15:submission_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.694437+00:00s16:evidence_summaryns3:seqi193;s4:refsl0:s5:actors10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:actions11:CREATE-VIEWs6:objects18:view:view-registrys6:origind2:s12:subsystem_ids6:kernels8:built_idi0;s6:targetns7:payloadd7:s4:binds16:view_definitionss4:kinds15:view_definitions4:names13:view-registrys4:texts63:master view view-registry: derived by the view_definitions folds4:tiers5:owners7:rule_ids18:view:view-registrys8:polaritys1:+s9:record_ids7:rec_193d16:s10:provenanced3:s10:could_readl0:s11:asserted_bys10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:sources6:systems10:rule_citeds8:BOOT-INTs11:record_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.705222+00:00s12:content_forms6:inlines15:occurrence_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.705294+00:00s15:submission_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.705287+00:00s16:evidence_summaryns3:seqi194;s4:refsl0:s5:actors10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:actions11:CREATE-INFOs6:objects18:pack:actor-classess6:origind2:s12:subsystem_ids6:kernels8:built_idi0;s6:targetns7:payloadd4:s4:kinds13:category_packs4:names13:actor-classess4:texts1427:C6 P8 DECLARATIONS 1 & 2 (B16 ACTOR CLASSES AS BANDS; K12 the field's domain closes). The actor CLASSES are labels over TWO declared CAPABILITIES — may be the arm of a STRUCTURED rule (structured-arm), may be the arm of an UNSTRUCTURED rule (unstructured-arm). HUMAN holds BOTH; an AI holds the UNSTRUCTURED arm ONLY (an AI is never the arm of a pure-structured rule); a PROGRAM holds the STRUCTURED arm ONLY (a program is never the arm of a rule with judgment). The cut bounds WHO EXECUTES a rule, never who may ask (B16). The class field's DOMAIN CLOSES to exactly these three (K12, D08.50's vocabulary rule): a class NOT in this list is not a valid band, so the band computed at read refuses it (a class not in the list cannot be validly written/classified). This is founding DATA (a category_pack), so re-cutting the classes is an AMEND-PACK, never a code change; the required capability for any task is READ OFF ITS CELL against this map (the arm of an unstructured rule if any side has judgment, else the arm of a structured rule), so the pairing needs no table beyond these two capabilities. C8-ACTOR-CLASSES-FROZEN (archi :5431/:5441): the capability_vocabulary and capabilities keys that once rode THIS row moved to their own row, pack:class-ceilings, directly after this one; this row keeps its levels and this text only, and is now itself frozen (PLACE-LAW-FROZEN-LISTS) — the ceilings that moved off it are not.s6:levelsl3:s5:humans2:ais7:programs9:record_ids7:rec_194d16:s10:provenanced3:s10:could_readl0:s11:asserted_bys10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:sources6:systems10:rule_citeds8:BOOT-INTs11:record_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.708045+00:00s12:content_forms6:inlines15:occurrence_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.708064+00:00s15:submission_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.708060+00:00s16:evidence_summaryns3:seqi195;s4:refsl0:s5:actors10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:actions11:CREATE-INFOs6:objects19:pack:class-ceilingss6:origind2:s12:subsystem_ids6:kernels8:built_idi0;s6:targetns7:payloadd5:s12:capabilitiesd3:s2:ail1:s16:unstructured-arms5:humanl2:s14:structured-arms16:unstructured-arms7:programl1:s14:structured-arms4:kinds13:category_packs4:names14:class-ceilingss4:texts1873:C8-ACTOR-CLASSES-FROZEN (archi :5431 (1) "pack:actor-classes is OWED ITS FREEZE", :5441 (2) the re-cut, "THE CEILINGS DO NOT FREEZE WITH THE WORDS ... the owner's registered sentence covers the words alone ... levels freeze as your plan does it; the capabilities move to their own founded home, owner-tier changeable"). THE CLASS CEILINGS, THEIR OWN ROW — moved byte-for-byte off pack:actor-classes (the row directly before this one), which now carries only its levels and its own text. `levels` here is the moved capability_vocabulary (structured-arm, unstructured-arm); `capabilities` is the moved {class: (arms...)} map, unchanged in content and read by the SAME two readers as before (views._class_capabilities and its oracle, gate._capabilities_flip_seq), re-pointed to this row's name so `class_capabilities()` returns the identical map and the flip sits at this row's seq — the row right after actor-classes, so the flip's POSITION relative to every gated act is unchanged. No class word (human, ai, program) is written here; the classes appear only as this map's keys, exactly as the familiar-names regions never re-write a class word (:5220). THIS ROW IS NOT FROZEN — PLACE-LAW-FROZEN-LISTS lists actor-classes (the words), never class-ceilings: an owner AMEND-PACK of this pack's levels is admitted as an ordinary levels-only pack write, and its capabilities map carries forward unchanged (the memoised fold's own comment: a levels-only amend carries no capabilities, so the last valid map persists). NO RUNTIME PATH CHANGES THE CEILINGS TODAY — this unit neither adds nor removes an owner change path for the capabilities map itself; the owner's eventual change path is NAMED, not built (archi :5441): a ceiling is conduct law whose home is rule form, so a capabilities change rides the whole rule-change law when it is authored, never a bare pack write.s6:levelsl2:s14:structured-arms16:unstructured-arms9:record_ids7:rec_195d16:s10:provenanced3:s10:could_readl0:s11:asserted_bys10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:sources6:systems10:rule_citeds8:BOOT-INTs11:record_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.710633+00:00s12:content_forms6:inlines15:occurrence_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.710650+00:00s15:submission_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.710647+00:00s16:evidence_summaryns3:seqi196;s4:refsl0:s5:actors10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:actions11:CREATE-RULEs6:objects8:CELL-LAWs6:origind2:s12:subsystem_ids6:kernels8:built_idi0;s6:targetns7:payloadd5:s11:enforced_bys1215:kernel.opdefs.validate_definition_shape._require_wellformed_cell (a declared cell must be one of S | U | U{s} | S{u}, at all THREE doors; inert on absence) AND founding.install._validate's cell-presence check, engaged when CELL-LAW is live (read from the pack's own rule records, the wire-at-birth idiom): every op the founding declares must carry a cell or the WHOLE founding is refused. The (actor class, task cell) PAIRING and the required-capability read are kernel.views (class_band, required_capability, pair, pairing_census) reading the actor-classes founding data; ENFORCEMENT OF THE PAIRING IS LIVE AT THE GATE (P8b, board :3731; supersedes the earlier HELD state of archi precision 2, board :3688): every place the actor class is paired with a cell reads kernel.views.act_cell, the one act-cell reader (C8-P13) — kernel.gate._pairing_step (the write chokepoint refusal), kernel.gate._incarnation_step's step 7 (the class ceiling at a loaded actor's act), kernel.views.pairing_census (the report over the whole record, published with its world) and kernel.views._class_admits (the load-act view and the installation list). No new check kind; the class is the existing ceiling machinery's computed shrink.s11:enforcements4:lives4:texts1868:C6 P8 DECLARATION 3 (L28 THE CELL). Every task is one actor, one input, one transformation, one output, in EXACTLY ONE CELL — S (structured both sides), U (judgment both sides), U{s} (judgment over a structured input), or S{u} (structured over a judgment input). The cell is a DECLARATION per operation (and per station), FOUNDING DATA, NEVER derived from the shapes of the op's fields: a program that inferred a cell from field shapes would be a program holding judgment about where judgment sits, which this law forbids. Every operation carries a declared cell or its definition is REFUSED at the founding door (never defaulted to S). The REQUIRED CAPABILITY is read off the cell (actor-classes): the arm of an UNSTRUCTURED rule if ANY side has judgment (a cell other than S), else the arm of a STRUCTURED rule. THE (ACTOR CLASS, TASK CELL) PAIRING runs through the EXISTING ceiling machinery — a PROGRAM is refused at any cell with judgment, an AI at a pure-S cell, a HUMAN holds any — and adds NO new check kind (a class is a computed ceiling that only shrinks, B18/I21). A declared-S operation must REPLAY TO IDENTITY or satisfy a predicate, or its declaration is a FINDING; a declared-judgment operation is validated to its envelope's schema and NEVER SCORED by the machine. The recorder's own SYSTEM mechanics (form-fill, validate, route) are OUTSIDE the pairing — the cell names the JUDGE's step, and the door checks the acting actor. ENFORCEMENT OF THE PAIRING IS HELD: a DRY-RUN CENSUS over the WHOLE RECORD reports every past act the pairing WOULD have refused, published WITH ITS WORLD (the founding version, the as-of head), and enforcement is a STOP until that census is read — a constitution is not turned on over its own history silently (C6 measures only, L25; the stop in L28). admitted_level and the band are DERIVED AT READ, never stored.s5:scopes10:space:roots7:rule_ids8:CELL-LAWs9:record_ids7:rec_196d16:s10:provenanced3:s10:could_readl0:s11:asserted_bys10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:sources6:systems10:rule_citeds8:BOOT-INTs11:record_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.715982+00:00s12:content_forms6:inlines15:occurrence_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.716020+00:00s15:submission_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.715997+00:00s16:evidence_summaryns3:seqi197;s4:refsl0:s5:actors10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:actions5:GRANTs6:objects23:grant:founding-opennesss6:origind2:s12:subsystem_ids6:kernels8:built_idi0;s6:targetns7:payloadd8:s11:enforcements5:inerts4:infos1:*s4:kinds5:grants4:texts214:the mother space's founding openness recorded as explicit law: today's open world as a grant anyone can read and later narrow space by space (design/31 EP-17 transition policy). It enforces nothing at the founding.s5:spaces10:space:roots7:actionss1:*s7:grantees1:*s8:polaritys1:+s9:record_ids7:rec_197d16:s10:provenanced3:s10:could_readl0:s11:asserted_bys10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:sources6:systems10:rule_citeds10:ROOT-NEG-6s11:record_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.718055+00:00s12:content_forms6:inlines15:occurrence_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.718071+00:00s15:submission_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.718068+00:00s16:evidence_summaryns3:seqi198;s4:refsl0:s5:actors10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:actions11:CREATE-VIEWs6:objects8:view:1.1s6:origind2:s12:subsystem_ids6:kernels8:built_idi0;s6:targetns7:payloadd9:s4:binds18:rule_changing_actss4:kinds15:view_definitions4:names3:1.1s4: