:00s15:submission_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.817756+00:00s16:evidence_summaryns3:seqi233;s4:refsl0:s5:actors10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:actions11:CREATE-RULEs6:objects15:REQUIRED-STAMPSs6:origind2:s12:subsystem_ids6:kernels8:built_idi0;s6:targetns7:payloadd4:s10:policy_keys15:required-stampss4:texts999:REQUIRED-STAMPS (design/25 v2.4 rulings 14/15 and 17b, board :3869; design/53 B10): a POLICY rule mapping a CLASS OF ACT (keyed by its action) to the master-view stamps that class must carry before the gate accepts it. The gate step reads this policy and refuses an act of a stamped class missing a required stamp; an unstamped class (no entry) passes untouched. EMPTY {} at the founding, so no production act is a stamped class until the climb pipeline that populates the stamps is minted (VT-6a) — day one every act passes untouched. The stamps themselves are a GATE-ADDED envelope field of the PROVENANCE CLASS in code, not declared here and in no operation definition: written by the gate inside `provenance`, excluded from the invoker's signed content and the store's countersignature, their stored integrity the record chain (there is no decider's seal over content). A caller may never supply stamps. Detection never legitimacy (ruling 14): no number of stamps makes an unlawful act lawful.s5:valued0:s7:rule_ids15:REQUIRED-STAMPSs9:record_ids7:rec_233d16:s10:provenanced3:s10:could_readl0:s11:asserted_bys10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:sources6:systems10:rule_citeds8:BOOT-INTs11:record_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.819777+00:00s12:content_forms6:inlines15:occurrence_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.819794+00:00s15:submission_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.819789+00:00s16:evidence_summaryns3:seqi234;s4:refsl0:s5:actors10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:actions11:CREATE-RULEs6:objects11:ACT-KIND-01s6:origind2:s12:subsystem_ids6:kernels8:built_idi0;s6:targetns7:payloadd7:s4:kinds19:seam_act_definitions4:texts725:ACT-KIND record-pen (design/54 §3 B11, §5 L16; archi :3993): one of the twelve KINDS OF WORK the kernel asks its host to perform, DEFINED HERE AS A ROW OF LAW so the seam's act set is derived from the record, never authored beside it (L16). Portability label: portable-host-primitive — names no Linux facility (disk, clock, entropy, threads). What it is: the sole appender + the record reads/stat/mkdir. The derived act set is a fold over these twelve rows (kernel/boot.py live_act_kinds); the running kernel is checked against them by hash and by declared work at every waking (check_kernel_against_rows), or the first act is refused. An act kind is a rule, not an operation — this is a CREATE-RULE, never a CREATE-OP.s5:labels23:portable-host-primitives5:scopes10:space:roots7:meanings47:the sole appender + the record reads/stat/mkdirs7:rule_ids11:ACT-KIND-01s9:seam_kinds10:record-pens9:record_ids7:rec_234d16:s10:provenanced3:s10:could_readl0:s11:asserted_bys10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:sources6:systems10:rule_citeds8:BOOT-INTs11:record_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.821963+00:00s12:content_forms6:inlines15:occurrence_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.821979+00:00s15:submission_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.821974+00:00s16:evidence_summaryns3:seqi235;s4:refsl0:s5:actors10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:actions11:CREATE-RULEs6:objects11:ACT-KIND-02s6:origind2:s12:subsystem_ids6:kernels8:built_idi0;s6:targetns7:payloadd7:s4:kinds19:seam_act_definitions4:texts747:ACT-KIND atomic-write-once (design/54 §3 B11, §5 L16; archi :3993): one of the twelve KINDS OF WORK the kernel asks its host to perform, DEFINED HERE AS A ROW OF LAW so the seam's act set is derived from the record, never authored beside it (L16). Portability label: portable-host-primitive — names no Linux facility (disk, clock, entropy, threads). What it is: the blob/vault write-once + the durability barrier (dir fsync). The derived act set is a fold over these twelve rows (kernel/boot.py live_act_kinds); the running kernel is checked against them by hash and by declared work at every waking (check_kernel_against_rows), or the first act is refused. An act kind is a rule, not an operation — this is a CREATE-RULE, never a CREATE-OP.s5:labels23:portable-host-primitives5:scopes10:space:roots7:meanings62:the blob/vault write-once + the durability barrier (dir fsync)s7:rule_ids11:ACT-KIND-02s9:seam_kinds17:atomic-write-onces9:record_ids7:rec_235d16:s10:provenanced3:s10:could_readl0:s11:asserted_bys10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:sources6:systems10:rule_citeds8:BOOT-INTs11:record_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.824870+00:00s12:content_forms6:inlines15:occurrence_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.824894+00:00s15:submission_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.824889+00:00s16:evidence_summaryns3:seqi236;s4:refsl0:s5:actors10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:actions11:CREATE-RULEs6:objects11:ACT-KIND-03s6:origind2:s12:subsystem_ids6:kernels8:built_idi0;s6:targetns7:payloadd7:s4:kinds19:seam_act_definitions4:texts707:ACT-KIND remove (design/54 §3 B11, §5 L16; archi :3993): one of the twelve KINDS OF WORK the kernel asks its host to perform, DEFINED HERE AS A ROW OF LAW so the seam's act set is derived from the record, never authored beside it (L16). Portability label: portable-host-primitive — names no Linux facility (disk, clock, entropy, threads). What it is: the handover removal tail (blobs). The derived act set is a fold over these twelve rows (kernel/boot.py live_act_kinds); the running kernel is checked against them by hash and by declared work at every waking (check_kernel_against_rows), or the first act is refused. An act kind is a rule, not an operation — this is a CREATE-RULE, never a CREATE-OP.s5:labels23:portable-host-primitives5:scopes10:space:roots7:meanings33:the handover removal tail (blobs)s7:rule_ids11:ACT-KIND-03s9:seam_kinds6:removes9:record_ids7:rec_236d16:s10:provenanced3:s10:could_readl0:s11:asserted_bys10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:sources6:systems10:rule_citeds8:BOOT-INTs11:record_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.841836+00:00s12:content_forms6:inlines15:occurrence_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.841876+00:00s15:submission_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.841871+00:00s16:evidence_summaryns3:seqi237;s4:refsl0:s5:actors10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:actions11:CREATE-RULEs6:objects11:ACT-KIND-04s6:origind2:s12:subsystem_ids6:kernels8:built_idi0;s6:targetns7:payloadd7:s4:kinds19:seam_act_definitions4:texts762:ACT-KIND single-writer-lock (design/54 §3 B11, §5 L16; archi :3993): one of the twelve KINDS OF WORK the kernel asks its host to perform, DEFINED HERE AS A ROW OF LAW so the seam's act set is derived from the record, never authored beside it (L16). Portability label: least-portable — a different host has different process semantics (the host-PID single-writer lock). What it is: the host-PID liveness lock — the LEAST-PORTABLE crossing. The derived act set is a fold over these twelve rows (kernel/boot.py live_act_kinds); the running kernel is checked against them by hash and by declared work at every waking (check_kernel_against_rows), or the first act is refused. An act kind is a rule, not an operation — this is a CREATE-RULE, never a CREATE-OP.s5:labels14:least-portables5:scopes10:space:roots7:meanings58:the host-PID liveness lock — the LEAST-PORTABLE crossings7:rule_ids11:ACT-KIND-04s9:seam_kinds18:single-writer-locks9:record_ids7:rec_237d16:s10:provenanced3:s10:could_readl0:s11:asserted_bys10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:sources6:systems10:rule_citeds8:BOOT-INTs11:record_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.843958+00:00s12:content_forms6:inlines15:occurrence_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.843972+00:00s15:submission_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.843969+00:00s16:evidence_summaryns3:seqi238;s4:refsl0:s5:actors10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:actions11:CREATE-RULEs6:objects11:ACT-KIND-05s6:origind2:s12:subsystem_ids6:kernels8:built_idi0;s6:targetns7:payloadd7:s4:kinds19:seam_act_definitions4:texts736:ACT-KIND recording-clock (design/54 §3 B11, §5 L16; archi :3993): one of the twelve KINDS OF WORK the kernel asks its host to perform, DEFINED HERE AS A ROW OF LAW so the seam's act set is derived from the record, never authored beside it (L16). Portability label: portable-host-primitive — names no Linux facility (disk, clock, entropy, threads). What it is: datetime.now(utc) — the recorded_at on every record. The derived act set is a fold over these twelve rows (kernel/boot.py live_act_kinds); the running kernel is checked against them by hash and by declared work at every waking (check_kernel_against_rows), or the first act is refused. An act kind is a rule, not an operation — this is a CREATE-RULE, never a CREATE-OP.s5:labels23:portable-host-primitives5:scopes10:space:roots7:meanings53:datetime.now(utc) — the recorded_at on every records7:rule_ids11:ACT-KIND-05s9:seam_kinds15:recording-clocks9:record_ids7:rec_238d16:s10:provenanced3:s10:could_readl0:s11:asserted_bys10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:sources6:systems10:rule_citeds8:BOOT-INTs11:record_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.846089+00:00s12:content_forms6:inlines15:occurrence_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.846109+00:00s15:submission_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.846103+00:00s16:evidence_summaryns3:seqi239;s4:refsl0:s5:actors10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:actions11:CREATE-RULEs6:objects11:ACT-KIND-06s6:origind2:s12:subsystem_ids6:kernels8:built_idi0;s6:targetns7:payloadd7:s4:kinds19:seam_act_definitions4:texts736:ACT-KIND commit-window (design/54 §3 B11, §5 L16; archi :3993): one of the twelve KINDS OF WORK the kernel asks its host to perform, DEFINED HERE AS A ROW OF LAW so the seam's act set is derived from the record, never authored beside it (L16). Portability label: portable-host-primitive — names no Linux facility (disk, clock, entropy, threads). What it is: time.monotonic / time.sleep — the group-commit window. The derived act set is a fold over these twelve rows (kernel/boot.py live_act_kinds); the running kernel is checked against them by hash and by declared work at every waking (check_kernel_against_rows), or the first act is refused. An act kind is a rule, not an operation — this is a CREATE-RULE, never a CREATE-OP.s5:labels23:portable-host-primitives5:scopes10:space:roots7:meanings55:time.monotonic / time.sleep — the group-commit windows7:rule_ids11:ACT-KIND-06s9:seam_kinds13:commit-windows9:record_ids7:rec_239d16:s10:provenanced3:s10:could_readl0:s11:asserted_bys10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:sources6:systems10:rule_citeds8:BOOT-INTs11:record_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.848674+00:00s12:content_forms6:inlines15:occurrence_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.848693+00:00s15:submission_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.848688+00:00s16:evidence_summaryns3:seqi240;s4:refsl0:s5:actors10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:actions11:CREATE-RULEs6:objects11:ACT-KIND-07s6:origind2:s12:subsystem_ids6:kernels8:built_idi0;s6:targetns7:payloadd7:s4:kinds19:seam_act_definitions4:texts714:ACT-KIND entropy (design/54 §3 B11, §5 L16; archi :3993): one of the twelve KINDS OF WORK the kernel asks its host to perform, DEFINED HERE AS A ROW OF LAW so the seam's act set is derived from the record, never authored beside it (L16). Portability label: portable-host-primitive — names no Linux facility (disk, clock, entropy, threads). What it is: os.urandom — nonces and fresh secrets. The derived act set is a fold over these twelve rows (kernel/boot.py live_act_kinds); the running kernel is checked against them by hash and by declared work at every waking (check_kernel_against_rows), or the first act is refused. An act kind is a rule, not an operation — this is a CREATE-RULE, never a CREATE-OP.s5:labels23:portable-host-primitives5:scopes10:space:roots7:meanings39:os.urandom — nonces and fresh secretss7:rule_ids11:ACT-KIND-07s9:seam_kinds7:entropys9:record_ids7:rec_240d16:s10:provenanced3:s10:could_readl0:s11:asserted_bys10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:sources6:systems10:rule_citeds8:BOOT-INTs11:record_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.851299+00:00s12:content_forms6:inlines15:occurrence_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.851322+00:00s15:submission_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.851316+00:00s16:evidence_summaryns3:seqi241;s4:refsl0:s5:actors10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:actions11:CREATE-RULEs6:objects11:ACT-KIND-08s6:origind2:s12:subsystem_ids6:kernels8:built_idi0;s6:targetns7:payloadd7:s4:kinds19:seam_act_definitions4:texts742:ACT-KIND concurrency (design/54 §3 B11, §5 L16; archi :3993): one of the twelve KINDS OF WORK the kernel asks its host to perform, DEFINED HERE AS A ROW OF LAW so the seam's act set is derived from the record, never authored beside it (L16). Portability label: portable-host-primitive — names no Linux facility (disk, clock, entropy, threads). What it is: the threading substrate (a host primitive the core must supply). The derived act set is a fold over these twelve rows (kernel/boot.py live_act_kinds); the running kernel is checked against them by hash and by declared work at every waking (check_kernel_against_rows), or the first act is refused. An act kind is a rule, not an operation — this is a CREATE-RULE, never a CREATE-OP.s5:labels23:portable-host-primitives5:scopes10:space:roots7:meanings63:the threading substrate (a host primitive the core must supply)s7:rule_ids11:ACT-KIND-08s9:seam_kinds11:concurrencys9:record_ids7:rec_241d16:s10:provenanced3:s10:could_readl0:s11:asserted_bys10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:sources6:systems10:rule_citeds8:BOOT-INTs11:record_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.853543+00:00s12:content_forms6:inlines15:occurrence_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.853565+00:00s15:submission_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.853561+00:00s16:evidence_summaryns3:seqi242;s4:refsl0:s5:actors10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:actions11:CREATE-RULEs6:objects11:ACT-KIND-09s6:origind2:s12:subsystem_ids6:kernels8:built_idi0;s6:targetns7:payloadd7:s4:kinds19:seam_act_definitions4:texts709:ACT-KIND network-socket (design/54 §3 B11, §5 L16; archi :3993): one of the twelve KINDS OF WORK the kernel asks its host to perform, DEFINED HERE AS A ROW OF LAW so the seam's act set is derived from the record, never authored beside it (L16). Portability label: guest-gated-capability — real only inside the pinned guest (EP-00 rule 9). What it is: the one guest-gated outbound socket. The derived act set is a fold over these twelve rows (kernel/boot.py live_act_kinds); the running kernel is checked against them by hash and by declared work at every waking (check_kernel_against_rows), or the first act is refused. An act kind is a rule, not an operation — this is a CREATE-RULE, never a CREATE-OP.s5:labels22:guest-gated-capabilitys5:scopes10:space:roots7:meanings35:the one guest-gated outbound sockets7:rule_ids11:ACT-KIND-09s9:seam_kinds14:network-sockets9:record_ids7:rec_242d16:s10:provenanced3:s10:could_readl0:s11:asserted_bys10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:sources6:systems10:rule_citeds8:BOOT-INTs11:record_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.855363+00:00s12:content_forms6:inlines15:occurrence_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.855382+00:00s15:submission_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.855377+00:00s16:evidence_summaryns3:seqi243;s4:refsl0:s5:actors10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:actions11:CREATE-RULEs6:objects11:ACT-KIND-10s6:origind2:s12:subsystem_ids6:kernels8:built_idi0;s6:targetns7:payloadd7:s4:kinds19:seam_act_definitions4:texts729:ACT-KIND body-read (design/54 §3 B11, §5 L16; archi :3993): one of the twelve KINDS OF WORK the kernel asks its host to perform, DEFINED HERE AS A ROW OF LAW so the seam's act set is derived from the record, never authored beside it (L16). Portability label: portable-host-primitive — names no Linux facility (disk, clock, entropy, threads). What it is: the attestation member read + os.walk of the S-plane. The derived act set is a fold over these twelve rows (kernel/boot.py live_act_kinds); the running kernel is checked against them by hash and by declared work at every waking (check_kernel_against_rows), or the first act is refused. An act kind is a rule, not an operation — this is a CREATE-RULE, never a CREATE-OP.s5:labels23:portable-host-primitives5:scopes10:space:roots7:meanings52:the attestation member read + os.walk of the S-planes7:rule_ids11:ACT-KIND-10s9:seam_kinds9:body-reads9:record_ids7:rec_243d16:s10:provenanced3:s10:could_readl0:s11:asserted_bys10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:sources6:systems10:rule_citeds8:BOOT-INTs11:record_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.858137+00:00s12:content_forms6:inlines15:occurrence_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.858178+00:00s15:submission_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.858173+00:00s16:evidence_summaryns3:seqi244;s4:refsl0:s5:actors10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:actions11:CREATE-RULEs6:objects11:ACT-KIND-11s6:origind2:s12:subsystem_ids6:kernels8:built_idi0;s6:targetns7:payloadd7:s4:kinds19:seam_act_definitions4:texts749:ACT-KIND founding-pack-read (design/54 §3 B11, §5 L16; archi :3993): one of the twelve KINDS OF WORK the kernel asks its host to perform, DEFINED HERE AS A ROW OF LAW so the seam's act set is derived from the record, never authored beside it (L16). Portability label: portable-host-primitive — names no Linux facility (disk, clock, entropy, threads). What it is: the installer's read of founding-pack.json (DATA, never edited). The derived act set is a fold over these twelve rows (kernel/boot.py live_act_kinds); the running kernel is checked against them by hash and by declared work at every waking (check_kernel_against_rows), or the first act is refused. An act kind is a rule, not an operation — this is a CREATE-RULE, never a CREATE-OP.s5:labels23:portable-host-primitives5:scopes10:space:roots7:meanings63:the installer's read of founding-pack.json (DATA, never edited)s7:rule_ids11:ACT-KIND-11s9:seam_kinds18:founding-pack-reads9:record_ids7:rec_244d16:s10:provenanced3:s10:could_readl0:s11:asserted_bys10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:sources6:systems10:rule_citeds8:BOOT-INTs11:record_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.860081+00:00s12:content_forms6:inlines15:occurrence_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.860100+00:00s15:submission_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.860094+00:00s16:evidence_summaryns3:seqi245;s4:refsl0:s5:actors10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:actions11:CREATE-RULEs6:objects11:ACT-KIND-12s6:origind2:s12:subsystem_ids6:kernels8:built_idi0;s6:targetns7:payloadd7:s4:kinds19:seam_act_definitions4:texts751:ACT-KIND memory (design/54 §3 B11, §5 L16; archi :3993): one of the twelve KINDS OF WORK the kernel asks its host to perform, DEFINED HERE AS A ROW OF LAW so the seam's act set is derived from the record, never authored beside it (L16). Portability label: portable-host-primitive — names no Linux facility (disk, clock, entropy, threads). What it is: host-backed anonymous memory — the C7 P7a interpreter-hosting growth (12th). The derived act set is a fold over these twelve rows (kernel/boot.py live_act_kinds); the running kernel is checked against them by hash and by declared work at every waking (check_kernel_against_rows), or the first act is refused. An act kind is a rule, not an operation — this is a CREATE-RULE, never a CREATE-OP.s5:labels23:portable-host-primitives5:scopes10:space:roots7:meanings77:host-backed anonymous memory — the C7 P7a interpreter-hosting growth (12th)s7:rule_ids11:ACT-KIND-12s9:seam_kinds6:memorys9:record_ids7:rec_245d16:s10:provenanced3:s10:could_readl0:s11:asserted_bys10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:sources6:systems10:rule_citeds8:BOOT-INTs11:record_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.862245+00:00s12:content_forms6:inlines15:occurrence_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.862375+00:00s15:submission_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.862368+00:00s16:evidence_summaryns3:seqi246;s4:refsl0:s5:actors10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:actions11:CREATE-RULEs6:objects27:STRUCTURED-UNSTRUCTURED-LAWs6:origind2:s12:subsystem_ids6:kernels8:built_idi0;s6:targetns7:payloadd5:s11:enforced_bys867:founding.install._validate (C8 P1): a declared-structured operation that does not replay to identity (definition flag replays_to_identity:false) is refused at the founding door when CELL-LAW is live — the ONE computer of the rule is kernel.opdefs.definition_replays_to_identity, reused by kernel.views.op_replays_to_identity so the founding-door refusal and the read-side finding (kernel.views.declared_s_findings / tools.conformance.cell_census) can never diverge. The confirming enumeration (tools.conformance.cell_census: all ninety-four operations declared structured, each replaying to identity, zero interpreting content) enumerates and confirms the declared cells; it derives nothing from field shapes. The runtime (actor class, task cell) pairing is enforced live at the gate (kernel.gate._pairing_step) since C6 P8b — READ here, not changed by this rule.s11:enforcements4:lives4:texts1972:C8 P1 (design/56 §3 B4; §5 L4/L28). THE STRUCTURED / UNSTRUCTURED RULE. An operation is STRUCTURED when its effect is fully fixed by its declared parameters WITHOUT interpreting content — a whole block moved unread is structured, a fully specified black-and-white edit (remove the final full stop only) is structured — and UNSTRUCTURED when the effect DEPENDS ON INTERPRETING CONTENT. Natural-language processing is unstructured work by this test. Structured/unstructured is a property of THE OPERATION ON ITS OBJECT (L4), decided per operation, NEVER derived from the shapes of the op's fields: a text field carries a name as easily as a judgment, so a shape can never tell structured from unstructured — the cell is DECLARED founding data (CELL-LAW, L28), and a confirming enumeration ENUMERATES and CONFIRMS the declared cells (every one of the ninety-four operations declares its cell, all structured, each replaying to identity), it does not reclassify. THE CLASS CONSEQUENCE (L28): a program performing an unstructured operation acts in the AI CLASS, not the program class, and meets that class's ceilings. THE FOUNDING TEST: a declared-structured operation MUST REPLAY TO IDENTITY (its record a pure function of its inputs — the estate's founding property, kill-the-registry-replay-identical) or its declaration is a FINDING; a declared-structured operation that does NOT replay to identity (it interprets content) is REFUSED AT THE FOUNDING DOOR when the pack installs (founding.install._validate; the read-side finding kernel.views.declared_s_findings promoted to an install refusal). A declared-judgment operation is validated to its schema and NEVER scored by the machine. The runtime (actor class, task cell) PAIRING is ENFORCED LIVE at the gate since C6 P8b (kernel.gate._pairing_step, superseding the earlier held state) — READ and leaned on here, its enforcement state unchanged by this rule; this rule's own new refusal is at the FOUNDING DOOR.s5:scopes10:space:roots7:rule_ids27:STRUCTURED-UNSTRUCTURED-LAWs9:record_ids7:rec_246d16:s10:provenanced3:s10:could_readl0:s11:asserted_bys10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:sources6:systems10:rule_citeds8:BOOT-INTs11:record_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.864988+00:00s12:content_forms6:inlines15:occurrence_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.865006+00:00s15:submission_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.865001+00:00s16:evidence_summaryns3:seqi247;s4:refsl0:s5:actors10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:actions11:CREATE-RULEs6:objects21:VIEWS-ARE-THE-SYSTEMSs6:origind2:s12:subsystem_ids6:kernels8:built_idi0;s6:targetns7:payloadd5:s11:enforced_bys1112:kernel.gate._constitution_guard (C8 P2, SYSTEM-only per C8-P2-REPAIR): a view_definition write — CREATE-VIEW, or any op whose effect payload carries kind 'view_definition' — by an actor that is NOT the literal SYSTEM recorder is REFUSED and recorded, citing VIEWS-ARE-THE-SYSTEMS by name, for EVERY view (ordinary filter views as well as masters) and for EVERY actor including the derived chain-end (the owner) writing a view DIRECTLY. The master-tier conservation branch (EP-08B B2) runs FIRST in the same guard and keeps its BOOT-INT citation for a protected master superseded by a NON-ROOT actor (that non-root refusal is UNCHANGED); this SYSTEM-only branch refuses every other direct view write, the owner's included — the owner's amendment travels as a SYSTEM-executed authorization (§10 H cut 1). The gate STILL decides every act against the live record (I3): the guard is a refusal step and changes NOTHING about how views compute from rows on read. The read-side property (a view recomputed from rows, killed and replayed identical) is untouched; a view is never patched in place (design/56 §3a).s11:enforcements4:lives4:texts2170:C8 P2 (design/56 §3 B3; §4 I5; §5 L2; §2; §3a; §10 H cut 1 — the SYSTEM-only repair, C8-P2-REPAIR). VIEWS ARE THE SYSTEM'S. CREATE-VIEW and EVERY view-writing operation are admitted to the SYSTEM's authority ONLY — the literal SYSTEM recorder (the OS). EVERY actor class the OS serves — human, ai, program, AND the derived chain-end root (kernel.views.chain_end, which under the founding is the owner and after a lawful handover is the successor) — READS a view and never writes one DIRECTLY: a user, root included, is always INDIRECT, and the custodian of every view operation is always the OS (owner ruling, board 2026-09-23). The owner's own view change TRAVELS as an authorization the SYSTEM executes, never a direct chain-end write (the submit-verify-execute path is its own later unit; §10 H cut 2). L2: 'all view mechanics are the system's role; no other program may load or edit a view'; §2: 'no program can create or change a view — views are the system's alone, computed from rows on read'. This holds for EVERY view: an ordinary filter view ('when matches -> move it'), a master (a bind naming an S-plane fold), and a derived row alike. A VIEW IS NEVER PATCHED IN PLACE (§3a): it is derived, dropped, derived again — a view change is a NEW appended definition (latest-wins), never a mutation of the stored record, and the served view is recomputed from rows on read (I1/I3). THE MASTER-TIER CONSERVATION (EP-08B B2) is the special case this rule GENERALISES, not weakens: a protected owner/constitutional master superseded by a non-root actor still refuses BOOT-INT and stays intact (that NON-ROOT refusal is UNCHANGED). This rule now RETIRES the owner's currently-founded DIRECT in-place master edit as well: the direct chain-end view write EP-08B B2 admitted is dropped, the owner's amendment travelling as a SYSTEM-executed authorization instead — executing the owner's L2/§2 and the 2026-09-23 SYSTEM-only-including-root ruling, which are LATER than the pre-L2 EP-08 openness and the EP-08B owner-direct edit (later rulings control). SYSTEM's founding seeds are appended at genesis above the gate (store._append) and are UNCHANGED.s5:scopes10:space:roots7:rule_ids21:VIEWS-ARE-THE-SYSTEMSs9:record_ids7:rec_247d16:s10:provenanced3:s10:could_readl0:s11:asserted_bys10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:sources6:systems10:rule_citeds10:ROOT-NEG-6s11:record_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.868829+00:00s12:content_forms6:inlines15:occurrence_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.868889+00:00s15:submission_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.868880+00:00s16:evidence_summaryns3:seqi248;s4:refsl0:s5:actors10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:actions11:CREATE-RULEs6:objects17:VIEW-SUBMIT-ROUTEs6:origind2:s12:subsystem_ids6:kernels8:built_idi0;s6:targetns7:payloadd5:s11:enforced_bys1080:kernel.gate._submit_view_step (the submit door: an established-or-anchor check -- the submitter is in views.accounts(), else refused VIEW-SUBMIT-ROUTE by name; a view-tier-authority check -- a proposal superseding an owner/constitutional master by a non-root submitter refuses BOOT-INT; a lawfulness check -- a malformed view definition refuses AR-2) and kernel.gate._maybe_execute_submit (the execute: on a lawful verified submit the gate fires a CREATE-VIEW as the literal SYSTEM whose payload carries authorising_submit = the submit row's content hash) and kernel.gate._constitution_guard (the execute door: the master-tier conservation reads the authoriser through the bound submit so the SYSTEM's execute of a root-authorised master change is admitted while a direct non-root write still refuses BOOT-INT; and an executed view write carrying authorising_submit that binds NO SUBMIT-VIEW row -- an orphan execute -- is refused VIEW-SUBMIT-ROUTE). OP_CHECKS is unchanged: the verify rides the existing authority/conservation and payload-lawfulness machinery, no new check kind.s11:enforcements4:lives4:texts1783:C8 VIEW-SUBMIT-AND-REPOINT (design/56 §10 H cut 2 -- the proposal-and-ban path). THE SUBMIT-VERIFY-EXECUTE ROUTE. Views are the system's (VIEWS-ARE-THE-SYSTEMS): a non-system actor never writes a view directly. This rule founds the LAWFUL INDIRECT route by which such an actor's change reaches the record. A non-system actor -- a person, the owner, a program -- invokes SUBMIT-VIEW to PROPOSE a view add/change; the gate VERIFIES (1) the submitter's VIEW-TIER AUTHORITY -- an established account or the genesis anchor holds standing to submit, and a master/owner-tier view requires the root chain-end (the master-tier conservation's root authority, EP-08B B2, expressed through the route) -- and (2) the change's LAWFULNESS (a well-formed view definition); then it EXECUTES the change as the SYSTEM (a CREATE-VIEW by the literal SYSTEM recorder whose payload CITES the submit row by reference, so the authorization is traceable by row reference and never a free-text authoriser value) or it BANS it ('if the system didn't like it, it is a ban' -- a refusal recorded, the reason named, no view write). An executed view write with NO bound submit row (an orphan execute) is REFUSED. SUBMIT-VIEW's admission is VIEW-TIER AUTHORITY, NOT account establishment: it carries no CREATE-ACCOUNT establishment check, so a founding boot anchor (the owner) submits without being refused 'never established', and it is NOT a second crossing -- a foreign body still travels BORDER-SUBMIT with its establishment law intact, while an unestablished non-anchor submitter is refused by name. This RESTORES the change route the SYSTEM-only rule (cut 1, C8-P2-REPAIR) retired for the owner's direct write, landing in the SAME set: the direct write retires as the indirect route opens (no window, no gap).s5:scopes10:space:roots7:rule_ids17:VIEW-SUBMIT-ROUTEs9:record_ids7:rec_248d16:s10:provenanced3:s10:could_readl0:s11:asserted_bys10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:sources6:systems10:rule_citeds8:BOOT-INTs11:record_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.872419+00:00s12:content_forms6:inlines15:occurrence_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.872439+00:00s15:submission_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.872434+00:00s16:evidence_summaryns3:seqi249;s4:refsl0:s5:actors10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:actions11:CREATE-RULEs6:objects16:INCARNATION-LOADs6:origind2:s12:subsystem_ids6:kernels8:built_idi0;s6:targetns7:payloadd14:s10:row_fieldsl7:s5:classs4:seals15:rule_set_digests8:openingss11:view_digests6:handles7:invokers14:founded_fieldsl2:s12:touch_pointss5:classs14:single_openingd1:s5:humans13:system-facings15:optional_fieldsl1:s6:parents16:declared_classesl2:s7:programs2:ais18:declaration_fieldsl2:s4:seals12:touch_pointss20:declaration_row_kinds23:incarnation-declarations3:acts4:LOADs4:kinds26:incarnation_act_definitions4:texts3607:C8 P3 (design/56 §3 B1, B7, §3a, §10 G; the owner, v0.58: "A PROGRAM IS INSTALLED ALL OPERATIONS CAPTURED AND HAVE A RULE TO LOAD THE LIST AS A VIEW WHEN LOADING THE PROGRAM FULL STOP. LOADING ANY PROGRAM IS AN ACTIVITY WHICH WILL BE RECORDED."). THE LOAD ACT, AN ACT KIND DEFINED AS A ROW OF LAW, NEVER AN OPERATION (the 1.55.0 precedent: an act kind is a rule, not an op; this row is of its own kind and never one of the seam's twelve). Every incarnation the system runs -- a program's process, a human's session, an AI's session, a driver -- is BORN by ONE row before its first act: actor SYSTEM, recorded as the system's activity (payload kind incarnation-load), object the actor's IDENTITY (its recorded establishment; a handle is never an identity), carrying: the identity's SEAL (for a class installed from a sealed image, program or ai, the digest of the image, checked against its installed declaration before the row is written, so a load whose bytes do not match the seal is refused; for a human, the identity as the record establishes it), THE INCARNATION'S CLASS (born here, one of the closed actor classes, equal to the identity's founded actor_class), the digest of the RULE SET its operations are decided under, its OPENINGS (design/39 §3: a system-facing and a user-facing channel; the human holds the system-facing one only), the DIGEST of the VIEW it decides against, its HANDLE and its INVOKER; a sub-process names its PARENT's handle. THE INSTALL (payload kind incarnation-declaration) captures the program's operations: a STATIC READ of the sealed image, before any run, lists the operation names its code references, each of which must exist by name in the registry (an unregistered operation does not exist), and the maker's declaration is cut to that read (wider is cut to the code, narrower is kept). THE TWO FIELDS THIS RULE FOUNDS: the DECLARED TOUCH POINTS, carried by the install row, and the CLASS, carried by the load row. THE VIEW is the intersection of the declared touch points, the grants the invoker holds and the ceilings of the incarnation's class, computed at load, its digest on the load row; the gate re-derives it from the live record at every act and never decides against a copy. REFUSED BY NAME: an act naming an incarnation with no birth row; an act through a handle born to another invoker; an act outside the declared touch points though the invoker holds the grant; an act through a third opening, or through another incarnation's opening (a direct move: a move between programs crosses the system, A's act through its own system-facing opening and B's receipt through its own); a view copy whose digest does not match the load row's, or whose load digest no longer matches the rules in force (stale; a view is never patched, the next load recomputes it); a load row missing a field this rule founds (a load row with no class is incomplete). The install, load and end rows are the SYSTEM's to write. The class LAW itself -- the class binds at every operation, every classing act records who classed under which rule -- is its own founding row, not this one. THE CEILING: the view computed at the load is the incarnation's ceiling, so an act whose operation lay outside the operations that view held must be refused by name even where the live record now grants it; a grant or rule made after the load reaches the next load, never the running incarnation, and a rule changed after the load narrows at once. A refused act of a loaded incarnation names its seal, stale when the rules deciding its operations no longer match the digest its load row carries.s5:scopes10:space:roots7:rule_ids16:INCARNATION-LOADs8:openingsl2:s13:system-facings11:user-facings8:row_kinds16:incarnation-loads9:record_ids7:rec_249d16:s10:provenanced3:s10:could_readl0:s11:asserted_bys10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:sources6:systems10:rule_citeds8:BOOT-INTs11:record_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.877399+00:00s12:content_forms6:inlines15:occurrence_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.877423+00:00s15:submission_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.877417+00:00s16:evidence_summaryns3:seqi250;s4:refsl0:s5:actors10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:actions11:CREATE-RULEs6:objects15:INCARNATION-ENDs6:origind2:s12:subsystem_ids6:kernels8:built_idi0;s6:targetns7:payloadd7:s10:row_fieldsl1:s6:handles3:acts3:ENDs4:kinds26:incarnation_act_definitions4:texts597:C8 P3 (design/56 §3 B1, §3a). THE END ACT, AN ACT KIND DEFINED AS A ROW OF LAW, NEVER AN OPERATION (the 1.55.0 precedent; of its own kind, never one of the seam's twelve). An incarnation ENDS by ONE row: actor SYSTEM, recorded as the system's activity (payload kind incarnation-end), object the identity it was born of, carrying its HANDLE; the row closes exactly one live incarnation, and a later act on the ended handle is refused by name. Nothing is cleared: the view was a derived thing, dropped with the incarnation, and the views are computed on read. The end row is the SYSTEM's to write.s5:scopes10:space:roots7:rule_ids15:INCARNATION-ENDs8:row_kinds15:incarnation-ends9:record_ids7:rec_250d16:s10:provenanced3:s10:could_readl0:s11:asserted_bys10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:sources6:systems10:rule_citeds8:BOOT-INTs11:record_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.880962+00:00s12:content_forms6:inlines15:occurrence_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.880986+00:00s15:submission_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.880980+00:00s16:evidence_summaryns3:seqi251;s4:refsl0:s5:actors10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:actions11:CREATE-RULEs6:objects21:REL-LAW-GEOMETRY-CELLs6:origind2:s12:subsystem_ids6:kernels8:built_idi0;s6:targetns7:payloadd3:s14:geometry_cellsd4:s2:ADs1:Ss2:EMs1:Ss2:INs1:Us2:NSs1:Ss4:texts333:declaring that two things overlap is a judgment: a relation row's task cell is read from its geometry — IN is unstructured (U); NS, EM and AD are structured (S) — S/U is decided at the operation on its object (the owner, design/56). So a program-class actor is refused declaring an overlap, and an ai-class actor may declare one.s7:rule_ids21:REL-LAW-GEOMETRY-CELLs9:record_ids7:rec_251d16:s10:provenanced3:s10:could_readl0:s11:asserted_bys10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:sources6:systems10:rule_citeds8:BOOT-INTs11:record_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.885222+00:00s12:content_forms6:inlines15:occurrence_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.885248+00:00s15:submission_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.885242+00:00s16:evidence_summaryns3:seqi252;s4:refsl0:s5:actors10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:actions11:CREATE-INFOs6:objects15:pack:actor-axess6:origind2:s12:subsystem_ids6:kernels8:built_idi0;s6:targetns7:payloadd4:s4:kinds13:category_packs4:names10:actor-axess4:texts487:C8-P0a-i (design/65, the owner's three sittings of 2026-09-25; archi :5216). THE SIX AXES BY NAME, THE CONSTITUTIONAL LEVEL (design/65 sitting three): every actor carries these readings, computed from the record, not stored; every classing is a recorded act citing a rule. This row and the axes change by descent alone, a new world citing its parent. The mind-kind category words stay founded once, in pack:actor-classes — this row names the axis, not the words (archi :5220 option A).s6:levelsl6:s8:categorys4:tagss22:single-or-organisations4:seens5:ruleds8:hardwares9:record_ids7:rec_252d16:s10:provenanced3:s10:could_readl0:s11:asserted_bys10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:sources6:systems10:rule_citeds8:BOOT-INTs11:record_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.887278+00:00s12:content_forms6:inlines15:occurrence_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.887297+00:00s15:submission_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.887291+00:00s16:evidence_summaryns3:seqi253;s4:refsl0:s5:actors10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:actions11:CREATE-INFOs6:objects14:pack:axis-tagss6:origind2:s12:subsystem_ids6:kernels8:built_idi0;s6:targetns7:payloadd4:s4:kinds13:category_packs4:names9:axis-tagss4:texts285:C8-P0a-i (design/65 §2). The structured/unstructured tag set an actor shows: {S} a program's arm, {U} a model's arm, {S,U} (S+U here) an organisation of both — the union of its members. No actor is forced into one half; the gate always reads the acting member against the operation.s6:levelsl3:s1:Ss1:Us3:S+Us9:record_ids7:rec_253d16:s10:provenanced3:s10:could_readl0:s11:asserted_bys10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:sources6:systems10:rule_citeds8:BOOT-INTs11:record_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.889527+00:00s12:content_forms6:inlines15:occurrence_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.889569+00:00s15:submission_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.889562+00:00s16:evidence_summaryns3:seqi254;s4:refsl0:s5:actors10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:actions11:CREATE-INFOs6:objects32:pack:axis-single-or-organisations6:origind2:s12:subsystem_ids6:kernels8:built_idi0;s6:targetns7:payloadd4:s4:kinds13:category_packs4:names27:axis-single-or-organisations4:texts293:C8-P0a-i (design/65 §3). Whether an actor is one thing or contains actors, read from containment rows, computed each time — not stored, not declared a second time. An organisation does not act itself; its members act, and a rule binding the organisation binds every member's acts inside it.s6:levelsl2:s6:singles12:organisations9:record_ids7:rec_254d16:s10:provenanced3:s10:could_readl0:s11:asserted_bys10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:sources6:systems10:rule_citeds8:BOOT-INTs11:record_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.891958+00:00s12:content_forms6:inlines15:occurrence_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.891980+00:00s15:submission_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.891975+00:00s16:evidence_summaryns3:seqi255;s4:refsl0:s5:actors10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:actions11:CREATE-INFOs6:objects14:pack:axis-seens6:origind2:s12:subsystem_ids6:kernels8:built_idi0;s6:targetns7:payloadd4:s4:kinds13:category_packs4:names9:axis-seens4:texts291:C8-P0a-i (design/65 §5). Whether we can read what the actor is made of and how it decides: glass — installed on our record, sealed bytes we hold, a declaration read from them, two openings we watch; sealed — insides dark, no row witnesses how it decided, its answers recorded as claims.s6:levelsl2:s5:glasss6:sealeds9:record_ids7:rec_255d16:s10:provenanced3:s10:could_readl0:s11:asserted_bys10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:sources6:systems10:rule_citeds8:BOOT-INTs11:record_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.894791+00:00s12:content_forms6:inlines15:occurrence_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.894811+00:00s15:submission_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.894806+00:00s16:evidence_summaryns3:seqi256;s4:refsl0:s5:actors10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:actions11:CREATE-INFOs6:objects15:pack:axis-ruleds6:origind2:s12:subsystem_ids6:kernels8:built_idi0;s6:targetns7:payloadd4:s4:kinds13:category_packs4:names10:axis-ruleds4:texts278:C8-P0a-i (design/65 §6). Whether the actor's acts are decided by our gate citing our rules (yes) or it interacts with us while it keeps its own law (no) — computed from how its acts arrive: through the gate, ruled; through the border as an ask we then decide, a counterparty.s6:levelsl2:s3:yess2:nos9:record_ids7:rec_256d16:s10:provenanced3:s10:could_readl0:s11:asserted_bys10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:sources6:systems10:rule_citeds8:BOOT-INTs11:record_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.897750+00:00s12:content_forms6:inlines15:occurrence_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.897773+00:00s15:submission_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.897767+00:00s16:evidence_summaryns3:seqi257;s4:refsl0:s5:actors10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:actions11:CREATE-INFOs6:objects18:pack:axis-hardwares6:origind2:s12:subsystem_ids6:kernels8:built_idi0;s6:targetns7:payloadd4:s4:kinds13:category_packs4:names13:axis-hardwares4:texts247:C8-P0a-i (design/65 §7). Whether the actor itself meets the metal — hands, firmware, a driver bound to its device — computed from device rows and seat rows. The system itself is not hardware-touching: it reaches every device through a driver.s6:levelsl2:s3:yess2:nos9:record_ids7:rec_257d16:s10:provenanced3:s10:could_readl0:s11:asserted_bys10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:sources6:systems10:rule_citeds8:BOOT-INTs11:record_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.900372+00:00s12:content_forms6:inlines15:occurrence_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.900397+00:00s15:submission_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.900391+00:00s16:evidence_summaryns3:seqi258;s4:refsl0:s5:actors10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:actions11:CREATE-INFOs6:objects18:pack:axis-categorys6:origind2:s12:subsystem_ids6:kernels8:built_idi0;s6:targetns7:payloadd5:s13:composed_fromd2:s18:pack:actor-classess69:levels (human, ai, program) — the mind-kind words' one founded homes6:systems219:CONST-ACTOR-CATEGORY's system_actors (step 05-root-laws) — the founded home of the mind-kind word "system"; composed from that row's system_actors, not copied (C8-CLASS-LAW-THE-ACTOR-CATEGORY, :5220's gate discharged)s4:kinds13:category_packs4:names13:axis-categorys4:texts754:C8-P0a-i (archi :5220 option A: THE CATEGORY AXIS IS WHOLE BY COMPOSITION, no word founded twice). This row's own founded levels are counterparty and none — no mind-kind word is written here. human, ai and program are read from pack:actor-classes' own levels (composed_from below), not copied: a second row carrying the same words would be the same-measure duplicate this estate turns away, and drift between two copies of "human" would be a constitutional defect minted by hand. The member "system" has no founded home yet — no class-law row exists — so it is admitted from the temporary source this row names below; the owner's pending class-law gate is its founded home, and that row's landing re-points this one reference, not the word (:5220).s6:levelsl2:s12:counterpartys4:nones9:record_ids7:rec_258d16:s10:provenanced3:s10:could_readl0:s11:asserted_bys10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:sources6:systems10:rule_citeds8:BOOT-INTs11:record_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.903145+00:00s12:content_forms6:inlines15:occurrence_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.903165+00:00s15:submission_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.903160+00:00s16:evidence_summaryns3:seqi259;s4:refsl0:s5:actors10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:actions11:CREATE-INFOs6:objects19:pack:familiar-namess6:origind2:s12:subsystem_ids6:kernels8:built_idi0;s6:targetns7:payloadd5:s4:kinds13:category_packs4:names14:familiar-namess4:texts1102:C8-P0a-i (design/65 sitting two's regions paragraph and sitting three's freeze; archi :5222 countersign). THE FAMILIAR NAMES — a founded word list of named regions, not a stored class: human user, LLM model, user application, service, driver, firmware, OS. Each name is defined BY its region — the axis values it names (an axis it leaves out is written out as every one of that axis's founded values, not as "any") plus the relation it names, where one applies. NLP is not an actor name (design/65 :5216) — it has no entry. THE WORD CORRECTION (archi :5222, the owner's rename, "sorry change AI to that"): the founded word is "LLM model", not "AI model" — sitting two's regions paragraph is corrected by sitting three, which controls; the region definition is unchanged, the word alone moved. This list is VERSION-FROZEN by PLACE-LAW-FROZEN-LISTS: a gov-os version birth is the one point it changes at. A new kind arriving between versions still works fully — placed by its axes, ruled by its regions, every act recorded — it simply carries no familiar word until the next version names it.s6:levelsl7:s10:human users9:LLM models16:user applications7:services6:drivers8:firmwares2:OSs7:regionsd7:s10:human userd2:s4:axesd6:s22:single-or-organisationl1:s6:singles4:seenl2:s5:glasss6:sealeds4:tagsl3:s1:Ss1:Us3:S+Us5:ruledl1:s3:yess8:categoryl1:s5:humans8:hardwarel2:s3:yess2:nos9:relationsl0:s16:user applicationd2:s4:axesd6:s22:single-or-organisationl2:s6:singles12:organisations4:seenl1:s5:glasss4:tagsl1:s1:Ss5:ruledl1:s3:yess8:categoryl1:s7:programs8:hardwarel2:s3:yess2:nos9:relationsl0:s2:OSd2:s4:axesd6:s22:single-or-organisationl2:s6:singles12:organisations4:seenl2:s5:glasss6:sealeds4:tagsl3:s1:Ss1:Us3:S+Us5:ruledl2:s3:yess2:nos8:categoryl1:s6:systems8:hardwarel2:s3:yess2:nos9:relationsl0:s6:driverd2:s4:axesd6:s22:single-or-organisationl2:s6:singles12:organisations4:seenl1:s5:glasss4:tagsl1:s1:Ss5:ruledl1:s3:yess8:categoryl1:s7:programs8:hardwarel2:s3:yess2:nos9:relationsl1:s25:bound_to_a_device_by_rowss7:serviced2:s4:axesd6:s22:single-or-organisationl2:s6:singles12:organisations4:seenl1:s5:glasss4:tagsl1:s1:Ss5:ruledl1:s3:yess8:categoryl1:s7:programs8:hardwarel2:s3:yess2:nos9:relationsl1:s27:started_by_system_on_a_rules8:firmwared2:s4:axesd6:s22:single-or-organisationl2:s6:singles12:organisations4:seenl1:s6:sealeds4:tagsl1:s1:Ss5:ruledl2:s3:yess2:nos8:categoryl1:s12:counterpartys8:hardwarel1:s3:yess9:relationsl0:s9:LLM modeld2:s4:axesd6:s22:single-or-organisationl2:s6:singles12:organisations4:seenl1:s6:sealeds4:tagsl1:s1:Us5:ruledl1:s3:yess8:categoryl1:s2:ais8:hardwarel2:s3:yess2:nos9:relationsl0:s9:record_ids7:rec_259d16:s10:provenanced3:s10:could_readl0:s11:asserted_bys10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:sources6:systems10:rule_citeds8:BOOT-INTs11:record_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.908737+00:00s12:content_forms6:inlines15:occurrence_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.908758+00:00s15:submission_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.908753+00:00s16:evidence_summaryns3:seqi260;s4:refsl0:s5:actors10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:actions11:CREATE-RULEs6:objects22:PLACE-LAW-FROZEN-LISTSs6:origind2:s12:subsystem_ids6:kernels8:built_idi0;s6:targetns7:payloadd3:s12:frozen_packsl10:s10:actor-axess9:axis-tagss27:axis-single-or-organisations9:axis-seens10:axis-ruleds13:axis-hardwares13:axis-categorys14:familiar-namess18:place-unread-namess13:actor-classess4:texts1934:C8-P0a-i (design/65 sitting three, the owner's two freeze levels; archi :5222 countersign) + C8-ACTOR-CLASSES-FROZEN (archi :5431 (1), :5441 (2) the re-cut). TWO LEVELS, both founded here. CONSTITUTIONAL: the axes and pack:actor-axes change ONLY by descent, a new world citing its parent — nobody amends them mid-flight; pack:actor-classes' mind-kind words (human, ai, program) join this level for the same reason — CONST-ACTOR-CATEGORY already states these mind-kind words change only by descent, and archi's ruling (:5431) is what binds that constitutional sentence to the pack that carries the words. VERSION-FROZEN: pack:familiar-names is changed ONLY at a gov-os version birth — nobody invents or bends a familiar label mid-flight, which is how classification games happen; the safety valve making this costless is that a new kind between versions still works fully by its axes and rows, it simply carries no familiar word until the next version names it. frozen_packs names TEN packs: the seven axis packs (actor-axes, axis-tags, axis-single-or-organisation, axis-seen, axis-ruled, axis-hardware, axis-category), familiar-names, place-unread-names (C8-P0a-iii, archi :5237/:5238, board :5349 -- the identity token's founded unread-name and row-absence vocabulary, VERSION-FROZEN exactly as familiar-names), and actor-classes (C8-ACTOR-CLASSES-FROZEN, archi :5431/:5441 -- the mind-kind words alone, CONSTITUTIONAL as above). Every actor and every op — AMEND-PACK, or a CREATE-INFO carrying the category_pack kind — is refused BY NAME at the gate for naming one of these, the owner included. pack:class-ceilings is deliberately NOT listed here: the ceilings that once rode the actor-classes row do NOT freeze with the words (archi :5441, "THE CEILINGS DO NOT FREEZE WITH THE WORDS") — they move to their own founded row, lawfully changeable at owner tier, its eventual change path named as rule form, unbuilt (:5441).s7:rule_ids22:PLACE-LAW-FROZEN-LISTSs9:record_ids7:rec_260d16:s10:provenanced3:s10:could_readl0:s11:asserted_bys10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:sources6:systems10:rule_citeds8:BOOT-INTs11:record_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.911018+00:00s12:content_forms6:inlines15:occurrence_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.911032+00:00s15:submission_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.911028+00:00s16:evidence_summaryns3:seqi261;s4:refsl0:s5:actors10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:actions11:CREATE-INFOs6:objects23:pack:place-unread-namess6:origind2:s12:subsystem_ids6:kernels8:built_idi0;s6:targetns7:payloadd4:s4:kinds13:category_packs4:names18:place-unread-namess4:texts1423:C8-P0a-iii (design/65 sitting three; archi :5237, :5238; board :5349's mechanical delta; board :5452's further mechanical delta). THE PLACE VIEW'S UNREAD ANSWERS, FOUNDED -- the closed set of by-name readings place_of and the identity token answer when a row does not yet decide one of the six axes, plus the two row-absence names for an identity's own rows: no install row, no bound key. Values here are computed at read time, not stored on any record; each name is a leaf value in the identity token's nine-leaf shape, salted the same as a founded axis reading. The eighth name, 'no declared class', names an established actor whose class band carries no ceiling row for the tags axis -- a gap C8-P0a-ii's place view named, folded into this founded set by the mechanical delta of board :5349. The ninth name, 'a system actor, named by the constitution, not established by a row', names a constitution-named system actor (a member of CONST-ACTOR-CATEGORY's own system_actors) carrying no CREATE-ACTOR or CREATE-ACCOUNT establishment row -- the identity token's own no-token answer for such an actor, folded into this founded set by the mechanical delta of board :5452. The tenth name, 'witnessed, not established', names a device a witness row has seen that no establishing act has named: it is placed by its computed fingerprint, with the witnessing row's seq carried beside the name as computed content, never inside it.s6:levelsl10:s15:never installeds9:bare names15:no arrivals yets16:no exchanges yets35:hardware waits on the device familys14:no install rows12:no bound keys17:no declared classs67:a system actor, named by the constitution, not established by a rows26:witnessed, not establisheds9:record_ids7:rec_261d16:s10:provenanced3:s10:could_readl0:s11:asserted_bys10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:sources6:systems10:rule_citeds8:BOOT-INTs11:record_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.913340+00:00s12:content_forms6:inlines15:occurrence_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.913356+00:00s15:submission_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.913351+00:00s16:evidence_summaryns3:seqi262;s4:refsl0:s5:actors10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:actions11:CREATE-INFOs6:objects26:pack:device-known-defaultss6:origind2:s12:subsystem_ids6:kernels8:built_idi0;s6:targetns7:payloadd4:s4:kinds13:category_packs4:names21:device-known-defaultss4:texts1016:C8-P19b-FINGERPRINT-ii-b (design/65's P19 device fingerprint work; archi :5129 (1) option (b), "a closed vocabulary, rides P0a where the axes land"; countersign :5416, board :5466 dispatch). THE KNOWN-DEFAULT DEVICE TRAITS, FOUNDED -- qemu's measured position-counter serial and shared virtio-net MAC (P19a FINDINGS.md A1, driven by real nested boots: b1-default.serial and b8-swap-positions.serial record block.serial=QM00001 (master) and block.serial=QM00002 (slave) byte-exact; b1-default.serial and b3-diskB-default.serial record network.mac=52:54:00:12:34:56 byte-exact), read by kernel.opdefs's known-default membership kind the way an axis pack is read, a membership question and nothing more. The list grows through AMEND-PACK, the door every category pack takes; a value absent from this list carries no verdict about whether it is a genuine per-device identity -- the born_before view's first-witness band still asks whether an identifying trait is a known default, and an absent value answers neither way.s6:levelsl3:s20:block.serial=QM00001s20:block.serial=QM00002s29:network.mac=52:54:00:12:34:56s9:record_ids7:rec_262d16:s10:provenanced3:s10:could_readl0:s11:asserted_bys10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:sources6:systems10:rule_citeds8:BOOT-INTs11:record_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.915152+00:00s12:content_forms6:inlines15:occurrence_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.915165+00:00s15:submission_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.915162+00:00s16:evidence_summaryns3:seqi263;s4:refsl0:s5:actors10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:actions11:CREATE-RULEs6:objects23:CHECKS-CITE-THEIR-RULESs6:origind2:s12:subsystem_ids6:kernels8:built_idi0;s6:targetns7:payloadd5:s11:enforced_bys834:kernel.opdefs._require_cites (definition-time: a check must carry every key CHECK_CITE_KEYS[kind] lists, non-empty, at all three doors -- the founding installer, CREATE-OP, AMEND-OP, inner checks included), engaged when CHECKS-CITE-THEIR-RULES is live: the founding installer reads it from the pack's own rule records (founding.install._validate), and CREATE-OP / AMEND-OP read it from views.active_rules(). The interpreter (kernel.opdefs._dispatch_check and its extracted _..._check helpers) reads each key with no code default when the row founding it is live; a world founded without this row reads CHECK_HISTORIC_DEFAULTS instead, exactly as it always did. kernel.views._rule_set reads every such key the same way in both worlds, live or historic, so the rule set an operation is decided under is whole by construction either way.s11:enforcements4:lives4:texts480:EVERY CHECK MUST NAME THE RULES IT REFUSES BY. In a world whose founding carries this row, a check that leaves any of its refusal paths' rules unnamed is refused at every definition door, and a check never refuses citing a rule its own row does not name; the rule set an operation is decided under is then whole by construction. A world founded without this row installs and decides as it always did, its historic default citations standing as that era's law (archi :5436, :5487).s5:scopes10:space:roots7:rule_ids23:CHECKS-CITE-THEIR-RULESs9:record_ids7:rec_263d16:s10:provenanced3:s10:could_readl0:s11:asserted_bys10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:sources6:systems10:rule_citeds8:BOOT-INTs11:record_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.916880+00:00s12:content_forms6:inlines15:occurrence_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.916896+00:00s15:submission_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.916893+00:00s16:evidence_summaryns3:seqi264;s4:refsl0:s5:actors10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:actions11:CREATE-RULEs6:objects18:REGION-UNDECIDABLEs6:origind2:s12:subsystem_ids6:kernels8:built_idi0;s6:targetns7:payloadd5:s11:enforced_bys168:kernel.region.RegionGate.execute (the pre-draft U2 placement and the REGION-UNDECIDABLE catch) and kernel.region.RegionPen._publish (U1, U3, U2's row-side second check)s11:enforcements4:lives4:texts467:A REGION MUST REFUSE WHAT ITS SEALED SET CANNOT DECIDE, AND NEVER DECIDE IT BY DEFAULT. In a world whose founding carries this row, a region's gate that is asked to act on an operation outside its delivered set, in a space outside its region, or under a rule its sealed set names but its own rows do not hold, writes a refusal on its own pen citing this rule. A world founded without this row raises the same answer and writes no row, as that era did (design/56 B16).s5:scopes10:space:roots7:rule_ids18:REGION-UNDECIDABLEs9:record_ids7:rec_264d16:s10:provenanced3:s10:could_readl0:s11:asserted_bys10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:sources6:systems10:rule_citeds8:BOOT-INTs11:record_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.918811+00:00s12:content_forms6:inlines15:occurrence_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.918829+00:00s15:submission_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.918824+00:00s16:evidence_summaryns3:seqi265;s4:refsl0:s5:actors10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:actions11:CREATE-RULEs6:objects4:AR-2s6:origind2:s12:subsystem_ids6:kernels8:built_idi0;s6:targetns7:payloadd5:s11:enforced_bys359:kernel.boot (CREATE-VIEW's nonconforming submissions), kernel.crossing.validate_station, kernel.opdefs (its call-shape refusals and its check-cite defaults), kernel.views (derived-view and master read-time refusals), kernel.gate (the nonconforming-call and view-submission steps) and observe.seam (the shared observation meta's declared cite and its refusals)s11:enforcements4:lives4:texts447:A CALL OR DECLARATION THAT DOES NOT CONFORM TO ITS OPERATION'S DECLARED SHAPE MUST BE REFUSED, CITING THIS RULE. A required parameter missing, a parameter the operation does not declare, a value of the wrong kind, or a check or definition row malformed at any door is refused and recorded; it is never repaired, defaulted or silently admitted. A world founded without this row keeps citing AR-2 as that era did, a name with no row (design/58 R10).s5:scopes10:space:roots7:rule_ids4:AR-2s9:record_ids7:rec_265d16:s10:provenanced3:s10:could_readl0:s11:asserted_bys10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:sources6:systems10:rule_citeds8:BOOT-INTs11:record_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.920891+00:00s12:content_forms6:inlines15:occurrence_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.920909+00:00s15:submission_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.920904+00:00s16:evidence_summaryns3:seqi266;s4:refsl0:s5:actors10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:actions11:CREATE-RULEs6:objects2:I8s6:origind2:s12:subsystem_ids6:kernels8:built_idi0;s6:targetns7:payloadd5:s11:enforced_bys135:kernel.views.refuse_double_claim, invoked at kernel.border's handshake step (P6, the live-stages one-machine-per-stage-per-scope check)s11:enforcements4:lives4:texts581:ONE MACHINE PER STAGE PER SCOPE: A SECOND MACHINE CLAIMING A STAGE ANOTHER ALREADY HOLDS FOR THE SAME SCOPE MUST BE REFUSED at the handshake, naming every conflicting stage and scope, UNLESS BOTH HOLD IT UNDER THE SAME RECEIVED RULE. Two holdings that each stand on one parent-signed rule, proven on the receiver's side by its own adoption record and on the other side by the parent's signature over the presented rule, are redundancy and are admitted. Disjoint scopes, or a single holder, pass. A world founded without this row keeps citing I8 as that era did, a name with no row.s5:scopes10:space:roots7:rule_ids2:I8s9:record_ids7:rec_266d16:s10:provenanced3:s10:could_readl0:s11:asserted_bys10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:sources6:systems10:rule_citeds8:BOOT-INTs11:record_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.923639+00:00s12:content_forms6:inlines15:occurrence_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.923663+00:00s15:submission_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.923657+00:00s16:evidence_summaryns3:seqi267;s4:refsl0:s5:actors10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:actions11:CREATE-RULEs6:objects23:OP-DECLARATION-RECORDEDs6:origind2:s12:subsystem_ids6:kernels8:built_idi0;s6:targetns7:payloadd5:s11:enforced_bys392:kernel.compose.record_op_declarations (the writer, called at the end of build_full_kernel/bridge.mount.build_brain and once more at observe.seam.register_observe_ops's install), kernel.views.registry_as_of (the as_of resolver the four readers consult) and kernel.gate._incarnation_row_step (the SYSTEM-only write check, keyed on the row's own payload kind exactly as the incarnation rows are)s11:enforcements4:lives4:texts711:Every operation registered in code must have its declaration -- its params, its cell and the rules it declares -- recorded as a SYSTEM row when it is first registered in a world and again whenever that declaration changes, never at a registration that changes nothing. A reader deciding as of a past point reads the declaration recorded then; a world whose record holds no such row reads the code as it stands. A declaration row records what the code declares, never whether the rules it names are founded. The gate's own steps that refuse only for named operations must declare, per operation, the rules they may cite, and that declaration is recorded the same way, as one row for the gate whenever it changes.s5:scopes10:space:roots7:rule_ids23:OP-DECLARATION-RECORDEDs9:record_ids7:rec_267d16:s10:provenanced3:s10:could_readl0:s11:asserted_bys10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:sources6:systems10:rule_citeds10:CAP-IS-LAWs11:record_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.925917+00:00s12:content_forms6:inlines15:occurrence_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.925951+00:00s15:submission_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:05.925945+00:00s16:evidence_summaryns3:seqi268;s4:refsl0:s5:actors10:PC_RUNTIMEs6:actions9:CREATE-OPs6:objects16:op:INSTALL-PRESSs6:origind2:s12:subsystem_ids6:kernels8:built_idi0;s6:targetns7:payloadd7:s10:definitiond8:s11:descriptions1201:THE PRESS (design/61 B5; archi :6080; C9-P5a). The owner-present act that consents to writing ONE named disk: it appends ONE press row, actor the person consenting, object the device actor id, citing the layout item by draft_seq, the device, and the layout hash the consent was given against. The layout item is an information item (CREATE-INFO) whose text is canonical JSON of kind install-layout naming the device; its layout hash is sha256 of that text, DERIVED at the act and never stored on the item or the press row. FOUR REFUSALS, BY NAME, each recorded, none writing a press row, named in the gate's own order: (a) a press already stands for that device (fold_threshold, presses_for_device < 1, keyed by device, in the handler); (b) draft_seq names no install-layout item for that device (kernel.gate._install_press_step); (c) the layout hash is not the hash of the cited item's text, so the drawing changed after consent; (d) the device has no identity row witnessed by an estate observation (views.device_of is None). The press writes no disk, draws no layout and loads no program; nothing consumes a standing press yet. Records a structured consent and interprets no content -> cell S (B4).s12:object_params6:devices12:payload_froml3:s9:draft_seqs6:devices11:layout_hashs17:structural_paramsl3:s9:draft_seqs6:devices11:layout_hashs4:cells1:Ss6:checksl1:d9:s10:add_actions13:INSTALL-PRESSs4:cites10:CAP-IS-LAWs5:checks14:fold_thresholds7:messages133:INSTALL-PRESS: a press already stands for this device -- one press per device; a second press is refused, recorded, and never writtens8:operators1:<s9:fold_names18:presses_for_devices9:key_fields6:devices9:key_params6:devices9:thresholdi1;s6:paramsd3:s11:layout_hashs8:requireds6:devices8:requireds9:draft_seqs8:requireds9:law_citeds10:CAP-IS-LAWs4:kinds13:op_definitions4:names13:INSTALL-PRESSs4:texts369:operation INSTALL-PRESS: when invoked, no press already stands for the device, the gate finds draft_seq names an install-layout information item for that device, layout_hash equals sha256 of that item's text, and the device carries an identity row witnessed by an estate observation -> append the one press row citing CAP-IS-LAW; otherwise refuse by name, in that orders4:tiers5:owners7:rule_ids16:op:INSTALL-PRESSs8:polaritys1:+s9:record_ids7:rec_268d16:s10:provenanced5:s10:could_readl0:s10:decided_ops14:CREATE-ACCOUNTs11:asserted_bys6:SYSTEMs13:decided_unders71:sha256:946399e9e9c6e6433ab1e8744d84acd85e763f71b4a830f706f3e30a7ec05297s6:sources6:systems10:rule_citeds10:CAP-IS-LAWs11:record_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:06.195386+00:00s12:content_forms6:inlines15:occurrence_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:06.195405+00:00s15:submission_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:06.195401+00:00s16:evidence_summaryns3:seqi290;s4:refsl0:s5:actors6:SYSTEMs6:actions14:CREATE-ACCOUNTs6:objects13:probe-programs6:origind2:s12:subsystem_ids6:kernels8:built_idi0;s6:targetns7:payloadd4:s10:account_ids13:probe-programs10:founded_bys6:SYSTEMs11:actor_classs7:programs4:kinds7:accounts9:record_ids7:rec_290d16:s10:provenanced5:s10:could_readl0:s10:decided_ops14:WRITE-ACTIVITYs11:asserted_bys6:SYSTEMs13:decided_unders71:sha256:57395d041f4d6dfc9f6b2ce2c21c7c7d76f0092ae65d08c7aa611555042f1052s6:sources6:systems10:rule_citeds16:INCARNATION-LOADs11:record_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:06.198831+00:00s12:content_forms6:inlines15:occurrence_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:06.198860+00:00s15:submission_times32:2026-10-02T21:53:06.198856+00:00s16:evidence_summaryns3:seqi291;s4:refsl0:s5:actors6:SYSTEMs6:actions14:WRITE-ACTIVITYs6:objects13:probe-programs6:origind2:s12:subsystem_ids6:kernels8:built_idi0;s6:targetns7:payloadd3:s12:touch_pointsd1:s10:operationsl2:s14:OBSERVE-DEVICEs14:WRITE-ACTIVITYs4:kinds23:incarnation-declarations4:seals71:sha256:6836e3ae60a820b9cf373bd127022f2bebcc7a33d82ab314830269b30a062250s9:record_ids7:rec_291s4:seqsl257:i3;i4;i5;i7;i8;i9;i10;i11;i12;i13;i14;i15;i16;i17;i18;i19;i20;i21;i22;i23;i24;i25;i26;i27;i28;i29;i30;i31;i32;i33;i34;i35;i36;i37;i38;i39;i40;i41;i42;i43;i44;i45;i46;i47;i48;i49;i50;i51;i52;i53;i54;i55;i56;i57;i58;i59;i60;i61;i62;i63;i64;i65;i66;i67;i68;i70;i71;i72;i75;i76;i77;i78;i79;i80;i81;i82;i83;i84;i85;i86;i87;i88;i89;i90;i91;i92;i93;i94;i95;i96;i97;i98;i99;i100;i101;i102;i103;i104;i105;i106;i107;i108;i109;i110;i111;i112;i113;i114;i115;i116;i117;i118;i119;i120;i121;i122;i123;i12